-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part snap1 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (United States, 7 U.S.C. ch. 51), sections 2012a to 2014a and 2018 -- THE SEAT LAYER of part snap1.
--
-- SEAT: a member of a household that applies for, or receives, benefits under the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP).
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the snap1 modules imported above as the questions that person would ask: whether the household may take part, what income
-- counts, what is deducted, what the limits are, which resources count, and what follows for a sponsored alien, a disaster victim or a household that moves.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: every answer is a call of a layer-1 rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, numbers, dates, the core's list of areas), each with an @desc worded for the household member.
-- Where a rule asks a yes-or-no-or-unknown answer (a MAYBE BOOLEAN) that the member may not know, the question asks two plain inputs ("do you know?" and "is it so?"),
-- and an unknown answer is passed on as NOTHING, so the result says "the text does not decide it" and never a "no".
-- RESULTS. A BOOLEAN result of a layer-1 rule is a MAYBE BOOLEAN here: JUST TRUE (the Act says yes), JUST FALSE (the Act says no in its own words) or NOTHING
-- (the Act does not say; see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING"). An amount is a MAYBE NUMBER when a missing fact leaves it open.
-- FIGURES THE ACT LEAVES TO THE SECRETARY. The income standards, the standard deduction, the shelter cap and the resource limits are the USDA's figures for fiscal year 2027
-- (1 October 2026 to 30 September 2027), which the rules take as data; a different year's figures would change these answers. The member is not asked for them.
-- SEAMS NOT WIRED IN THIS PART. A fact that another part of the Act answers (the exceptions of section 2015, the definition of a household in section 2012(m)(4), whether a member
-- is elderly or disabled under section 2012(j)) is asked of the member as a plain yes-or-no, to be replaced by the answering part's rule at the merge.

-- The fiscal year of the USDA tables the rules hold.
`snap1 seat the fiscal year of the tables` MEANS 2027

GIVEN known IS A BOOLEAN
      value IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`snap1 seat the answer if known` MEANS
    IF known THEN JUST value ELSE NOTHING

-- A person for the two rules that read only one or two facts about a person: the other fields are placeholders no rule called here reads.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
      ssi IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Individual
`snap1 seat a person` MEANS Individual WITH
    `age in years` IS age
    -- Placeholders: the rules called here do not read the next six fields.
    `physically and mentally fit` IS TRUE
    `pregnant` IS FALSE
    `immigration status` IS `a citizen or national of the United States`
    `resident of the United States` IS TRUE
    `receives supplemental security income benefits` IS ssi
    `hours worked per week, averaged monthly` IS 0
    `enrolled at least half-time in an institution of higher education` IS FALSE

GIVEN deduction IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`snap1 seat the deduction or nothing` MEANS
    CONSIDER deduction
        WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
        WHEN JUST d THEN d

-- A deduction counts only where the rule shows the household entitled (composition rule of snap1-s2014-e1: a household not shown to be entitled deducts nothing).
GIVEN entitled IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`snap1 seat the deduction if shown` MEANS
    IF `snap1 is definitely yes` entitled THEN amount ELSE 0

§ `Under section 2012a`

-- Section 2012a. Applies the rules on private nonprofit drug and alcohol treatment programs to publicly operated community health centers.
@export Under section 2012a, does section 2019 also apply to the publicly operated community health center I use?
GIVEN `my center is a publicly operated community health center` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the center you use a community health center that a public body runs?
      `the rule concerns private nonprofit drug or alcohol treatment programs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the rule you are asking about one for private nonprofit drug addiction or alcohol treatment and rehabilitation programs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2012a, does section 2019 also apply to the publicly operated community health center I use` MEANS
    `s 2012a the provision is also applicable to the center` `s 2012a section 2019` `the rule concerns private nonprofit drug or alcohol treatment programs` `my center is a publicly operated community health center`

§ `Under section 2013`

-- Section 2013(a)(1). The program, and what the benefits may buy.
@export Under section 2013(a)(1), is my household given the opportunity to receive an allotment?
GIVEN `money has been appropriated for the program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, has money been appropriated for the program?
      `my State agency has asked to run the program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your State agency asked to run the program?
      `my household is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your household eligible?
      `sales taxes are collected in my State on food bought with benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary found that State or local sales taxes are collected in your State on food bought with benefits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2013(a)(1), is my household given the opportunity to receive an allotment` MEANS
    `s 2013(a)(1) the eligible household is provided an opportunity to obtain a more nutritious diet through the issuance of an allotment` `money has been appropriated for the program` `my State agency has asked to run the program` `my household is eligible` `sales taxes are collected in my State on food bought with benefits`

@export Under section 2013(a)(1), may I use my benefits for this purchase?
GIVEN `I am buying food` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you are buying food?
      `I am buying it from an approved retail food store` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you buying it from a retail food store that has been approved to take part in the program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2013(a)(1), may I use my benefits for this purchase` MEANS
    `s 2013(a)(1) the benefits may be used for the purchase` `I am buying food` `I am buying it from an approved retail food store`

-- Section 2013(b). Food distribution on Indian reservations. Ask this group only of a person who lives on, or is disqualified from, the program on an Indian reservation.
@export Under section 2013(b)(2), who is responsible for the food distribution on my reservation?
GIVEN `the distribution is on all or part of an Indian reservation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the food distribution on all or part of an Indian reservation?
      `I know whether the Secretary has found the tribal organization capable of running it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know whether the Secretary has found the tribal organization capable of effectively and efficiently running the distribution?
      `the Secretary has found the tribal organization capable of running it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary found the tribal organization capable of effectively and efficiently running the distribution?
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
`Under section 2013(b)(2), who is responsible for the food distribution on my reservation` MEANS
    `s 2013(b)(2) the party that administers the distribution` `the distribution is on all or part of an Indian reservation`
        (`s 2013(b)(2)(B) the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently administering the distribution` (`snap1 seat the answer if known` `I know whether the Secretary has found the tribal organization capable of running it` `the Secretary has found the tribal organization capable of running it`))

@export Under section 2013(b)(3), am I barred from SNAP because I was disqualified from the food distribution program on Indian reservations?
GIVEN `I was disqualified from the food distribution program on Indian reservations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you disqualified from the food distribution program on Indian reservations?
      `I know whether the period the Secretary set has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know whether the period the Secretary set for your ineligibility has ended?
      `the period the Secretary set has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that period still running?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2013(b)(3), am I barred from SNAP because I was disqualified from the food distribution program on Indian reservations` MEANS
    `s 2013(b)(3) the individual is not eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` `I was disqualified from the food distribution program on Indian reservations` (`snap1 seat the answer if known` `I know whether the period the Secretary set has ended` `the period the Secretary set has not ended`)

§ `Under section 2014(a) to (c)`

-- Section 2014(a). Who may take part.
@export Under section 2014(a), is my household eligible because every member gets cash assistance, SSI or aid to the aged, blind or disabled?
GIVEN `every member of my household receives one of those benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does every member of your household receive cash assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act, supplemental security income, or aid to the aged, blind or disabled?
      `I know whether an exception in section 2015 applies to my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know whether any exception in section 2015 (for example, for a member who has been disqualified) applies to your household?
      `an exception in section 2015 applies to my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does such an exception apply to your household?
      `my group of people may constitute a household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you and the others you share food with count as a household under section 2012(m)(4)? (It says a group cannot count if they live in an institution or boarding house, or live with others and pay them for meals.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(a), is my household eligible because every member gets cash assistance, SSI or aid to the aged, blind or disabled` MEANS
    `s 2014(a) the household is eligible because each member receives a listed benefit` `every member of my household receives one of those benefits`
        (`snap1 seat the answer if known` `I know whether an exception in section 2015 applies to my household` `an exception in section 2015 applies to my household`)
        (`snap1 seat the answer if known` `I know whether an exception in section 2015 applies to my household` `an exception in section 2015 applies to my household`)
        (`snap1 seat the answer if known` `I know whether an exception in section 2015 applies to my household` `an exception in section 2015 applies to my household`)
        (`snap1 seat the answer if known` `I know whether an exception in section 2015 applies to my household` `an exception in section 2015 applies to my household`)
        (JUST `my group of people may constitute a household`)

@export Under section 2014(a), is my household eligible because every member gets general assistance?
GIVEN `every member of my household receives general assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does every member of your household receive benefits under a State or local general assistance program?
      `the program meets the Secretary's income standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the program meet the Secretary's standards for ensuring that it is based on income criteria comparable to or more restrictive than the gross income limit of section 2014(c)(2)?
      `the program pays more than one-time emergency payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the program more than one-time emergency payments that cannot be paid for more than one consecutive month?
      `I know whether an exception in section 2015 or 2025 applies to my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know whether any exception in section 2015 or section 2025(e)(1) applies to your household?
      `an exception in section 2015 or 2025 applies to my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does such an exception apply to your household?
      `my group of people may constitute a household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you and the others you share food with count as a household under section 2012(m)(4)? (It says a group cannot count if they live in an institution or boarding house, or live with others and pay them for meals.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(a), is my household eligible because every member gets general assistance` MEANS
    `s 2014(a) the household is eligible because each member receives general assistance` `every member of my household receives general assistance` `the program meets the Secretary's income standard` `the program pays more than one-time emergency payments`
        (`snap1 seat the answer if known` `I know whether an exception in section 2015 or 2025 applies to my household` `an exception in section 2015 or 2025 applies to my household`)
        (`snap1 seat the answer if known` `I know whether an exception in section 2015 or 2025 applies to my household` `an exception in section 2015 or 2025 applies to my household`)
        (JUST `my group of people may constitute a household`)

@export Under section 2014(a), must assistance be furnished to my household?
GIVEN `my household is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your household eligible?
      `my household has applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your household applied to take part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(a), must assistance be furnished to my household` MEANS
    `s 2014(a) assistance must be furnished to the household` `my household is eligible` `my household has applied`

-- Section 2014(b). Standards that differ from State to State.
@export Under section 2014(b), may my State agency require a condition of eligibility that is not one the Secretary set?
GIVEN `my State agency requires a condition of eligibility other than those the Secretary established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your State agency require a condition of eligibility for taking part that the Secretary did not establish?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(b), may my State agency require a condition of eligibility that is not one the Secretary set` MEANS
    `s 2014(b) the State agency may impose the standard` `my State agency requires a condition of eligibility other than those the Secretary established`

-- Section 2014(c). The income limits, in the USDA's figures for the fiscal year of the tables.
@export Under section 2014(c)(1), what is the most net income my household may have in a month, in dollars?
GIVEN `where I live` IS AN Area @desc Where do you live?
      `the number of people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your household?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(c)(1), what is the most net income my household may have in a month` MEANS
    `s 2014(c)(1) the poverty line for the household` `snap1 seat the fiscal year of the tables` `where I live` `the number of people in my household`

@export Under section 2014(c)(2), what is the most gross income my household may have in a month, in dollars?
GIVEN `where I live` IS AN Area @desc Where do you live?
      `the number of people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your household?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(c)(2), what is the most gross income my household may have in a month` MEANS
    `s 2014(c)(2) the gross monthly income limit for the household` `snap1 seat the fiscal year of the tables` `where I live` `the number of people in my household`

@export Under section 2014(c)(1), is my household ineligible because its net income is over the limit?
GIVEN `where I live` IS AN Area @desc Where do you live?
      `the number of people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your household?
      `my household's net income in a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your household's net income in a month, in dollars, after the exclusions and deductions of section 2014(d) and (e)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(c)(1), is my household ineligible because its net income is over the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2014(c)(1) the poverty line for the household` `snap1 seat the fiscal year of the tables` `where I live` `the number of people in my household`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): no limit is held for that household size
        WHEN JUST line THEN `s 2014(c)(1) the household is ineligible because its net income exceeds the poverty line` `my household's net income in a month` line

@export Under section 2014(c)(2), is my household ineligible because its gross income is over the limit?
GIVEN `where I live` IS AN Area @desc Where do you live?
      `the number of people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your household?
      `my household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is anyone in your household elderly (60 or older) or disabled?
      `my household's gross income in a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your household's gross income in a month, in dollars, after the exclusions of section 2014(d) but before the deductions of section 2014(e)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(c)(2), is my household ineligible because its gross income is over the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2014(c)(2) the gross monthly income limit for the household` `snap1 seat the fiscal year of the tables` `where I live` `the number of people in my household`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): no limit is held for that household size
        WHEN JUST limit THEN `s 2014(c)(2) the household is ineligible because its gross income exceeds the gross monthly income limit` (JUST `my household includes an elderly or disabled member`) `my household's gross income in a month` limit

§ `Under section 2014(d)`

-- Section 2014(d). What counts as income and what is left out.
@export Under section 2014(d)(1), is a benefit I get that is not money paid to my household left out of my income?
GIVEN `the benefit is not money paid directly to my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit something other than money paid directly to your household (for example, a service or goods)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(d)(1), is a benefit I get that is not money paid to my household left out of my income` MEANS
    `s 2014(d)(1) the item is excluded because it is not money payable directly to a household` `the benefit is not money paid directly to my household`

@export Under section 2014(d)(3), how much of my educational loan, grant, scholarship or fellowship is left out of my income, in dollars a month?
GIVEN `it is an educational loan with deferred payment, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship or the like` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an educational loan on which payment is deferred, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' educational benefit or the like?
      `a household member is enrolled in a qualifying program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a member of your household enrolled at a recognized institution of post-secondary education, a school for the handicapped, a vocational education program, or a program that provides for completion of a secondary diploma?
      `its monthly amount` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is it a month, in dollars?
      `the allowance for tuition, fees, books, supplies, transportation and other expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What allowance does the school or grantor give for tuition, mandatory fees, books, supplies, transportation and other personal expenses (not living expenses), in dollars a month?
      `the origination fees and insurance premiums the loan includes` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are the origination fees and insurance premiums that the loan includes, in dollars a month?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(d)(3), how much of my educational loan, grant, scholarship or fellowship is left out of my income` MEANS
    `s 2014(d)(3) the amount excluded` `it is an educational loan with deferred payment, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship or the like` `a household member is enrolled in a qualifying program` `its monthly amount` `the allowance for tuition, fees, books, supplies, transportation and other expenses` `the origination fees and insurance premiums the loan includes`

@export Under section 2014(d)(7), is my child's earned income left out of my household's income?
GIVEN `the income is earned by a child in my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the income earned by a child who is a member of your household?
      `the child is an elementary or secondary school student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child an elementary or secondary school student?
      `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the child, in years?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(d)(7), is my child's earned income left out of my household's income` MEANS
    `s 2014(d)(7) the child's earned income is excluded` `the income is earned by a child in my household` `the child is an elementary or secondary school student` `the child's age`

@export Under section 2014(d)(11), is my energy assistance payment left out of my income?
GIVEN `the payment is energy assistance under a Federal law other than part A of title IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment energy assistance under a Federal law other than the cash assistance program in part A of title IV of the Social Security Act?
      `the payment is a one-time payment for weatherization or emergency repair of a heating or cooling device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a one-time payment under a Federal or State law for weatherization, or for emergency repair or replacement of an unsafe or inoperative furnace or other heating or cooling device?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(d)(11), is my energy assistance payment left out of my income` MEANS
    `s 2014(d)(11) the payment or allowance is excluded` `the payment is energy assistance under a Federal law other than part A of title IV` `the payment is a one-time payment for weatherization or emergency repair of a heating or cooling device`

@export Under section 2014(d)(12), is a cost-of-living increase in my income left out of my household's income?
GIVEN `the date the cost-of-living adjustment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the cost-of-living adjustment made?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking?
      `the increase is a cost-of-living adjustment under title II or XVI of the Social Security Act, the Railroad Retirement Act of 1974 or section 5312 of title 38` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the increase from a cost-of-living adjustment under title II or XVI of the Social Security Act, section 3(a)(1) of the Railroad Retirement Act of 1974, or section 5312 of title 38?
      `my household was certified or received an allotment the month before the adjustment took effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your household certified as eligible, or did it receive an allotment, in the month before the first month in which the adjustment took effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(d)(12), is a cost-of-living increase in my income left out of my household's income` MEANS
    `s 2014(d)(12) the cost-of-living increase is excluded on the date` `the date the cost-of-living adjustment was made` `the date I am asking about` `the increase is a cost-of-living adjustment under title II or XVI of the Social Security Act, the Railroad Retirement Act of 1974 or section 5312 of title 38` `my household was certified or received an allotment the month before the adjustment took effect`

@export Under section 2014(d), how much of my household's income counts each month, in dollars?
GIVEN `the monthly income from work that counts` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household get from work each month, in dollars, after the income that section 2014(d) leaves out?
      `the monthly income from other sources that counts` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household get from other sources each month, in dollars, after the income that section 2014(d) leaves out?
      `the cost of producing my self-employment income` IS A NUMBER @desc What does it cost you each month to produce your self-employment income, in dollars?
      `my income from self-employment as a farmer` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you get each month from self-employment as a farmer, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 2014(d), how much of my household's income counts each month` MEANS
    `s 2014(d) household income` (LIST `the monthly income from work that counts`, `the monthly income from other sources that counts`)
        (`s 2014(d)(9) the reduction of the other income that is included` `the cost of producing my self-employment income` `my income from self-employment as a farmer`)

§ `Under section 2014(e)`

-- Section 2014(e). The deductions, and the net income that is left. (Chain assembled here from the layer-1 rules in the order the subsection gives.)
@export Under section 2014(e)(1), what is my household's standard deduction, in dollars a month?
GIVEN `where I live` IS AN Area @desc Where do you live?
      `the number of people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your household?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(e)(1), what is my household's standard deduction` MEANS
    `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` `snap1 seat the fiscal year of the tables` `where I live` `the number of people in my household`

@export Under section 2014(e)(2), what is my household's earned income deduction, in dollars a month?
GIVEN `the earned income that remains after section 2014(d)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household earn each month, in dollars, after the income that section 2014(d) leaves out?
      `the earned income under a work supplementation program` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that is earned under a work supplementation or support program and comes from public assistance, in dollars?
      `this is an overissuance for failing to report earned income on time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you asking about an overissuance because your household did not report earned income in time?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(e)(2), what is my household's earned income deduction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2014(e)(2) the household is allowed the earned income deduction` (`s 2014(e)(2)(A) the earned income` `the earned income that remains after section 2014(d)` `the earned income under a work supplementation program`) `this is an overissuance for failing to report earned income on time`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say whether the household is allowed the deduction
        WHEN JUST allowed THEN
            IF allowed THEN JUST (`s 2014(e)(2)(B) the earned income deduction` (`s 2014(e)(2)(A) the earned income` `the earned income that remains after section 2014(d)` `the earned income under a work supplementation program`))
            ELSE JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words) on the layer-1 answer JUST FALSE: the deduction is not allowed in the overissuance case, so nothing is deducted

@export Under section 2014(e)(3), what is my household's dependent care deduction, in dollars a month?
GIVEN `the payments are necessary for the care of a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for the care of a dependent?
      `the care lets a household member take or keep a job, or train or study for one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the care let a member of your household accept or continue work, or training or education that prepares for work?
      `what the care costs` IS A NUMBER @desc What does the care actually cost each month, in dollars?
      `what a third party pays` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that does a third party pay on your household's behalf, in dollars?
      `what an educational award covers` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that is covered by money that section 2014(d)(3) leaves out of your income (for example, an educational award), in dollars?
      `what an employment and training program pays` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that is paid under an employment and training program or pilot project (section 2015(d)(4) or 2025(h)(1)(F)), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 2014(e)(3), what is my household's dependent care deduction` MEANS
    `snap1 seat the deduction if shown`
        (`s 2014(e)(3)(A) the household is entitled to the dependent care deduction` `the payments are necessary for the care of a dependent` `the care lets a household member take or keep a job, or train or study for one`)
        (`s 2014(e)(3)(A) the dependent care deduction` `what the care costs` `what a third party pays` `what an educational award covers` `what an employment and training program pays`)

@export Under section 2014(e)(4), what is my household's child support deduction, in dollars a month?
GIVEN `my State agency gives a deduction for child support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your State agency chosen to give a deduction for legally owed child support payments?
      `the child support I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How much child support that you are legally obliged to pay does a member of your household pay each month, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(e)(4), what is my household's child support deduction` MEANS
    `s 2014(e)(4)(A) the child support deduction` `my State agency gives a deduction for child support` `the child support I pay`

@export Under section 2014(e)(5), what is my household's medical expense deduction, in dollars a month?
GIVEN `my household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is anyone in your household elderly (60 or older) or disabled?
      `the medical costs of that member` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do that member's allowable medical expenses cost each month, in dollars, apart from special diets and anything a third party pays?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(e)(5), what is my household's medical expense deduction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2014(e)(5)(A) the household is entitled to the excess medical expense deduction` (JUST `my household includes an elderly or disabled member`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deduction is for "a household containing an elderly or disabled member"
        WHEN JUST entitled THEN
            IF entitled THEN JUST (`s 2014(e)(5)(A) the excess medical expense deduction` `the medical costs of that member`)
            ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the rule answers only JUST TRUE or NOTHING, so this branch is not reached today

@export Under section 2014(e)(6), what is my household's excess shelter deduction, in dollars a month?
GIVEN `my monthly shelter costs` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household spend each month on shelter (rent or mortgage, taxes, insurance, utilities), in dollars, apart from anything a third party pays?
      `my monthly income after the other deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your household's monthly income after all the other deductions, in dollars?
      `my household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is anyone in your household elderly (60 or older) or disabled?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking?
      `where I live` IS AN Area @desc Where do you live?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(e)(6), what is my household's excess shelter deduction` MEANS
    `s 2014(e)(6) the excess shelter expense deduction`
        (`s 2014(e)(6)(A) the excess shelter expense deduction before the maximum` `my monthly shelter costs` `my monthly income after the other deductions`)
        (`s 2014(e)(6)(B) the maximum excess shelter expense deduction on the date` (JUST `my household includes an elderly or disabled member`) `the day I am asking about` `where I live`)

@export Under section 2014(e), what is my household's net income each month, in dollars?
GIVEN `where I live` IS AN Area @desc Where do you live?
      `the number of people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your household?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking?
      `my earned income that counts` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household earn each month, in dollars, after the income that section 2014(d) leaves out?
      `my other income that counts` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household get each month from other sources, in dollars, after the income that section 2014(d) leaves out?
      `my household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is anyone in your household elderly (60 or older) or disabled?
      `what my dependent care costs` IS A NUMBER @desc What does care of a dependent cost each month, in dollars, so that a member can work or study?
      `my State agency gives a deduction for child support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your State agency chosen to give a deduction for legally owed child support payments?
      `the child support I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How much legally owed child support does your household pay each month, in dollars?
      `my medical costs` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does the elderly or disabled member's allowable medical care cost each month, in dollars?
      `my monthly shelter costs` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household spend each month on shelter, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(e), what is my household's net income each month` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` `snap1 seat the fiscal year of the tables` `where I live` `the number of people in my household`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): no standard deduction is held for that household size
        WHEN JUST standard THEN
            `s 2014(e) the household's net income`
                (`s 2014(e) the household's income after the deductions other than the shelter deduction`
                    (`my earned income that counts` PLUS `my other income that counts`)
                    standard
                    (`snap1 seat the deduction if shown` (`s 2014(e)(2) the household is allowed the earned income deduction` `my earned income that counts` FALSE) (`s 2014(e)(2)(B) the earned income deduction` `my earned income that counts`))
                    (`snap1 seat the deduction if shown` (`s 2014(e)(3)(A) the household is entitled to the dependent care deduction` TRUE TRUE) (`s 2014(e)(3)(A) the dependent care deduction` `what my dependent care costs` 0 0 0))
                    (`snap1 seat the deduction or nothing` (`s 2014(e)(4)(A) the child support deduction` `my State agency gives a deduction for child support` `the child support I pay`))
                    (`snap1 seat the deduction if shown` (`s 2014(e)(5)(A) the household is entitled to the excess medical expense deduction` (JUST `my household includes an elderly or disabled member`)) (`s 2014(e)(5)(A) the excess medical expense deduction` `my medical costs`)))
                (`s 2014(e)(6) the excess shelter expense deduction`
                    (`s 2014(e)(6)(A) the excess shelter expense deduction before the maximum` `my monthly shelter costs`
                        (`s 2014(e) the household's income after the deductions other than the shelter deduction`
                            (`my earned income that counts` PLUS `my other income that counts`)
                            standard
                            (`snap1 seat the deduction if shown` (`s 2014(e)(2) the household is allowed the earned income deduction` `my earned income that counts` FALSE) (`s 2014(e)(2)(B) the earned income deduction` `my earned income that counts`))
                            (`snap1 seat the deduction if shown` (`s 2014(e)(3)(A) the household is entitled to the dependent care deduction` TRUE TRUE) (`s 2014(e)(3)(A) the dependent care deduction` `what my dependent care costs` 0 0 0))
                            (`snap1 seat the deduction or nothing` (`s 2014(e)(4)(A) the child support deduction` `my State agency gives a deduction for child support` `the child support I pay`))
                            (`snap1 seat the deduction if shown` (`s 2014(e)(5)(A) the household is entitled to the excess medical expense deduction` (JUST `my household includes an elderly or disabled member`)) (`s 2014(e)(5)(A) the excess medical expense deduction` `my medical costs`))))
                    (`s 2014(e)(6)(B) the maximum excess shelter expense deduction on the date` (JUST `my household includes an elderly or disabled member`) `the day I am asking about` `where I live`))

§ `Under section 2014(f)`

-- Section 2014(f). How income is calculated.
@export Under section 2014(f)(1), what is my monthly income if it is averaged over twelve months, in dollars?
GIVEN `I earn my annual income in a period shorter than one year by contract or self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you earn your whole year's income in a period shorter than one year, under a contract that is not hourly or piecework, or by self-employment?
      `the income I earn in that period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you earn in that period, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(f)(1), what is my monthly income if it is averaged over twelve months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2014(f)(1)(A) the household income is averaged over a twelve-month period` `I earn my annual income in a period shorter than one year by contract or self-employment`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the averaging is for households that derive their annual income in a shorter period
        WHEN JUST averaged THEN
            IF averaged THEN JUST (`s 2014(f)(1)(A) the monthly income when averaged over a twelve-month period` `the income I earn in that period`)
            ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not averaged under this sentence

@export Under section 2014(f)(2), on what basis is my household's income calculated?
GIVEN `this is the first month I am certified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the first month of a continuous period in which your household is certified?
      `this is the second month I am certified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the second month of a continuous period in which your household is certified?
      `my State applies the first-month rule to the second month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your State chosen to calculate the first and the second month on the income and circumstances of that month?
      `I know whether my household is in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know whether your household is one of those named in clauses (i), (ii) and (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A)?
      `my household is in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it?
      `I know whether my household must file monthly reports` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know whether your household must file monthly reports of income and circumstances under section 2015(c)(1)?
      `my household must file monthly reports` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must it?
      `my State chose the retrospective basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your State chosen to calculate income on a retrospective basis?
GIVETH A `s 2014(f)(2) basis of the calculation`
`Under section 2014(f)(2), on what basis is my household's income calculated` MEANS
    -- The answer is the layer-1 constructor as it stands, including "basis not covered by this text" (a NOTHING-kind answer): the seat adds no reading of its own.
    `s 2014(f)(2) the basis on which the household's income is calculated` `this is the first month I am certified` `this is the second month I am certified` `my State applies the first-month rule to the second month`
        (`snap1 seat the answer if known` `I know whether my household is in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A)` `my household is in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of section 2015(c)(1)(A)`)
        (`snap1 seat the answer if known` `I know whether my household must file monthly reports` `my household must file monthly reports`)
        `my State chose the retrospective basis`

§ `Under section 2014(g)`

-- Section 2014(g). Resources. The member states what the household holds; the resources the Act counts, leaves out or leaves to regulations are worked out by the rules.
@export Under section 2014(g), are my household's resources over the limit?
GIVEN `my household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is anyone in your household elderly (60 or older) or disabled?
      `my savings accounts` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is in your household's savings accounts, in dollars?
      `my other cash and bank balances` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household hold in cash and in checking or other bank accounts that are not savings accounts, in dollars?
      `my vacation home` IS A NUMBER @desc What is any vacation home your household owns worth, in dollars (0 if none)?
      `my recreational boat, snowmobile or airplane` IS A NUMBER @desc What are any boats, snowmobiles or airplanes that your household uses for recreation worth, in dollars (0 if none)?
      `the market value of my vehicle` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fair market value of your licensed vehicle, in dollars (0 if none)?
      `my vehicle is used for household transportation or to get or keep a job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the vehicle for household transportation, or to obtain or continue employment?
      `my vehicle is used to produce earned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vehicle used to produce earned income?
      `my vehicle is needed to transport a disabled member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vehicle necessary for the transportation of a physically disabled member of your household?
      `my vehicle carries fuel or water the household depends on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your household depend on the vehicle to carry fuel for heating or water for home use, as the main source of either?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(g), are my household's resources over the limit` MEANS
    `s 2014(g)(1)(A) the household is ineligible because its resources exceed the limit`
        (`s 2014(g)(1) the total value of the resources shown to count` `the resources of my household`)
        (`s 2014(g)(1) the total value of the resources that may count` `the resources of my household`)
        (JUST `my household includes an elderly or disabled member`)
        `s 2014(g)(1) resource limit for all other households, FY 2027`
        `s 2014(g)(1) resource limit for a household with an elderly or disabled member, FY 2027`
    WHERE
        `the resources of my household` MEANS
            LIST `a savings account of my household`, `other cash of my household`, `a vacation home of my household`, `recreational property of my household`, `the vehicle of my household`
        `a savings account of my household` MEANS `s 2014(g) resource` WITH
            `s 2014(g) the value of the resource if it counts, in dollars` IS `my savings accounts`
            `s 2014(g) whether the text includes the resource` IS `s 2014(g)(2)(B)(v) the resource is included in financial resources` TRUE
            `s 2014(g) whether the text excludes the resource` IS NOTHING
        `other cash of my household` MEANS `s 2014(g) resource` WITH
            `s 2014(g) the value of the resource if it counts, in dollars` IS `my other cash and bank balances`
            -- The regulations of 1 June 1982 are not among the sources, so whether cash counts is not shown.
            `s 2014(g) whether the text includes the resource` IS `s 2014(g)(2)(A) the resource is included in financial resources by the regulations in force as of June 1, 1982` FALSE FALSE NOTHING
            `s 2014(g) whether the text excludes the resource` IS NOTHING
        `a vacation home of my household` MEANS `s 2014(g) resource` WITH
            `s 2014(g) the value of the resource if it counts, in dollars` IS `my vacation home`
            `s 2014(g) whether the text includes the resource` IS `s 2014(g)(2)(B)(ii) the resource is included in financial resources` TRUE
            `s 2014(g) whether the text excludes the resource` IS NOTHING
        `recreational property of my household` MEANS `s 2014(g) resource` WITH
            `s 2014(g) the value of the resource if it counts, in dollars` IS `my recreational boat, snowmobile or airplane`
            `s 2014(g) whether the text includes the resource` IS `s 2014(g)(2)(B)(i) the resource is included in financial resources` TRUE TRUE
            `s 2014(g) whether the text excludes the resource` IS NOTHING
        `the vehicle of my household` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 2014(g)(2)(B)(iv) the value of the vehicle that counts as a resource` `my vehicle is used for household transportation or to get or keep a job` (`snap1 is definitely no` (`s 2014(g)(2)(C) the vehicle is included in financial resources under paragraph (2)` `my vehicle is used to produce earned income` `my vehicle is needed to transport a disabled member` `my vehicle carries fuel or water the household depends on`)) FALSE FALSE 0 `the market value of my vehicle`
                WHEN JUST counted THEN `s 2014(g) resource` WITH
                    `s 2014(g) the value of the resource if it counts, in dollars` IS counted
                    `s 2014(g) whether the text includes the resource` IS JUST TRUE
                    `s 2014(g) whether the text excludes the resource` IS NOTHING
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 2014(g) resource` WITH
                    `s 2014(g) the value of the resource if it counts, in dollars` IS `the market value of my vehicle`
                    `s 2014(g) whether the text includes the resource` IS NOTHING
                    `s 2014(g) whether the text excludes the resource` IS NOTHING

§ `Under section 2014(h) to (n)`

-- Section 2014(h). Emergency standards and disaster allotments. Ask this group only of a household hit by a disaster.
@export Under section 2014(h)(1), will emergency standards of eligibility be set for my household after a disaster?
GIVEN `my household is a victim of a disaster that disrupts commercial channels of food distribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your household a victim of a disaster that disrupts the commercial channels of food distribution?
      `my household needs temporary food assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your household need temporary food assistance?
      `commercial channels of food distribution are available again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have commercial channels of food distribution become available again to meet your household's temporary food needs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(h)(1), will emergency standards of eligibility be set for my household after a disaster` MEANS
    `s 2014(h)(1) the Secretary must establish temporary emergency standards of eligibility for the household` `my household is a victim of a disaster that disrupts commercial channels of food distribution` `my household needs temporary food assistance` `commercial channels of food distribution are available again`

@export Under section 2014(h)(3), how much will be replaced if my food was destroyed in a disaster, in dollars?
GIVEN `my household is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your household an eligible household?
      `my food was destroyed in a disaster` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your household's food destroyed in a disaster?
      `the value of the food I lost` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of the food you actually lost, in dollars?
      `the limit the Secretary approved` IS A NUMBER @desc What limit has the Secretary approved on replacement, in dollars?
      `the largest monthly allotment for my household size` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum monthly allotment for a household of your size, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(h)(3), how much will be replaced if my food was destroyed in a disaster` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2014(h)(3)(A) the household is provided an emergency allotment to replace food destroyed in a disaster` `my household is eligible` `my food was destroyed in a disaster`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the allotments are "to eligible households to replace food destroyed in a disaster"
        WHEN JUST provided THEN
            IF provided THEN JUST (`s 2014(h)(3)(A) the value of the food replaced` `the value of the food I lost` `the limit the Secretary approved` `the largest monthly allotment for my household size`)
            ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not provided under this subparagraph

-- Section 2014(i). Sponsored aliens. Ask this group only of a person who entered the United States with a sponsor.
@export Under section 2014(i)(1), is my sponsor's income and resources counted as mine?
GIVEN `I am an alien described in section 2015(f)(2)(B)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an alien described in section 2015(f)(2)(B) (a lawfully admitted alien who is not otherwise a qualified alien under that section)?
      `my sponsor signed an affidavit of support or similar agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person sponsor your entry into the United States by signing an affidavit of support or similar agreement?
      `I am a member of my sponsor's household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of your sponsor's household?
      `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under 18 years of age?
      `the date I entered the United States` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you enter the United States?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(i)(1), is my sponsor's income and resources counted as mine` MEANS
    `s 2014(i)(1) the income and resources of the sponsor are deemed to be the income and resources of the individual` (JUST `I am an alien described in section 2015(f)(2)(B)`) `my sponsor signed an affidavit of support or similar agreement` `I am a member of my sponsor's household` `I am under 18` `the date I entered the United States` `the date I am asking about`

@export Under section 2014(i)(2), how much income a month is counted as mine from my sponsor, in dollars?
GIVEN `my sponsor's yearly income, with the spouse's if living with the sponsor` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your sponsor's total yearly income (earned and unearned), including the sponsor's spouse's if they live together, in dollars?
      `the yearly income standard for my sponsor's household` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the yearly amount of the income eligibility standard under section 2014(c) for a household the size of your sponsor's household (the sponsor, a spouse who lives with the sponsor, and anyone who depends on them), in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(i)(2), how much income a month is counted as mine from my sponsor` MEANS
    `s 2014(i)(2)(A) the monthly income attributed to the alien` `my sponsor's yearly income, with the spouse's if living with the sponsor` `the yearly income standard for my sponsor's household`

@export Under section 2014(i)(2), how much of my sponsor's resources are counted as mine, in dollars?
GIVEN `my sponsor's resources, with the spouse's if living with the sponsor` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your sponsor's total resources, including the sponsor's spouse's if they live together, in dollars?GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2014(i)(2), how much of my sponsor's resources are counted as mine` MEANS
    `s 2014(i)(2)(B) the resources deemed to be the alien's resources` `my sponsor's resources, with the spouse's if living with the sponsor`

@export Under section 2014(i)(2)(D), are my sponsor and I both liable for an overpayment?
GIVEN `the date I entered the United States` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you enter the United States?
      `the date the overpayment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the overpayment made to you?
      `it was made because my sponsor did not give correct information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the overpayment made because your sponsor failed to give correct information?
      `my sponsor was without fault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your sponsor without fault?
      `there was good cause for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there good cause for the failure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(i)(2)(D), are my sponsor and I both liable for an overpayment` MEANS
    `s 2014(i)(2)(D) the sponsor and the alien are jointly and severally liable for the overpayment` `the date I entered the United States` `the date the overpayment was made` `it was made because my sponsor did not give correct information` `my sponsor was without fault` `there was good cause for the failure`

-- Section 2014(j). SSI, aid to the aged, blind or disabled, or cash assistance: the resource limits are treated as met.
@export Under section 2014(j), am I treated as having met the resource limits because I receive SSI, aid or cash assistance?
GIVEN `I receive supplemental security income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act?
      `I receive aid to the aged, blind or disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive aid to the aged, blind or disabled under title I, II, X, XIV or XVI of the Social Security Act?
      `I receive benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(j), am I treated as having met the resource limits because I receive SSI, aid or cash assistance` MEANS
    `s 2014(j) the member is considered to have satisfied the resource limitations of subsection (g)` (`snap1 seat a person` 30 `I receive supplemental security income`) `I receive aid to the aged, blind or disabled` `I receive benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV`

-- Section 2014(k). Help paid to someone else for my household.
@export Under section 2014(k)(1), is help paid to my landlord or another third party counted as money paid to my household?
GIVEN `the help is paid to a third party for my household by a State or local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the help paid to a third party, on your household's behalf, by a State or local government?
      `it is paid in place of cash assistance for living expenses under part A of title IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid in place of a regular cash benefit for living expenses under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act?
      `it is paid in place of a general assistance housing benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid in place of a housing benefit under a State or local general assistance program?
      `it is paid in place of a comparable housing benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid in place of a housing benefit under another basic assistance program comparable to general assistance, as the Secretary determines?
      `it is medical assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it medical assistance?
      `it is child care assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it child care assistance?
      `it is an energy payment or allowance described in section 2014(d)(11)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment or allowance described in section 2014(d)(11)?
      `it is paid by a housing authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it assistance provided by a State or local housing authority?
      `it is emergency help for migrant or seasonal farmworkers in the job stream` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it emergency assistance for a migrant or seasonal farmworker household during the period it is in the job stream?
      `it is emergency or special assistance the Secretary's regulations exclude` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it emergency and special assistance, to the extent the Secretary's regulations exclude it?
      `it is help under a general assistance program that by State law cannot be paid in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it assistance under a general assistance program, or a comparable local program, that State law does not allow to be paid to the household in cash?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(k)(1), is help paid to my landlord or another third party counted as money paid to my household` MEANS
    `s 2014(k)(1) the assistance to a third party is considered money payable directly to the household` `the help is paid to a third party for my household by a State or local government` `it is paid in place of cash assistance for living expenses under part A of title IV` `it is paid in place of a general assistance housing benefit` `it is paid in place of a comparable housing benefit`
        (`s 2014(k)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the assistance` `it is medical assistance` `it is child care assistance` `it is an energy payment or allowance described in section 2014(d)(11)` `it is paid by a housing authority` `it is emergency help for migrant or seasonal farmworkers in the job stream` `it is emergency or special assistance the Secretary's regulations exclude` `it is help under a general assistance program that by State law cannot be paid in cash`)

@export Under section 2014(k)(3), is an educational award paid to a school for my living expenses counted as money paid to my household?
GIVEN `it is an educational loan with deferred payment, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' educational benefit or the like` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an educational loan on which payment is deferred, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' educational benefit or the like?
      `it is paid to a third party for my living expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid to a third party on your household's behalf for living expenses?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(k)(3), is an educational award paid to a school for my living expenses counted as money paid to my household` MEANS
    `s 2014(k)(3) the educational assistance is treated as money payable directly to the household` `it is an educational loan with deferred payment, a grant, a scholarship, a fellowship, a veterans' educational benefit or the like` `it is paid to a third party for my living expenses`

@export Under section 2014(k)(4), is an energy assistance payment made under State law counted as money paid to my household?
GIVEN `the payment is made under a State law to provide energy assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment made under a State law to provide energy assistance (and not under a general assistance law whose help cannot be paid in cash)?
      `my household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is anyone in your household elderly (60 or older) or disabled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(k)(4), is an energy assistance payment made under State law counted as money paid to my household` MEANS
    `s 2014(k)(4)(A) the energy assistance payment is considered money payable directly to the household` `the payment is made under a State law to provide energy assistance` (JUST `my household includes an elderly or disabled member`)

@export Under section 2014(k)(4), is an energy assistance expense paid for my household under State law counted as one I paid myself?
GIVEN `the expense is paid on my household's behalf under a State law to provide energy assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the expense paid on your household's behalf under a State law to provide energy assistance?
      `my household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is anyone in your household elderly (60 or older) or disabled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(k)(4), is an energy assistance expense paid for my household under State law counted as one I paid myself` MEANS
    `s 2014(k)(4)(B) the energy assistance expense is considered an out-of-pocket expense incurred and paid by the household` `the expense is paid on my household's behalf under a State law to provide energy assistance` (JUST `my household includes an elderly or disabled member`)

-- Section 2014(l). On-the-job training earnings.
@export Under section 2014(l), are my on-the-job training earnings counted as earned income?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in years?
      `I am a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a dependent?
      `I take part in on-the-job training under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you take part in on-the-job training under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014(l), are my on-the-job training earnings counted as earned income` MEANS
    `s 2014(l) the earnings of the individual in on-the-job training are considered earned income` (`snap1 seat a person` `my age` FALSE) `I take part in on-the-job training under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act` `I am a dependent`

§ `Under section 2014a`

-- Section 2014a. Moving out of the State where the household is certified.
@export Under section 2014a, must my household report that it no longer lives in the State where it is certified?
GIVEN `my household is certified to take part in SNAP` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your household certified to participate in SNAP?
      `my household no longer lives in that State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your household no longer live in the State where it is certified?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2014a, must my household report that it no longer lives in the State where it is certified` MEANS
    `s 2014a the household is required to report that it no longer resides in the State in which it is certified` `my household is certified to take part in SNAP` `my household no longer lives in that State` `the date I am asking about`

§ `Under section 2018`

-- Section 2018(j). Store incentives. Ask this group only of a person who buys at a store that offers an incentive.
@export Under section 2018(j)(1), is this food an eligible incentive food?
GIVEN `it is a staple food identified for increased consumption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a staple food that is identified for increased consumption, consistent with the most recent dietary recommendations?
      `it is a fruit, vegetable, dairy, whole grain, or a product of one of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a fruit, vegetable, dairy, whole grain, or a product of one of them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2018(j)(1), is this food an eligible incentive food` MEANS
    `s 2018(j)(1) the food is an eligible incentive food` `it is a staple food identified for increased consumption` `it is a fruit, vegetable, dairy, whole grain, or a product of one of them`

@export Under section 2018(j)(2), may I use a store's incentive for this purchase?
GIVEN `I am buying an eligible incentive food` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you are buying an eligible incentive food?
      `I am using it at the point of purchase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you using the incentive at the point of purchase?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2018(j)(2), may I use a store's incentive for this purchase` MEANS
    `s 2018(j)(2)(A) the incentive may be used for the purchase` `I am buying an eligible incentive food` `I am using it at the point of purchase`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part snap2 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), sections 2015, 2027 and 2029 -- THE SEAT LAYER (snap2).
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text; nothing here is verified against it.
--
-- SEAT: a member of a household that applies for, or receives, benefits under the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program.
-- The person asks, on facts they can state, whether they or their household are eligible, what disqualifies a member,
-- for how long, what the work requirements ask of them, and what follows from a violation. Nothing here is new law:
-- every question calls one rule of the layer-1 modules imported above and restates none.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from the modules' own lists),
-- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The answers the Act
-- hands to someone else (the Secretary's determination, the State agency's choice, the answer of another section)
-- are asked as plain facts and passed to the layer-1 rule as a stated answer (JUST); a person who cannot state one has
-- no way to ask the question, which is the honest outcome, and the rule's own NOTHING for a case the text does not
-- cover is returned unchanged.
--
-- RESULTS. A yes or no is JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE, and NOTHING means that the text does not cover the case. A caller
-- must never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- THE @desc WORDING of most inputs is generated from the name of the layer-1 input ("Is it true that ...?"); the
-- questions of sections 2015(d)(1)(A), (e), (o)(1), (o)(2), (o)(3) and (r)(1) are written by hand. No seat question
-- is asked for a provision that speaks only to an official (a Secretary's power, a State agency's procedure, the
-- Committees): NOTES.md lists them.

§ `Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 -- the questions of a member of a household that applies for or receives benefits (snap2)`

§§ `Section 2015(a) to (c): eligibility, fraud, and reporting`

-- s 2015(a): the household or individual is eligible to participate.
@export Under section 2015(a), is the household or individual eligible to participate?
GIVEN `the standards of eligibility are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the standards of eligibility are met?
      `the household or individual meets and complies with the specific requirements of this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the household or individual meets and complies with the specific requirements of this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(a), is the household or individual eligible to participate` MEANS
    `s 2015(a) the household or individual is eligible to participate` (JUST `the standards of eligibility are met`) (JUST `the household or individual meets and complies with the specific requirements of this section`)

-- s 2015(b)(1): the period of ineligibility the finding carries.
@export Under section 2015(b)(1), what is the period of ineligibility the finding carries?
GIVEN `found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency?
      `intentionally made a false or misleading statement, or misrepresented, concealed or withheld facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that intentionally made a false or misleading statement, or misrepresented, concealed or withheld facts?
      `intentionally committed an act that violates this chapter, its regulations or a State statute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that intentionally committed an act that violates this chapter, its regulations or a State statute?
      `for the purpose of using, presenting, transferring, acquiring, receiving or possessing program benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that for the purpose of using, presenting, transferring, acquiring, receiving or possessing program benefits?
      `the occasion of such a determination, counting from 1` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the occasion of such a determination, counting from 1? (a number)
      `the occasion of a court finding of trading a controlled substance for benefits, 0 if none` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the occasion of a court finding of trading a controlled substance for benefits, 0 if none? (a number)
      `a court has found, for the first occasion, the trading of firearms, ammunition or explosives for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a court has found, for the first occasion, the trading of firearms, ammunition or explosives for benefits?
      `convicted of an offense under subsection (b) or (c) of section 2024 involving a covered item` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that convicted of an offense under subsection (b) or (c) of section 2024 involving a covered item?
      `the value of that item in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of that item in dollars? (a number)
GIVETH A `s 2015(b)(1) outcome`
`Under section 2015(b)(1), what is the period of ineligibility the finding carries` MEANS
    `s 2015(b)(1) the period of ineligibility the finding carries` `found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency` `intentionally made a false or misleading statement, or misrepresented, concealed or withheld facts` `intentionally committed an act that violates this chapter, its regulations or a State statute` `for the purpose of using, presenting, transferring, acquiring, receiving or possessing program benefits` `the occasion of such a determination, counting from 1` `the occasion of a court finding of trading a controlled substance for benefits, 0 if none` `a court has found, for the first occasion, the trading of firearms, ammunition or explosives for benefits` `convicted of an offense under subsection (b) or (c) of section 2024 involving a covered item` `the value of that item in dollars`

-- s 2015(b)(1): the household may receive increased benefits as the result of the member's disqualification.
@export Under section 2015(b)(1), may the household receive increased benefits as the result of the member's disqualification?
GIVEN `the member was disqualified under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the member was disqualified under subsection (b)?
      `the period of ineligibility is running` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the period of ineligibility is running?
      `the household's increase in benefits is the result of that disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the household's increase in benefits is the result of that disqualification?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(b)(1), may the household receive increased benefits as the result of the member's disqualification` MEANS
    `s 2015(b)(1) the household may receive increased benefits as the result of the member's disqualification` `the member was disqualified under subsection (b)` `the period of ineligibility is running` `the household's increase in benefits is the result of that disqualification`

-- s 2015(b)(2): the State agency has proceeded against the individual in a way the paragraph provides.
@export Under section 2015(b)(2), has the State agency proceeded against the individual in a way the paragraph provides?
GIVEN `the individual is alleged to have engaged in such activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is alleged to have engaged in such activity?
      `the State agency proceeds by an administrative hearing, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing at the State level` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State agency proceeds by an administrative hearing, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing at the State level?
      `the State agency refers the matter to appropriate authorities for civil or criminal action in a court of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State agency refers the matter to appropriate authorities for civil or criminal action in a court of law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(b)(2), has the State agency proceeded against the individual in a way the paragraph provides` MEANS
    `s 2015(b)(2) the State agency has proceeded against the individual in a way the paragraph provides` `the individual is alleged to have engaged in such activity` `the State agency proceeds by an administrative hearing, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing at the State level` `the State agency refers the matter to appropriate authorities for civil or criminal action in a court of law`

-- s 2015(b)(3): the period of ineligibility remains in effect.
@export Under section 2015(b)(3), does the period of ineligibility remain in effect?
GIVEN `the period of ineligibility is one provided for in paragraph (1) of subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the period of ineligibility is one provided for in paragraph (1) of subsection (b)?
      `the finding on which the ineligibility is based has been reversed by a court of appropriate jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the finding on which the ineligibility is based has been reversed by a court of appropriate jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(b)(3), does the period of ineligibility remain in effect` MEANS
