§§ `Section 2015(d): work requirements`

-- s 2015(d)(1)(A): the individual is ineligible to participate in the program.
@export Under section 2015(d)(1)(A), is the individual ineligible to participate in the program?
GIVEN `the age of the individual in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the age of the individual in years? (a number)
      `the individual is physically and mentally fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is physically and mentally fit?
      `refuses to register for employment at the time of application and every 12 months thereafter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the individual refuse to register for employment at the time of application and every 12 months thereafter?
      `refuses to participate in an employment and training program to the extent required by the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the individual refuse to participate in an employment and training program to the extent required by the State agency?
      `refuses to accept an offer of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the individual refuse to accept an offer of employment?
      `the offer is at a site or plant not subject to a strike or lockout at the time of the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offer is at a site or plant not subject to a strike or lockout at the time of the refusal?
      `the hourly wage offered, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly wage offered, in dollars? (a number)
      `the applicable Federal or State minimum hourly wage, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the applicable Federal or State minimum hourly wage, in dollars? (a number)
      `the hourly wage that would have governed had the Fair Labor Standards Act minimum rate applied, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hourly wage that would have governed had the Fair Labor Standards Act minimum rate applied, in dollars? (a number)
      `refuses to provide the State agency with sufficient information to determine employment status or job availability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the individual refuse to provide the State agency with sufficient information to determine employment status or job availability?
      `voluntarily quits a job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the individual voluntarily quit a job?
      `voluntarily reduces work effort` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the individual voluntarily reduce work effort?
      `hours worked per week after the reduction` IS A NUMBER @desc Give the number: hours worked per week after the reduction.
      `fails to comply with section 2029` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the individual fail to comply with section 2029?
      `there was good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there good cause?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(1)(A), is the individual ineligible to participate in the program` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(1)(A) the individual is ineligible to participate in the program` `the age of the individual in years` `the individual is physically and mentally fit` `the facts as stated`
    WHERE
        `the facts as stated` MEANS `s 2015(d)(1)(A) conduct` OF `refuses to register for employment at the time of application and every 12 months thereafter`, `refuses to participate in an employment and training program to the extent required by the State agency`, `refuses to accept an offer of employment`, `the offer is at a site or plant not subject to a strike or lockout at the time of the refusal`, `the hourly wage offered, in dollars`, `the applicable Federal or State minimum hourly wage, in dollars`, `the hourly wage that would have governed had the Fair Labor Standards Act minimum rate applied, in dollars`, `refuses to provide the State agency with sufficient information to determine employment status or job availability`, `voluntarily quits a job`, `voluntarily reduces work effort`, `hours worked per week after the reduction`, `fails to comply with section 2029`, (JUST `there was good cause`)

-- s 2015(d)(1)(B): the longest period of household ineligibility the State agency may determine, in days.
@export Under section 2015(d)(1)(B), what is the longest period of household ineligibility the State agency may determine, in days?
GIVEN `the individual is the head of a household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is the head of a household?
      `the individual became ineligible under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual became ineligible under subparagraph (A)?
      `the State agency has chosen to make the household ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State agency has chosen to make the household ineligible?
      `the duration of the individual's ineligibility under subparagraph (C), in days` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the duration of the individual's ineligibility under subparagraph (C), in days? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2015(d)(1)(B), what is the longest period of household ineligibility the State agency may determine, in days` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(1)(B) the longest period of household ineligibility the State agency may determine, in days` `the individual is the head of a household` (JUST `the individual became ineligible under subparagraph (A)`) `the State agency has chosen to make the household ineligible` `the duration of the individual's ineligibility under subparagraph (C), in days`

-- s 2015(d)(1)(B): the period the State agency determined is allowed.
@export Under section 2015(d)(1)(B), is the period the State agency determined allowed?
GIVEN `the longest period the State agency may determine, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest period the State agency may determine, in days? (a number)
      `the period the State agency determined, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the period the State agency determined, in days? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(1)(B), is the period the State agency determined allowed` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(1)(B) the period the State agency determined is allowed` (JUST `the longest period the State agency may determine, in days`) `the period the State agency determined, in days`

-- s 2015(d)(1)(C): the individual remains ineligible until.
@export Under section 2015(d)(1)(C), until when does the individual remain ineligible?
GIVEN `the number of the violation, counting from 1` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of the violation, counting from 1? (a number)
      `the date the individual became ineligible` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the individual became ineligible? (a date)
      `the date the individual becomes eligible under subparagraph (A), if it has come` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the individual becomes eligible under subparagraph (A), if it has come? (a date)
      `the date the State agency determined, if it determined one` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the State agency determined, if it determined one? (a date)
      `the State agency has elected permanent ineligibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State agency has elected permanent ineligibility?
GIVETH A `s 2015(d)(1)(C) outcome`
`Under section 2015(d)(1)(C), until when does the individual remain ineligible` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(1)(C) the individual remains ineligible until` `the number of the violation, counting from 1` `the date the individual became ineligible` (JUST `the date the individual becomes eligible under subparagraph (A), if it has come`) (JUST `the date the State agency determined, if it determined one`) `the State agency has elected permanent ineligibility`

-- s 2015(d)(1)(D)(i) and (ii): there is good cause, or the individual voluntarily quit or reduced work effort, as the Secretary determines.
@export Under section 2015(d)(1)(D)(i) and (ii), is there good cause, or did the individual voluntarily quit or reduce work effort, as the Secretary determines?
