GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(1)(D)(i) and (ii), is there good cause, or did the individual voluntarily quit or reduce work effort, as the Secretary determines` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(1)(D)(i) and (ii) there is good cause, or the individual voluntarily quit or reduced work effort, as the Secretary determines` (JUST `the Secretary's meaning covers the reason`)

-- s 2015(d)(1)(D)(iv): the individual is considered to have voluntarily quit without good cause.
@export Under section 2015(d)(1)(D)(iv), is the individual considered to have voluntarily quit without good cause?
GIVEN `the individual is an employee of the Federal Government, a State, or a political subdivision of a State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is an employee of the Federal Government, a State, or a political subdivision of a State?
      `the individual was dismissed for participating in a strike against that employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual was dismissed for participating in a strike against that employer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(1)(D)(iv), is the individual considered to have voluntarily quit without good cause` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(1)(D)(iv) the individual is considered to have voluntarily quit without good cause` `the individual is an employee of the Federal Government, a State, or a political subdivision of a State` `the individual was dismissed for participating in a strike against that employer`

-- s 2015(d)(1)(D)(v)(I): the State agency must allow the household to select the person as head of the household.
