      `a member of the household is striking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a member of the household is striking?
      `the increase in the allotment is the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the increase in the allotment is the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(3), may the household receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(3) the household may receive an increased allotment as the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member` `the household was eligible immediately prior to the strike` `a member of the household is striking` `the increase in the allotment is the result of a decrease in the income of the striking member`

§§ `Section 2015(d)(4): employment and training`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(D): the State agency may exempt the category or the individual member from the requirement.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(D), may the State agency exempt the category or the individual member from the requirement?
GIVEN `the exemption is for a category of household members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the exemption is for a category of household members?
      `the household member is in a category designated as exempt under clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the household member is in a category designated as exempt under clause (i)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(D), may the State agency exempt the category or the individual member from the requirement` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(D) the State agency may exempt the category or the individual member from the requirement` `the exemption is for a category of household members` `the household member is in a category designated as exempt under clause (i)`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(E)(iii): the individual is considered to be in compliance with the employment and training requirements.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(E)(iii), is the individual considered to be in compliance with the employment and training requirements?
GIVEN `the State agency requires the individual to participate in an employment and training program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State agency requires the individual to participate in an employment and training program?
      `the individual participates in a workforce partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual participates in a workforce partnership?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(E)(iii), is the individual considered to be in compliance with the employment and training requirements` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(E)(iii) the individual is considered to be in compliance with the employment and training requirements` `the State agency requires the individual to participate in an employment and training program` `the individual participates in a workforce partnership`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(F)(i): the required hours of the household's members exceed the limit.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(F)(i), do the required hours of the household's members exceed the limit?
GIVEN `the total hours of work required of the household's members in an employment and training program and in any program under section 2029 in the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total hours of work required of the household's members in an employment and training program and in any program under section 2029 in the month? (a number)
      `the household's allotment for the month, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the household's allotment for the month, in dollars? (a number)
      `the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or the Federal minimum hourly rate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or the Federal minimum hourly rate, in dollars? (a number)
      `the individual is voluntarily electing to participate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is voluntarily electing to participate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(F)(i), do the required hours of the household's members exceed the limit` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(F)(i) the required hours of the household's members exceed the limit` `the total hours of work required of the household's members in an employment and training program and in any program under section 2029 in the month` `the household's allotment for the month, in dollars` `the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or the Federal minimum hourly rate, in dollars` `the individual is voluntarily electing to participate`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(F)(ii): the required hours of the member exceed one hundred and twenty hours per month.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(F)(ii), do the required hours of the member exceed one hundred and twenty hours per month?
GIVEN `the hours of participation required of the member in the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hours of participation required of the member in the month? (a number)
      `the hours worked in another program under section 2029` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hours worked in another program under section 2029? (a number)
      `the hours worked for compensation in cash or in kind in any other capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hours worked for compensation in cash or in kind in any other capacity? (a number)
      `the member is voluntarily electing to participate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the member is voluntarily electing to participate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(F)(ii), do the required hours of the member exceed one hundred and twenty hours per month` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(F)(ii) the required hours of the member exceed one hundred and twenty hours per month` `the hours of participation required of the member in the month` `the hours worked in another program under section 2029` `the hours worked for compensation in cash or in kind in any other capacity` `the member is voluntarily electing to participate`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(I): the State agency is required to pay or reimburse the cost.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(I), is the State agency required to pay or reimburse the cost?
GIVEN `the person is a participant in a program carried out under this paragraph, including an individual participating under subparagraph (G)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a participant in a program carried out under this paragraph, including an individual participating under subparagraph (G)?
      `the cost is an actual cost of transportation or another actual cost other than dependent care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cost is an actual cost of transportation or another actual cost other than dependent care?
      `the cost is reasonably necessary and directly related to participation in the program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cost is reasonably necessary and directly related to participation in the program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(I), is the State agency required to pay or reimburse the cost` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(I) the State agency is required to pay or reimburse the cost` `the person is a participant in a program carried out under this paragraph, including an individual participating under subparagraph (G)` `the cost is an actual cost of transportation or another actual cost other than dependent care` `the cost is reasonably necessary and directly related to participation in the program`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II): the State agency is required to pay or reimburse the dependent care cost.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II), is the State agency required to pay or reimburse the dependent care cost?
GIVEN `the person is a participant in a program carried out under this paragraph, including an individual participating under subparagraph (G)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a participant in a program carried out under this paragraph, including an individual participating under subparagraph (G)?
      `the cost is an actual dependent care expense the State agency determined to be necessary for the participation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the cost is an actual dependent care expense the State agency determined to be necessary for the participation?
      `the person is the caretaker relative of a dependent in a family receiving benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act in a local area where an employment, training, or education program under title IV is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is the caretaker relative of a dependent in a family receiving benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act in a local area where an employment, training, or education program under title IV is in operation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II), is the State agency required to pay or reimburse the dependent care cost` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II) the State agency is required to pay or reimburse the dependent care cost` `the person is a participant in a program carried out under this paragraph, including an individual participating under subparagraph (G)` `the cost is an actual dependent care expense the State agency determined to be necessary for the participation` `the person is the caretaker relative of a dependent in a family receiving benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act in a local area where an employment, training, or education program under title IV is in operation`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II): the most the State agency may pay or reimburse for the dependent care, in dollars.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II), what is the most the State agency may pay or reimburse for the dependent care, in dollars?
GIVEN `the actual dependent care cost, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the actual dependent care cost, in dollars? (a number)
      `the applicable local market rate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the applicable local market rate, in dollars? (a number)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II), what is the most the State agency may pay or reimburse for the dependent care, in dollars` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II) the most the State agency may pay or reimburse for the dependent care, in dollars` `the actual dependent care cost, in dollars` `the applicable local market rate, in dollars`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i): the individual may be required to participate in the program.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i), may the individual be required to participate in the program?
GIVEN `the dependent care costs exceed the limit the State agency established under subclause (II)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the dependent care costs exceed the limit the State agency established under subclause (II)?
      `other actual costs exceed a limit established under subclause (I)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that other actual costs exceed a limit established under subclause (I)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(i), may the individual be required to participate in the program` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i) the individual may be required to participate in the program` `the dependent care costs exceed the limit the State agency established under subclause (II)` `other actual costs exceed a limit established under subclause (I)`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(I)(ii): the State agency may arrange dependent care instead of reimbursing it.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(ii), may the State agency arrange dependent care instead of reimbursing it?
GIVEN `the State agency arranges dependent care through providers by purchase of service contracts or vouchers, or provides vouchers to the household, in lieu of payments or reimbursements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State agency arranges dependent care through providers by purchase of service contracts or vouchers, or provides vouchers to the household, in lieu of payments or reimbursements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(ii), may the State agency arrange dependent care instead of reimbursing it` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(I)(ii) the State agency may arrange dependent care instead of reimbursing it` `the State agency arranges dependent care through providers by purchase of service contracts or vouchers, or provides vouchers to the household, in lieu of payments or reimbursements`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(I)(iii)(I): the value or amount is treated as income for the other program.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(iii)(I), is the value or amount treated as income for the other program?
GIVEN `the value or amount is of dependent care services provided or arranged under clause (ii), or a payment or reimbursement under clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the value or amount is of dependent care services provided or arranged under clause (ii), or a payment or reimbursement under clause (i)?
      `the other program is a Federal or federally assisted program that bases eligibility for, or the amount of benefits on, need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other program is a Federal or federally assisted program that bases eligibility for, or the amount of benefits on, need?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(iii)(I), is the value or amount treated as income for the other program` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(I)(iii)(I) the value or amount is treated as income for the other program` `the value or amount is of dependent care services provided or arranged under clause (ii), or a payment or reimbursement under clause (i)` `the other program is a Federal or federally assisted program that bases eligibility for, or the amount of benefits on, need`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(I)(iii)(II): the value or amount may be claimed as an employment-related expense for the credit under section 21 of title 26.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(iii)(II), may the value or amount be claimed as an employment-related expense for the credit under section 21 of title 26?
GIVEN `the value or amount is of dependent care services provided or arranged under clause (ii), or a payment or reimbursement under clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the value or amount is of dependent care services provided or arranged under clause (ii), or a payment or reimbursement under clause (i)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(I)(iii)(II), may the value or amount be claimed as an employment-related expense for the credit under section 21 of title 26` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(I)(iii)(II) the value or amount may be claimed as an employment-related expense for the credit under section 21 of title 26` `the value or amount is of dependent care services provided or arranged under clause (ii), or a payment or reimbursement under clause (i)`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(N)(iii)(II): the State agency may require the member to participate in a workforce partnership.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(N)(iii)(II), may the State agency require the member to participate in a workforce partnership?
GIVEN `the person is a member of a household participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a member of a household participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(N)(iii)(II), may the State agency require the member to participate in a workforce partnership` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(N)(iii)(II) the State agency may require the member to participate in a workforce partnership` `the person is a member of a household participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(O)(ii): the individual is found to have refused without good cause to participate in an employment and training program.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(O)(ii), is the individual found to have refused without good cause to participate in an employment and training program?
GIVEN `the individual is undergoing and complying with the process established under clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is undergoing and complying with the process established under clause (i)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(O)(ii), is the individual found to have refused without good cause to participate in an employment and training program` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(O)(ii) the individual is found to have refused without good cause to participate in an employment and training program` `the individual is undergoing and complying with the process established under clause (i)`

-- s 2015(d)(4)(N)(iii)(I): at certification and recertification a household member subject to work requirements is given the list of certified workforce partnerships.
@export Under section 2015(d)(4)(N)(iii)(I), must the State agency give me the list of certified workforce partnerships?
GIVEN `it is my certification or recertification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this your certification or recertification?
      `I am subject to work requirements under subsection (d)(1) or subsection (o)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to work requirements under section 2015(d)(1) or section 2015(o)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(d)(4)(N)(iii)(I), must the State agency give me the list of certified workforce partnerships` MEANS
    `s 2015(d)(4)(N)(iii)(I) the State agency is required to provide the list of certified workforce partnerships to the household member` `it is my certification or recertification` `I am subject to work requirements under subsection (d)(1) or subsection (o)`

§§ `Section 2015(e) to (n): students, status, and the other bars`

-- s 2015(e): the individual is ineligible as a student.
@export Under section 2015(e), is the individual ineligible as a student?
GIVEN `the individual is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate?
      `the individual is enrolled at least half-time in an institution of higher education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is enrolled at least half-time in an institution of higher education?
      `the individual's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the individual's age in years? (a number)
      `the individual is physically and mentally fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is physically and mentally fit?
      `the individual is assigned to or placed in the institution through a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is assigned to or placed in the institution through a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act?
      `the individual is placed through an employment and training program under section 2015 and the course is part of a career and technical education program that may be completed in not more than 4 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is placed through an employment and training program under section 2015 and the course is part of a career and technical education program that may be completed in not more than 4 years?
      `the individual is placed through an employment and training program under section 2015 and the course is limited to remedial courses, basic adult education, literacy, or English as a second language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is placed through an employment and training program under section 2015 and the course is limited to remedial courses, basic adult education, literacy, or English as a second language?
      `the individual is placed through a program under section 2296 of title 19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is placed through a program under section 2296 of title 19?
      `the individual is placed through another State or local government employment and training program, as determined to be appropriate by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is placed through another State or local government employment and training program, as determined to be appropriate by the Secretary?
      `the individual's hours of employment per week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the individual's hours of employment per week? (a number)
      `the individual participates in a State or federally financed work study program during the regular school year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual participates in a State or federally financed work study program during the regular school year?
      `the individual is a parent with responsibility for the care of a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is a parent with responsibility for the care of a dependent child?
      `the age of the dependent child in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the age of the dependent child in years? (a number)
      `adequate child care is available to enable the individual to attend class and satisfy the requirements of paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that adequate child care is available to enable the individual to attend class and satisfy the requirements of paragraph (4)?
      `the individual is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act?
      `the individual is enrolled as a result of participation in the work incentive program under title IV of the Social Security Act or its successor programs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is enrolled as a result of participation in the work incentive program under title IV of the Social Security Act or its successor programs?
      `the individual is enrolled full-time as determined by the institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is enrolled full-time as determined by the institution?
      `the individual is a single parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is a single parent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(e), is the individual ineligible as a student` MEANS
    `s 2015(e) the individual is ineligible as a student` `the facts as stated`
    WHERE
        `the facts as stated` MEANS `s 2015(e) facts` OF `the individual is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate`, `the individual is enrolled at least half-time in an institution of higher education`, `the individual's age in years`, `the individual is physically and mentally fit`, `the individual is assigned to or placed in the institution through a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act`, `the individual is placed through an employment and training program under section 2015 and the course is part of a career and technical education program that may be completed in not more than 4 years`, `the individual is placed through an employment and training program under section 2015 and the course is limited to remedial courses, basic adult education, literacy, or English as a second language`, `the individual is placed through a program under section 2296 of title 19`, (JUST `the individual is placed through another State or local government employment and training program, as determined to be appropriate by the Secretary`), `the individual's hours of employment per week`, `the individual participates in a State or federally financed work study program during the regular school year`, `the individual is a parent with responsibility for the care of a dependent child`, `the age of the dependent child in years`, `adequate child care is available to enable the individual to attend class and satisfy the requirements of paragraph (4)`, `the individual is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act`, `the individual is enrolled as a result of participation in the work incentive program under title IV of the Social Security Act or its successor programs`, `the individual is enrolled full-time as determined by the institution`, `the individual is a single parent`

-- s 2015(f): the individual is ineligible for want of residence or status.
@export Under section 2015(f), is the individual ineligible for want of residence or status?
GIVEN `my immigration status` IS AN `Immigration status` @desc Which of these is your immigration status?
      `I live in the United States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live in the United States?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(f), is the individual ineligible for want of residence or status` MEANS
    `s 2015(f) the individual is ineligible for want of residence or status` `me, as the person asked about`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the rule above never reads the fields of the person that are not asked.
        `me, as the person asked about` MEANS Individual OF 0, TRUE, FALSE, `my immigration status`, `I live in the United States`, FALSE, 0, FALSE

-- s 2015(f): the income of the ineligible individual counted for the household, in dollars.
@export Under section 2015(f), what is the income of the ineligible individual counted for the household, in dollars?
GIVEN `the individual was rendered ineligible under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual was rendered ineligible under this subsection?
      `the individual's income, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the individual's income, in dollars? (a number)
      `the State has chosen to leave out a pro rata share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State has chosen to leave out a pro rata share?
      `the pro rata share, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the pro rata share, in dollars? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2015(f), what is the income of the ineligible individual counted for the household, in dollars` MEANS
    `s 2015(f) the income of the ineligible individual counted for the household, in dollars` `the individual was rendered ineligible under this subsection` `the individual's income, in dollars` `the State has chosen to leave out a pro rata share` `the pro rata share, in dollars`

-- s 2015(f): the financial resources of the ineligible individual are considered for the household.
@export Under section 2015(f), are the financial resources of the ineligible individual considered for the household?
GIVEN `the individual was rendered ineligible under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual was rendered ineligible under this subsection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(f), are the financial resources of the ineligible individual considered for the household` MEANS
    `s 2015(f) the financial resources of the ineligible individual are considered for the household` `the individual was rendered ineligible under this subsection`

-- s 2015(g): the individual is not considered a member of a household for the month.
@export Under section 2015(g), is the individual not considered a member of a household for the month?
GIVEN `the individual receives supplemental security income benefits, State supplementary payments described in section 1616, or payments of the type referred to in section 212(a) of Public Law 93-66` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual receives supplemental security income benefits, State supplementary payments described in section 1616, or payments of the type referred to in section 212(a) of Public Law 93-66?
      `the individual resides in a State that provides State supplementary payments of the type described in section 1616(a) and section 212(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual resides in a State that provides State supplementary payments of the type described in section 1616(a) and section 212(a)?
      `the Commissioner of Social Security has found the level specifically increased so as to include the bonus value of food stamps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Commissioner of Social Security has found the level specifically increased so as to include the bonus value of food stamps?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(g), is the individual not considered a member of a household for the month` MEANS
    `s 2015(g) the individual is not considered a member of a household for the month` `the individual receives supplemental security income benefits, State supplementary payments described in section 1616, or payments of the type referred to in section 212(a) of Public Law 93-66` `the individual resides in a State that provides State supplementary payments of the type described in section 1616(a) and section 212(a)` (JUST `the Commissioner of Social Security has found the level specifically increased so as to include the bonus value of food stamps`)

-- s 2015(h): the household is ineligible on the date.
@export Under section 2015(h), is the household ineligible on the date?
GIVEN `the household knowingly transferred assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the household knowingly transferred assets?
      `the transfer was for the purpose of qualifying or attempting to qualify for the program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transfer was for the purpose of qualifying or attempting to qualify for the program?
      `the date of discovery of the transfer` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of discovery of the transfer? (a date)
      `the number of months for which the household is made ineligible` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of months for which the household is made ineligible? (a number)
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date asked about? (a date)
GIVETH A `s 2015(h) outcome`
`Under section 2015(h), is the household ineligible on the date` MEANS
    `s 2015(h) the household is ineligible on the date` `the household knowingly transferred assets` `the transfer was for the purpose of qualifying or attempting to qualify for the program` `the date of discovery of the transfer` `the number of months for which the household is made ineligible` `the date asked about`

-- s 2015(i)(1): the State agency may impose the same disqualification under the program.
@export Under section 2015(i)(1), may the State agency impose the same disqualification under the program?
GIVEN `a disqualification is imposed on a member of a household for a failure to perform an action required under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a disqualification is imposed on a member of a household for a failure to perform an action required under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(i)(1), may the State agency impose the same disqualification under the program` MEANS
    `s 2015(i)(1) the State agency may impose the same disqualification under the program` `a disqualification is imposed on a member of a household for a failure to perform an action required under a Federal, State, or local law relating to a means-tested public assistance program`

-- s 2015(i)(2): the State agency may use the rules and procedures of part A of title IV.
@export Under section 2015(i)(2), may the State agency use the rules and procedures of part A of title IV?
GIVEN `the disqualification is imposed under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the disqualification is imposed under paragraph (1)?
      `the failure was to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the failure was to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(i)(2), may the State agency use the rules and procedures of part A of title IV` MEANS
    `s 2015(i)(2) the State agency may use the rules and procedures of part A of title IV` `the disqualification is imposed under paragraph (1)` `the failure was to perform an action required under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act`

-- s 2015(i)(3): a prior disqualification under subsection (d) is considered in determining the former member's eligibility.
@export Under section 2015(i)(3), is a prior disqualification under subsection (d) considered in determining the former member's eligibility?
GIVEN `the member is disqualified under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the member is disqualified under paragraph (1)?
      `the disqualification period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the disqualification period has expired?
      `there was a prior disqualification under subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there was a prior disqualification under subsection (d)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(i)(3), is a prior disqualification under subsection (d) considered in determining the former member's eligibility` MEANS
    `s 2015(i)(3) a prior disqualification under subsection (d) is considered in determining the former member's eligibility` `the member is disqualified under paragraph (1)` `the disqualification period has expired` `there was a prior disqualification under subsection (d)`

-- s 2015(i)(3): the member who applies is treated as a new applicant.
@export Under section 2015(i)(3), is the member who applies treated as a new applicant?
GIVEN `the member is disqualified under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the member is disqualified under paragraph (1)?
      `the disqualification period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the disqualification period has expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(i)(3), is the member who applies treated as a new applicant` MEANS
    `s 2015(i)(3) the member who applies is treated as a new applicant` `the member is disqualified under paragraph (1)` `the disqualification period has expired`

-- s 2015(j): the period of ineligibility for receiving multiple benefits.
@export Under section 2015(j), for how long is the individual ineligible for receiving multiple benefits?
GIVEN `the individual is found by a State agency to have made a fraudulent statement or representation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is found by a State agency to have made a fraudulent statement or representation?
      `the individual is convicted in a Federal or State court of having made a fraudulent statement or representation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is convicted in a Federal or State court of having made a fraudulent statement or representation?
      `the statement or representation was with respect to the identity or place of residence of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statement or representation was with respect to the identity or place of residence of the individual?
      `it was made in order to receive multiple benefits simultaneously under the program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was made in order to receive multiple benefits simultaneously under the program?
GIVETH A `s 2015(j) outcome`
`Under section 2015(j), for how long is the individual ineligible for receiving multiple benefits` MEANS
    `s 2015(j) the period of ineligibility for receiving multiple benefits` `the individual is found by a State agency to have made a fraudulent statement or representation` `the individual is convicted in a Federal or State court of having made a fraudulent statement or representation` `the statement or representation was with respect to the identity or place of residence of the individual` `it was made in order to receive multiple benefits simultaneously under the program`

-- s 2015(k)(1): the individual is ineligible while fleeing or violating probation or parole.
@export Under section 2015(k)(1), is the individual ineligible while fleeing or violating probation or parole?
GIVEN `the person is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate?
      `the individual is fleeing, as the Secretary defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is fleeing, as the Secretary defines the term?
      `the flight is to avoid prosecution, or custody or confinement after conviction, for a felony under the law of the place fled from, or for a high misdemeanor in New Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the flight is to avoid prosecution, or custody or confinement after conviction, for a felony under the law of the place fled from, or for a high misdemeanor in New Jersey?
      `the individual is violating a condition of probation or parole imposed under a Federal or State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is violating a condition of probation or parole imposed under a Federal or State law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(k)(1), is the individual ineligible while fleeing or violating probation or parole` MEANS
    `s 2015(k)(1) the individual is ineligible while fleeing or violating probation or parole` `the person is a member of a household otherwise eligible to participate` (JUST `the individual is fleeing, as the Secretary defines the term`) `the flight is to avoid prosecution, or custody or confinement after conviction, for a felony under the law of the place fled from, or for a high misdemeanor in New Jersey` `the individual is violating a condition of probation or parole imposed under a Federal or State law`

-- s 2015(l): the individual is ineligible for want of cooperation with the child support agency.
@export Under section 2015(l), is the individual ineligible for want of cooperation with the child support agency?
GIVEN `the State agency has chosen to apply this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State agency has chosen to apply this paragraph?
      `the individual is a parent or other individual living with and exercising parental control over a child under the age of 18 who has an absent parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is a parent or other individual living with and exercising parental control over a child under the age of 18 who has an absent parent?
      `the child was born out of wedlock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the child was born out of wedlock?
      `the individual cooperates in establishing the paternity of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual cooperates in establishing the paternity of the child?
      `the individual cooperates in obtaining support for the child, or for the individual and the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual cooperates in obtaining support for the child, or for the individual and the child?
      `good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(l), is the individual ineligible for want of cooperation with the child support agency` MEANS
    `s 2015(l) the individual is ineligible for want of cooperation with the child support agency` `the State agency has chosen to apply this paragraph` `the individual is a parent or other individual living with and exercising parental control over a child under the age of 18 who has an absent parent` `the child was born out of wedlock` `the individual cooperates in establishing the paternity of the child` `the individual cooperates in obtaining support for the child, or for the individual and the child` (JUST `good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards`)

-- s 2015(l)(2): paragraph (1) does not apply to the individual.
@export Under section 2015(l)(2), is it so that paragraph (1) does not apply to the individual?
GIVEN `good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(l)(2), is it so that paragraph (1) does not apply to the individual` MEANS
    `s 2015(l)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the individual` (JUST `good cause for refusing to cooperate is found by the State agency under the Secretary's standards`)

-- s 2015(l)(3): the individual is required to pay a fee or other cost for the service.
@export Under section 2015(l)(3), is the individual required to pay a fee or other cost for the service?
GIVEN `the service is provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the service is provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(l)(3), is the individual required to pay a fee or other cost for the service` MEANS
    `s 2015(l)(3) the individual is required to pay a fee or other cost for the service` `the service is provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act`

-- s 2015(m)(1): the noncustodial parent is ineligible for refusing to cooperate with the child support agency.
@export Under section 2015(m)(1), is the noncustodial parent ineligible for refusing to cooperate with the child support agency?
GIVEN `the State agency has chosen to apply this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State agency has chosen to apply this paragraph?
      `the individual is a putative or identified noncustodial parent of a child under the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is a putative or identified noncustodial parent of a child under the age of 18?
      `the child was born out of wedlock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the child was born out of wedlock?
      `the individual refuses to cooperate in establishing the paternity of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual refuses to cooperate in establishing the paternity of the child?
      `the individual refuses to cooperate in providing support for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual refuses to cooperate in providing support for the child?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(m)(1), is the noncustodial parent ineligible for refusing to cooperate with the child support agency` MEANS
    `s 2015(m)(1) the noncustodial parent is ineligible for refusing to cooperate with the child support agency` `the State agency has chosen to apply this paragraph` `the individual is a putative or identified noncustodial parent of a child under the age of 18` `the child was born out of wedlock` `the individual refuses to cooperate in establishing the paternity of the child` `the individual refuses to cooperate in providing support for the child`

-- s 2015(m)(2): the matter is a refusal to cooperate under the guidelines and procedures.
@export Under section 2015(m)(2), is the matter a refusal to cooperate under the guidelines and procedures?
GIVEN `the Secretary's guidelines and the State agency's procedures say the matter is a refusal to cooperate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Secretary's guidelines and the State agency's procedures say the matter is a refusal to cooperate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(m)(2), is the matter a refusal to cooperate under the guidelines and procedures` MEANS
    `s 2015(m)(2) the matter is a refusal to cooperate under the guidelines and procedures` (JUST `the Secretary's guidelines and the State agency's procedures say the matter is a refusal to cooperate`)

-- s 2015(m)(3): the individual is required to pay a fee or other cost for the service.
@export Under section 2015(m)(3), is the individual required to pay a fee or other cost for the service?
GIVEN `the service is provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the service is provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(m)(3), is the individual required to pay a fee or other cost for the service` MEANS
    `s 2015(m)(3) the individual is required to pay a fee or other cost for the service` `the service is provided under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act`

-- s 2015(n): the individual is ineligible for the month for child support arrears.
@export Under section 2015(n), is the individual ineligible for the month for child support arrears?
GIVEN `the State agency has chosen to apply this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State agency has chosen to apply this subsection?
      `the individual is delinquent during the month in a payment due under a court order for the support of a child of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is delinquent during the month in a payment due under a court order for the support of a child of the individual?
      `a court is allowing the individual to delay payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a court is allowing the individual to delay payment?
      `the individual is complying with a payment plan approved by a court or by the State agency designated under part D of title IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is complying with a payment plan approved by a court or by the State agency designated under part D of title IV?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(n), is the individual ineligible for the month for child support arrears` MEANS
    `s 2015(n) the individual is ineligible for the month for child support arrears` `the State agency has chosen to apply this subsection` `the individual is delinquent during the month in a payment due under a court order for the support of a child of the individual` `a court is allowing the individual to delay payment` `the individual is complying with a payment plan approved by a court or by the State agency designated under part D of title IV`

-- s 2015(m)(4): what a noncustodial parent's information, collected by a State agency administering the child support program, may be used for.
@export Under section 2015(m)(4), must the State agency restrict the use of information about me to the purposes for which it was collected?
GIVEN `the information was collected by a State agency administering the child support program under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information about you collected by a State agency administering the child support program under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(m)(4), must the State agency restrict the use of information about me to the purposes for which it was collected` MEANS
    `s 2015(m)(4) the State agency is required to provide safeguards restricting the use of the information to the purposes for which it was collected` `the information was collected by a State agency administering the child support program under part D of title IV of the Social Security Act`

§§ `Section 2015(o): the work requirement for some adults`

-- s 2015(o)(3): paragraph (2) does not apply to the individual.
@export Under section 2015(o)(3), does paragraph (2) not apply to the individual?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in years?
      `I am pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant?
      `the individual is medically certified as physically or mentally unfit for employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is medically certified as physically or mentally unfit for employment?
      `the individual is a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for a dependent child?
      `the age of that child in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the age of that child in years? (a number)
      `the person is exempt from the requirements of paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is exempt from the requirements of paragraph (1)?
      `the individual is an Indian or an Urban Indian as defined in paragraphs (13) and (28) of section 1603 of title 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is an Indian or an Urban Indian as defined in paragraphs (13) and (28) of section 1603 of title 25?
      `the individual is a California Indian described in section 1679(a) of title 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is a California Indian described in section 1679(a) of title 25?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(3), does paragraph (2) not apply to the individual` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(3) paragraph (2) does not apply to the individual` `me, as the person asked about` `the individual is medically certified as physically or mentally unfit for employment` `the individual is a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for a dependent child` `the age of that child in years` (JUST `the person is exempt from the requirements of paragraph (1)`) `the individual is an Indian or an Urban Indian as defined in paragraphs (13) and (28) of section 1603 of title 25` `the individual is a California Indian described in section 1679(a) of title 25`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the rule above never reads the fields of the person that are not asked.
        `me, as the person asked about` MEANS Individual OF `my age in years`, TRUE, `I am pregnant`, `a citizen or national of the United States`, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE

-- s 2015(o)(4)(A): the Secretary may waive the applicability of paragraph (2) to the group of individuals.
@export Under section 2015(o)(4)(A), may the Secretary waive the applicability of paragraph (2) to the group of individuals?
GIVEN `the State agency has requested the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the State agency has requested the waiver?
      `the chief executive officer of the State supports the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the chief executive officer of the State supports the request?
      `the Secretary has determined that the area in which the individuals reside qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Secretary has determined that the area in which the individuals reside qualifies?
      `the unemployment rate of the area, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the unemployment rate of the area, as a fraction? (a number)
      `the State in which the area lies` IS AN `Area` @desc Which applies: the State in which the area lies?
      `the national unemployment rate, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the national unemployment rate, as a fraction? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(4)(A), may the Secretary waive the applicability of paragraph (2) to the group of individuals` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(4)(A) the Secretary may waive the applicability of paragraph (2) to the group of individuals` `the State agency has requested the waiver` `the chief executive officer of the State supports the request` (JUST `the Secretary has determined that the area in which the individuals reside qualifies`) `the unemployment rate of the area, as a fraction` `the State in which the area lies` `the national unemployment rate, as a fraction`

-- s 2015(o)(4)(C): the place is a noncontiguous State.
@export Under section 2015(o)(4)(C), is the place a noncontiguous State?
GIVEN `place` IS AN `Area` @desc Which applies: place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(4)(C), is the place a noncontiguous State` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(4)(C) the place is a noncontiguous State` `place`

-- s 2015(o)(5)(A): the individual regains eligibility.
@export Under section 2015(o)(5)(A), does the individual regain eligibility?
GIVEN `the individual was denied eligibility under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual was denied eligibility under paragraph (2)?
      `hours the individual worked in the 30-day period` IS A NUMBER @desc Give the number: hours the individual worked in the 30-day period.
      `hours the individual participated in a work program in the 30-day period, as determined by a State agency` IS A NUMBER @desc Give the number: hours the individual participated in a work program in the 30-day period, as determined by a State agency.
      `the individual complied with the requirements of the work program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual complied with the requirements of the work program?
      `the individual participated in and complied with a program under section 2029 or a comparable program in the 30-day period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual participated in and complied with a program under section 2029 or a comparable program in the 30-day period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(5)(A), does the individual regain eligibility` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(5)(A) the individual regains eligibility` `the individual was denied eligibility under paragraph (2)` `hours the individual worked in the 30-day period` `hours the individual participated in a work program in the 30-day period, as determined by a State agency` `the individual complied with the requirements of the work program` `the individual participated in and complied with a program under section 2029 or a comparable program in the 30-day period`

-- s 2015(o)(5)(B): the individual remains eligible.
@export Under section 2015(o)(5)(B), does the individual remain eligible?
GIVEN `the individual regained eligibility under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual regained eligibility under subparagraph (A)?
      `the individual meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(5)(B), does the individual remain eligible` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(5)(B) the individual remains eligible` `the individual regained eligibility under subparagraph (A)` `the individual meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)`

-- s 2015(o)(5)(C): the individual remains eligible on the date for the 3-month period.
@export Under section 2015(o)(5)(C), does the individual remain eligible on the date for the 3-month period?
GIVEN `the individual regained eligibility under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual regained eligibility under subparagraph (A)?
      `the individual no longer meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual no longer meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)?
      `the date the individual first notified the State agency` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the individual first notified the State agency? (a date)
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date asked about? (a date)
      `the individual received benefits pursuant to clause (i) for a 3-month period within the 36 months before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual received benefits pursuant to clause (i) for a 3-month period within the 36 months before?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(5)(C), does the individual remain eligible on the date for the 3-month period` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(5)(C) the individual remains eligible on the date for the 3-month period` `the individual regained eligibility under subparagraph (A)` `the individual no longer meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)` `the date the individual first notified the State agency` `the date asked about` `the individual received benefits pursuant to clause (i) for a 3-month period within the 36 months before`

-- s 2015(o)(6)(A)(ii): the individual is a covered individual.
@export Under section 2015(o)(6)(A)(ii), is the individual a covered individual?
GIVEN `the individual is a member of a household that receives benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is a member of a household that receives benefits?
      `the individual was denied eligibility solely due to paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual was denied eligibility solely due to paragraph (2)?
      `the individual is not eligible for an exception under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is not eligible for an exception under paragraph (3)?
      `the individual does not reside in an area covered by a waiver granted under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual does not reside in an area covered by a waiver granted under paragraph (4)?
      `the individual is not complying with subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is not complying with subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)?
      `the individual is not receiving benefits during the 3 months of eligibility provided under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is not receiving benefits during the 3 months of eligibility provided under paragraph (2)?
      `the individual is not receiving benefits under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is not receiving benefits under paragraph (5)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(6)(A)(ii), is the individual a covered individual` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(6)(A)(ii) the individual is a covered individual` `the individual is a member of a household that receives benefits` `the individual was denied eligibility solely due to paragraph (2)` `the individual is not eligible for an exception under paragraph (3)` `the individual does not reside in an area covered by a waiver granted under paragraph (4)` `the individual is not complying with subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)` `the individual is not receiving benefits during the 3 months of eligibility provided under paragraph (2)` `the individual is not receiving benefits under paragraph (5)`

-- s 2015(o)(6)(B): the State agency may provide an exemption from paragraph (2).
@export Under section 2015(o)(6)(B), may the State agency provide an exemption from paragraph (2)?
GIVEN `the individual is a covered individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is a covered individual?
      `the average monthly number of exemptions is within the limit of subparagraphs (C) through (I)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the average monthly number of exemptions is within the limit of subparagraphs (C) through (I)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(6)(B), may the State agency provide an exemption from paragraph (2)` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(6)(B) the State agency may provide an exemption from paragraph (2)` (JUST `the individual is a covered individual`) (JUST `the average monthly number of exemptions is within the limit of subparagraphs (C) through (I)`)

-- s 2015(o)(8): this subsection makes the individual eligible for benefits.
@export Under section 2015(o)(8), does this subsection make the individual eligible for benefits?
GIVEN `the individual is otherwise eligible for benefits under the other provisions of this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is otherwise eligible for benefits under the other provisions of this chapter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(8), does this subsection make the individual eligible for benefits` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(8) this subsection makes the individual eligible for benefits` (JUST `the individual is otherwise eligible for benefits under the other provisions of this chapter`)

-- s 2015(o)(1): the closed list of what is a "work program".
@export Under section 2015(o)(1), is my program a work program?
GIVEN `my program is a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your program a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act?
      `my program is a program under section 2296 of title 19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your program a program under section 2296 of title 19?
      `my program is a program of employment and training operated or supervised by a State or political subdivision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your program a program of employment and training operated or supervised by a State or political subdivision of a State?
      `its standards are approved by the Governor of the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your program meet standards approved by the Governor of the State?
      `it is a supervised job search program or a job search training program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your program a supervised job search program or a job search training program?
      `my program is a program of employment and training for veterans operated by the Department of Labor or the Department of Veterans Affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your program a program of employment and training for veterans operated by the Department of Labor or the Department of Veterans Affairs?
      `the Secretary approved it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary approved your veterans program?
      `my program is a workforce partnership under subsection (d)(4)(N)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your program a workforce partnership under subsection (d)(4)(N)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(1), is my program a work program` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(1) the program is a work program` `my kind of program`
    WHERE
        `my kind of program` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `my program is a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act` THEN `s 2015(o)(1)(A) a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act`
                IF `my program is a program under section 2296 of title 19` THEN `s 2015(o)(1)(B) a program under section 2296 of title 19`
                IF `my program is a program of employment and training operated or supervised by a State or political subdivision` THEN `s 2015(o)(1)(C) a program of employment and training operated or supervised by a State or political subdivision` OF `its standards are approved by the Governor of the State`, `it is a supervised job search program or a job search training program`
                IF `my program is a program of employment and training for veterans operated by the Department of Labor or the Department of Veterans Affairs` THEN `s 2015(o)(1)(D) a program of employment and training for veterans operated by the Department of Labor or the Department of Veterans Affairs` OF `the Secretary approved it`
                IF `my program is a workforce partnership under subsection (d)(4)(N)` THEN `s 2015(o)(1)(E) a workforce partnership under subsection (d)(4)(N)`
                OTHERWISE `s 2015(o)(1) another kind of program`

-- s 2015(o)(2): the 36-month work requirement. The months are asked as two counts; the list the rule reads is built from them.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A `s 2015(o)(2) month`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 2015(o)(2) month`
`Under section 2015(o)(2), n copies of a month` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0 THEN EMPTY ELSE x FOLLOWED BY `Under section 2015(o)(2), n copies of a month` (n MINUS 1) x

@export Under section 2015(o)(2), am I ineligible for failing the work requirement?
GIVEN `the number of months in the last 36 in which I received benefits and did none of the four things` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the last 36 months did you receive benefits and not work 20 hours a week, not take part in a work program for 20 hours a week and comply, not take part in a workfare or comparable program, and not receive benefits under paragraph (3), (4), (5) or (6)?
      `the number of my other months among the last 36` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the last 36 months are not in that count? (the two numbers together are at most 36)
      `an exception of paragraph (3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an exception of paragraph (3) apply to you (under 18 or over 65, medically unfit, a parent of a child under 14, exempt under (d)(2), pregnant, an Indian or Urban Indian, or a California Indian)?
      `a waiver of paragraph (4) covers my area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a waiver of paragraph (4) cover the area where you live?
      `I have regained eligibility under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you regained eligibility under paragraph (5)?
      `my State agency exempts me under paragraph (6) or (7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your State agency exempt you under paragraph (6) or (7)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(o)(2), am I ineligible for failing the work requirement` MEANS
    `s 2015(o)(2) the individual is ineligible for failing the work requirement` `my months` (JUST `an exception of paragraph (3) applies to me`) `a waiver of paragraph (4) covers my area` `I have regained eligibility under paragraph (5)` `my State agency exempts me under paragraph (6) or (7)`
    WHERE
        `my months` MEANS append (`Under section 2015(o)(2), n copies of a month` `the number of months in the last 36 in which I received benefits and did none of the four things` (`s 2015(o)(2) month` OF TRUE, 0, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)) (`Under section 2015(o)(2), n copies of a month` `the number of my other months among the last 36` (`s 2015(o)(2) month` OF FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))

§§ `Section 2015(p) to (s): cash, food sales, felons, winnings`

-- s 2015(p): the person is ineligible for benefits.
@export Under section 2015(p), is the person ineligible for benefits?
GIVEN `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)?
      `the finding is that the person intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the finding is that the person intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(p), is the person ineligible for benefits` MEANS
    `s 2015(p) the person is ineligible for benefits` `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` `the finding is that the person intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount`

-- s 2015(p): the period of ineligibility.
@export Under section 2015(p), what is the period of ineligibility?
GIVEN `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)?
      `the finding is that the person intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the finding is that the person intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of ineligibility`
`Under section 2015(p), what is the period of ineligibility` MEANS
    `s 2015(p) the period of ineligibility` `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` `the finding is that the person intentionally obtained cash by purchasing products with benefits that have containers that require return deposits, discarding the product, and returning the container for the deposit amount`

-- s 2015(q): the person is ineligible for benefits.
@export Under section 2015(q), is the person ineligible for benefits?
GIVEN `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)?
      `the finding is that the person intentionally sold food that was purchased using benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the finding is that the person intentionally sold food that was purchased using benefits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(q), is the person ineligible for benefits` MEANS
    `s 2015(q) the person is ineligible for benefits` `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` `the finding is that the person intentionally sold food that was purchased using benefits`

-- s 2015(q): the period of ineligibility.
@export Under section 2015(q), what is the period of ineligibility?
GIVEN `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)?
      `the finding is that the person intentionally sold food that was purchased using benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the finding is that the person intentionally sold food that was purchased using benefits?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of ineligibility`
`Under section 2015(q), what is the period of ineligibility` MEANS
    `s 2015(q) the period of ineligibility` `the person was found by a State or Federal court or administrative agency in a hearing under subsection (b)` `the finding is that the person intentionally sold food that was purchased using benefits`

-- s 2015(r)(2): the individual is counted as a member of the household.
@export Under section 2015(r)(2), is the individual counted as a member of the household?
GIVEN `paragraph (1) applies to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that paragraph (1) applies to the individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(r)(2), is the individual counted as a member of the household` MEANS
    `s 2015(r)(2) the individual is counted as a member of the household` (JUST `paragraph (1) applies to the individual`)

-- s 2015(r)(2): the number of members of the household counted in determining the amount of benefits.
@export Under section 2015(r)(2), what is the number of members of the household counted in determining the amount of benefits?
GIVEN `the number of members of the household, counting the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of members of the household, counting the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies? (a number)
      `paragraph (1) applies to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that paragraph (1) applies to the individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2015(r)(2), what is the number of members of the household counted in determining the amount of benefits` MEANS
    `s 2015(r)(2) the number of members of the household counted in determining the amount of benefits` `the number of members of the household, counting the individual to whom paragraph (1) applies` (JUST `paragraph (1) applies to the individual`)

-- s 2015(r)(2): the income and resources of the individual are counted as income and resources of the household.
@export Under section 2015(r)(2), are the income and resources of the individual counted as income and resources of the household?
GIVEN `paragraph (1) applies to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that paragraph (1) applies to the individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(r)(2), are the income and resources of the individual counted as income and resources of the household` MEANS
    `s 2015(r)(2) the income and resources of the individual are counted as income and resources of the household` (JUST `paragraph (1) applies to the individual`)

-- s 2015(r)(3): the State is required to require the individual to attest to whether the individual or any member of the household has been convicted of a crime described in paragraph (1).
@export Under section 2015(r)(3), is the State required to require the individual to attest to whether the individual or any member of the household has been convicted of a crime described in paragraph (1)?
GIVEN `the individual is applying for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual is applying for benefits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(r)(3), is the State required to require the individual to attest to whether the individual or any member of the household has been convicted of a crime described in paragraph (1)` MEANS
    `s 2015(r)(3) the State is required to require the individual to attest to whether the individual or any member of the household has been convicted of a crime described in paragraph (1)` `the individual is applying for benefits`

-- s 2015(s)(1): the household loses eligibility for benefits upon receipt of the winnings.
@export Under section 2015(s)(1), does the household lose eligibility for benefits upon receipt of the winnings?
GIVEN `a member of the household received lottery or gambling winnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a member of the household received lottery or gambling winnings?
      `the Secretary has determined that the winnings are substantial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Secretary has determined that the winnings are substantial?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(s)(1), does the household lose eligibility for benefits upon receipt of the winnings` MEANS
    `s 2015(s)(1) the household loses eligibility for benefits upon receipt of the winnings` `a member of the household received lottery or gambling winnings` (JUST `the Secretary has determined that the winnings are substantial`)

-- s 2015(s)(2): the household remains ineligible for participation.
@export Under section 2015(s)(2), does the household remain ineligible for participation?
GIVEN `paragraph (1) applies to the household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that paragraph (1) applies to the household?
      `the household meets the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the household meets the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(s)(2), does the household remain ineligible for participation` MEANS
    `s 2015(s)(2) the household remains ineligible for participation` (JUST `paragraph (1) applies to the household`) (JUST `the household meets the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n)`)

-- s 2015(s): the household is ineligible on the date.
@export Under section 2015(s), is the household ineligible on the date?
GIVEN `a member of the household received lottery or gambling winnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a member of the household received lottery or gambling winnings?
      `the Secretary has determined that the winnings are substantial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Secretary has determined that the winnings are substantial?
      `the date the winnings were received` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the winnings were received? (a date)
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date asked about? (a date)
      `the household met the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n) between the receipt and the date asked about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the household met the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n) between the receipt and the date asked about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(s), is the household ineligible on the date` MEANS
    `s 2015(s) the household is ineligible on the date` `a member of the household received lottery or gambling winnings` (JUST `the Secretary has determined that the winnings are substantial`) `the date the winnings were received` `the date asked about` (JUST `the household met the allowable financial resources and income eligibility requirements under subsections (c), (d), (e), (f), (g), (i), (k), (l), (m), and (n) between the receipt and the date asked about`)

-- s 2015(r)(1): a convicted felon who is not in compliance.
@export Under section 2015(r)(1), am I ineligible for benefits as a convicted felon?
GIVEN `I have been convicted of an offense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of an offense?
      `it was aggravated sexual abuse under section 2241 of title 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it aggravated sexual abuse under section 2241 of title 18?
      `it was murder under section 1111 of title 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it murder under section 1111 of title 18?
      `it was an offense under chapter 110 of title 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it an offense under chapter 110 of title 18?
      `it was a Federal or State offense involving sexual assault, as defined in section 13925(a) of title 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a Federal or State offense involving sexual assault, as defined in section 13925(a) of title 42?
      `it was an offense under State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it an offense under State law?
      `the Attorney General has determined it is substantially similar to an offense described in clause (i), (ii), or (iii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Attorney General determined that your State offense is substantially similar to aggravated sexual abuse, murder, or an offense under chapter 110 of title 18?
      `I am in compliance with the terms of my sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in compliance with the terms of your sentence?
      `subsection (k) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the fleeing felons rule of subsection (k) apply to you (you are fleeing to avoid prosecution, custody or confinement, or you are violating a condition of probation or parole)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2015(r)(1), am I ineligible for benefits as a convicted felon` MEANS
    `s 2015(r)(1) the individual is ineligible for benefits` `I have been convicted of an offense` `my offense` `I am in compliance with the terms of my sentence` (JUST `subsection (k) applies to me`)
    WHERE
        `my offense` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `it was aggravated sexual abuse under section 2241 of title 18` THEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(i) aggravated sexual abuse under section 2241 of title 18`
                IF `it was murder under section 1111 of title 18` THEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(ii) murder under section 1111 of title 18`
                IF `it was an offense under chapter 110 of title 18` THEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(iii) an offense under chapter 110 of title 18`
                IF `it was a Federal or State offense involving sexual assault, as defined in section 13925(a) of title 42` THEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(iv) a Federal or State offense involving sexual assault, as defined in section 13925(a) of title 42`
                IF `it was an offense under State law` THEN `s 2015(r)(1)(A)(v) an offense under State law` OF (JUST `the Attorney General has determined it is substantially similar to an offense described in clause (i), (ii), or (iii)`)
                OTHERWISE `s 2015(r)(1)(A) some other offense`

§§ `Section 2027: appropriations and allotments`

-- s 2027(b): the Secretary is required to direct State agencies to reduce the value of the allotments to be issued.
@export Under section 2027(b), is the Secretary required to direct State agencies to reduce the value of the allotments to be issued?
GIVEN `the Secretary finds that the requirements of participating States will exceed the appropriation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Secretary finds that the requirements of participating States will exceed the appropriation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2027(b), is the Secretary required to direct State agencies to reduce the value of the allotments to be issued` MEANS
    `s 2027(b) the Secretary is required to direct State agencies to reduce the value of the allotments to be issued` (JUST `the Secretary finds that the requirements of participating States will exceed the appropriation`)

-- s 2027(b): the reduction in the value of the allotments to the extent necessary to comply with the subsection.
@export Under section 2027(b), what is the reduction in the value of the allotments to the extent necessary to comply with the subsection?
GIVEN `the requirements of participating States for the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the requirements of participating States for the fiscal year? (a number)
      `the appropriation for the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the appropriation for the fiscal year? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2027(b), what is the reduction in the value of the allotments to the extent necessary to comply with the subsection` MEANS
    `s 2027(b) the reduction in the value of the allotments to the extent necessary to comply with the subsection` `the requirements of participating States for the fiscal year` `the appropriation for the fiscal year`

-- s 2027(c): the ratio of household income to the income standard of eligibility.
@export Under section 2027(c), what is the ratio of household income to the income standard of eligibility?
GIVEN `the household income, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the household income, in dollars? (a number)
      `the income standard of eligibility for households of equal size, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the income standard of eligibility for households of equal size, in dollars? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2027(c), what is the ratio of household income to the income standard of eligibility` MEANS
    `s 2027(c) the ratio of household income to the income standard of eligibility` `the household income, in dollars` `the income standard of eligibility for households of equal size, in dollars`

-- s 2027(c)(1): the Secretary may establish special provisions applicable to the person in prescribing the manner of reducing allotments.
@export Under section 2027(c)(1), may the Secretary establish special provisions applicable to the person in prescribing the manner of reducing allotments?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in years?
      `the person is physically or mentally handicapped or otherwise disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is physically or mentally handicapped or otherwise disabled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2027(c)(1), may the Secretary establish special provisions applicable to the person in prescribing the manner of reducing allotments` MEANS
    `s 2027(c)(1) the Secretary may establish special provisions applicable to the person in prescribing the manner of reducing allotments` `me, as the person asked about` `the person is physically or mentally handicapped or otherwise disabled`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the rule above never reads the fields of the person that are not asked.
        `me, as the person asked about` MEANS Individual OF `my age in years`, TRUE, FALSE, `a citizen or national of the United States`, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE

-- s 2027(c)(2): the Secretary may establish minimum allotments after any reductions are otherwise determined.
@export Under section 2027(c)(2), may the Secretary establish minimum allotments after any reductions are otherwise determined?
GIVEN `the Secretary is prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Secretary is prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2027(c)(2), may the Secretary establish minimum allotments after any reductions are otherwise determined` MEANS
    `s 2027(c)(2) the Secretary may establish minimum allotments after any reductions are otherwise determined` `the Secretary is prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced`

§§ `Section 2029: workfare`

-- s 2029(a)(1): the member is required to accept an offer from the subdivision to perform work.
@export Under section 2029(a)(1), is the member required to accept an offer from the subdivision to perform work?
GIVEN `the member participates in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of a household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the member participates in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of a household?
      `the subdivision operates a workfare program under this section for the household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the subdivision operates a workfare program under this section for the household?
      `the household member is exempt from workfare requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the household member is exempt from workfare requirements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2029(a)(1), is the member required to accept an offer from the subdivision to perform work` MEANS
    `s 2029(a)(1) the member is required to accept an offer from the subdivision to perform work` `the member participates in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of a household` `the subdivision operates a workfare program under this section for the household` (JUST `the household member is exempt from workfare requirements`)

-- s 2029(a)(1): the portion of the allotment the household is entitled to for the hours of work.
@export Under section 2029(a)(1), what is the portion of the allotment the household is entitled to for the hours of work?
GIVEN `the hours of work` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hours of work? (a number)
      `the applicable State minimum wage per hour` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the applicable State minimum wage per hour? (a number)
      `the Federal minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 per hour` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Federal minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 per hour? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2029(a)(1), what is the portion of the allotment the household is entitled to for the hours of work` MEANS
    `s 2029(a)(1) the portion of the allotment the household is entitled to for the hours of work` `the hours of work` `the applicable State minimum wage per hour` `the Federal minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 per hour`

-- s 2029(b): the household member is exempt from workfare requirements.
@export Under section 2029(b), is the household member exempt from workfare requirements?
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in years?
      `I am physically and mentally fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you physically and mentally fit for work?
      `the person is exempt from section 2015(d)(1) as the result of clause (B), (C), (D), (E), or (F)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is exempt from section 2015(d)(1) as the result of clause (B), (C), (D), (E), or (F)?
      `the operating agency has opted to exempt a member in a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the operating agency has opted to exempt a member in a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act?
      `the member is subject to a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the member is subject to a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act?
      `the member is currently actively and satisfactorily participating in the work activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the member is currently actively and satisfactorily participating in the work activity?
      `hours a week the member participates in the work activity` IS A NUMBER @desc Give the number: hours a week the member participates in the work activity.
      `the member is a parent or other caretaker of a child in the household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the member is a parent or other caretaker of a child in the household?
      `another member of the household is subject to the requirements of this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that another member of the household is subject to the requirements of this section?
      `another member of the household is employed fulltime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that another member of the household is employed fulltime?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2029(b), is the household member exempt from workfare requirements` MEANS
    `s 2029(b) the household member is exempt from workfare requirements` `me, as the person asked about` (JUST `the person is exempt from section 2015(d)(1) as the result of clause (B), (C), (D), (E), or (F)`) `the operating agency has opted to exempt a member in a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act` `the member is subject to a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act` `the member is currently actively and satisfactorily participating in the work activity` `hours a week the member participates in the work activity` `the member is a parent or other caretaker of a child in the household` `another member of the household is subject to the requirements of this section` `another member of the household is employed fulltime`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the rule above never reads the fields of the person that are not asked.
        `me, as the person asked about` MEANS Individual OF `my age in years`, `I am physically and mentally fit`, FALSE, `a citizen or national of the United States`, TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE

-- s 2029(c): the operating agency may require the work.
@export Under section 2029(c), may the operating agency require the work?
GIVEN `the value of the work the participating member is required to do, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the work the participating member is required to do, in dollars? (a number)
      `the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars? (a number)
      `the hours of work the member is required to do in the workfare position that week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the hours of work the member is required to do in the workfare position that week? (a number)
      `the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2029(c), may the operating agency require the work` MEANS
    `s 2029(c) the operating agency may require the work` `the value of the work the participating member is required to do, in dollars` `the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars` `the hours of work the member is required to do in the workfare position that week` `the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity`

-- s 2029(c): the most hours of workfare work the agency may require of the member that week.
@export Under section 2029(c), what is the most hours of workfare work the agency may require of the member that week?
GIVEN `the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity? (a number)
      `the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars? (a number)
      `the value of an hour of work, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of an hour of work, in dollars? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2029(c), what is the most hours of workfare work the agency may require of the member that week` MEANS
    `s 2029(c) the most hours of workfare work the agency may require of the member that week` `the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity` `the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars` `the value of an hour of work, in dollars`

-- s 2029(d)(1): the operating agency may provide the work.
@export Under section 2029(d)(1), may the operating agency provide the work?
GIVEN `the work has the effect of replacing or preventing the employment of an individual not participating in the workfare program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the work has the effect of replacing or preventing the employment of an individual not participating in the workfare program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2029(d)(1), may the operating agency provide the work` MEANS
    `s 2029(d)(1) the operating agency may provide the work` `the work has the effect of replacing or preventing the employment of an individual not participating in the workfare program`

-- s 2029(d)(2): the operating agency is required to provide the same benefits and working conditions that are provided at the job site.
@export Under section 2029(d)(2), is the operating agency required to provide the same benefits and working conditions that are provided at the job site?
GIVEN `the participant performs work comparable to the work of employees at the job site, for comparable hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the participant performs work comparable to the work of employees at the job site, for comparable hours?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2029(d)(2), is the operating agency required to provide the same benefits and working conditions that are provided at the job site` MEANS
    `s 2029(d)(2) the operating agency is required to provide the same benefits and working conditions that are provided at the job site` `the participant performs work comparable to the work of employees at the job site, for comparable hours`

-- s 2029(d)(3): the amount the operating agency is required to reimburse for the month.
@export Under section 2029(d)(3), what is the amount the operating agency is required to reimburse for the month?
GIVEN `the participant's actual costs of transportation and other actual costs, reasonably necessary and directly related to participation, in the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the participant's actual costs of transportation and other actual costs, reasonably necessary and directly related to participation, in the month? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under section 2029(d)(3), what is the amount the operating agency is required to reimburse for the month` MEANS
    `s 2029(d)(3) the amount the operating agency is required to reimburse for the month` `the participant's actual costs of transportation and other actual costs, reasonably necessary and directly related to participation, in the month`

-- s 2029(e): the operating agency may allow a job search period of the length, prior to making workfare assignments.
@export Under section 2029(e), may the operating agency allow a job search period of the length, prior to making workfare assignments?
GIVEN `the length of the job search period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the length of the job search period in days? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2029(e), may the operating agency allow a job search period of the length, prior to making workfare assignments` MEANS
    `s 2029(e) the operating agency may allow a job search period of the length, prior to making workfare assignments` `the length of the job search period in days`

-- s 2029(e): the last day of the longest job search period.
@export Under section 2029(e), what is the last day of the longest job search period?
GIVEN `the date of the determination of eligibility` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the determination of eligibility? (a date)
GIVETH A DATE
`Under section 2029(e), what is the last day of the longest job search period` MEANS
    `s 2029(e) the last day of the longest job search period` `the date of the determination of eligibility`

-- s 2029(f): the individual or household may become ineligible under section 2015(d)(1) for failing to comply with this section.
@export Under section 2029(f), may the individual or household become ineligible under section 2015(d)(1) for failing to comply with this section?
GIVEN `the individual or household failed to comply with this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the individual or household failed to comply with this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under section 2029(f), may the individual or household become ineligible under section 2015(d)(1) for failing to comply with this section` MEANS
    `s 2029(f) the individual or household may become ineligible under section 2015(d)(1) for failing to comply with this section` `the individual or household failed to comply with this section`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part snap3 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (United States, 7 U.S.C. ch. 51), sections 2016, 2016a, 2017, 2022, 2023 and 2024 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- Source: a converter's plain-text rendering of the OLRC text, not the official text. Nothing here is "verified against the official text".
--
-- SEAT: a member of a household that applies for, or receives, benefits under the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP).
--
-- This layer asks the questions that person would ask about the parts of the Act encoded in the snap3 modules: how their benefits may be used and delivered,
-- what happens when their EBT benefits are stolen, what their monthly allotment is worth, what the State may take back if they were overpaid, how far back wrongly withheld allotments are restored,
-- and what follows from misusing benefits. Nothing here is new law: every question calls a layer-1 rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no, number, date or choice answers, one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- Judgments the Act hands to someone else (what the Secretary determines, what the State agency decides) are not asked as law: the person states the fact ("Did the State agency decide the benefits were stolen?").
-- A SEAT PRESUMPTION: the person is a member of a household and the benefits are SNAP benefits administered by a State agency, so the section 2012 answers the rules ask
-- (s 2012(d) benefit, s 2012(m) household, s 2012(s) State agency, s 2012(g) food) are passed as "yes" where the question concerns this person's own household and benefits. The person states whether the thing bought is food.
--
-- WHAT EACH ANSWER MEANS. JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not say (silent, list not closed, points outside the text, or limited by its own wording).
-- A NOTHING is never a "no": see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (snap3)".
--
-- NOT IN THIS LAYER: section 2023(a) (a store, wholesale food concern or State agency asking for administrative and judicial review) and the duties and powers that lie only between the Secretary, the State agencies,
-- banks and retail food stores (the rest of section 2016(h), (j) and (k); section 2022(a)). They are in layer 1. A household member is not a party to them.

§ `Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 -- the household member's questions`

§§ `Under section 2016 -- issuance and use of my benefits`

-- s 2016(a), (i). An EBT card is the plastic card on which SNAP benefits are loaded. Subsection (a) lets a State issue one only to a household that has been duly certified as eligible; subsection (i) is a State option for people made ineligible only by certain welfare-reform rules.
@export Under section 2016(a), may an EBT card be issued to my household?
GIVEN `my household has been duly certified as eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your household been duly certified as eligible to take part in SNAP?
      `the card is issued under the State option in subsection (i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the card being issued under the State option for people made ineligible only by certain welfare-reform rules (subsection (i))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(a), may an EBT card be issued to my household` IS
    `s 2016(a) an EBT card may be issued to the household` (JUST `my household has been duly certified as eligible`) `the card is issued under the State option in subsection (i)`

-- s 2016(b). Benefits may be used only to buy food, from a retail food store approved for SNAP, at the store's prevailing prices.
@export Under section 2016(b), may I use my benefits for this purchase?
GIVEN `what I am buying is food` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you are buying food?
      `the store is approved for SNAP` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the retail food store one that has been approved to take part in SNAP?
      `I am paying the store's usual price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paying the price the store charges everyone for it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(b), may I use my benefits for this purchase` IS
    `s 2016(b) the household may use the benefits for the purchase` (JUST `what I am buying is food`) (JUST `the store is approved for SNAP`) `I am paying the store's usual price`

-- s 2016(k)(2)(B). When you order food online, benefits cannot pay delivery, ordering, convenience or other fees or charges.
@export Under section 2016(k)(2)(B), may I use my benefits to pay a fee on an online food order?
GIVEN `the charge is a delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fee or charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge a delivery, ordering, convenience or other fee or charge (rather than the price of the food)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(k)(2)(B), may I use my benefits to pay a fee on an online food order` IS
    `s 2016(k)(2)(B) the benefits may be used to pay the charge` `the charge is a delivery, ordering, convenience, or other fee or charge`

-- s 2016(g)(2)(A)(ii). If your State staggers issuance through the month, no household may wait more than 40 days between issuances.
@export Under section 2016(g)(2)(A)(ii), is the wait between my issuances within the 40-day limit?
GIVEN `the number of days between two issuances to my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days were there between the two issuances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(g)(2)(A)(ii), is the wait between my issuances within the 40-day limit` IS
    `s 2016(g)(2)(A)(ii) the interval between issuances meets the requirement` `the number of days between two issuances to my household`

-- s 2016(h)(8)(A). A State agency may charge for a replacement EBT card by reducing the monthly allotment of the household that gets it.
@export Under section 2016(h)(8)(A), may my State agency charge me for a replacement EBT card by reducing my monthly allotment?
GIVEN `the card is a replacement for a lost or damaged EBT card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the card a replacement for one that was lost or damaged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(h)(8)(A), may my State agency charge me for a replacement card by reducing my allotment` IS
    `s 2016(h)(8)(A) the State agency may collect a charge by reducing the monthly allotment of the household receiving the replacement card` `the card is a replacement for a lost or damaged EBT card`

-- s 2016(h)(8)(B)(i). If a household asks for replacement cards excessively, the Secretary may require the State agency to refuse another one, unless the household explains the losses when asked.
@export Under section 2016(h)(8)(B)(i), may the State agency be required to refuse me another replacement card?
GIVEN `my household has asked for replacement cards excessively` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your household asked for replacement EBT cards an excessive number of times?
      `I gave an explanation when the State agency asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the State agency asked, did your household explain why the cards were lost?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(h)(8)(B)(i), may the State agency be required to refuse me another replacement card` IS
    `s 2016(h)(8)(B)(i) the Secretary may require the State agency to decline to issue a replacement card to the household` `my household has asked for replacement cards excessively` `I gave an explanation when the State agency asked`

-- s 2016(h)(8)(D). A State may hold back a replacement card until you satisfy the requirements, but that is not a denial of your eligibility.
@export Under section 2016(h)(8)(D), does being refused a replacement card count as a denial of my eligibility for benefits?
GIVEN `the State agency is holding back my replacement card until my household satisfies the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the State agency holding back your replacement EBT card until your household meets the card-replacement requirements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(h)(8)(D), does being refused a replacement card count as a denial of my eligibility` IS
    `s 2016(h)(8) declining to issue the card is a denial of, or a limitation on, the eligibility for benefits under section 2014` `the State agency is holding back my replacement card until my household satisfies the requirements`

-- s 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(II). Benefits stored off-line because of inactivity must be made available within 48 hours of your request.
@export Under section 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(II), did the State agency make my stored benefits available in time?
GIVEN `the number of hours between my request and the moment the benefits were made available` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours passed between your request for your stored benefits and the moment they were made available to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(II), did the State agency make my stored benefits available in time` IS
    `s 2016(h)(12)(B)(ii)(II) the State agency made the stored benefits available in time` `the number of hours between my request and the moment the benefits were made available`

-- s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I). Before benefits that have sat unused are expunged, the State agency must give sufficient notice, not later than 30 days before the expunging date.
@export Under section 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I), was my notice that my unused benefits would be expunged given in time?
GIVEN `the notice said the benefits will be expunged due to inactivity and gave the date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the notice say that your benefits will be expunged because the account was inactive, and give the date on which they will be expunged?
      `the date I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the State agency give you the notice?
      `the date my benefits are to be expunged` IS A DATE @desc On what date are your benefits to be expunged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I), was my notice that my unused benefits would be expunged given in time` IS
    `s 2016(h)(12)(C)(ii)(I) the State agency gave sufficient notice in time` `the notice said the benefits will be expunged due to inactivity and gave the date` `the date I received the notice` `the date my benefits are to be expunged`

-- s 2016(h)(13)(A). No interchange fee applies to an EBT transaction.
@export Under section 2016(h)(13)(A), does an interchange fee apply to my EBT transaction?
GIVEN `the transaction is an electronic benefit transfer transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction an EBT (electronic benefit transfer) transaction using your SNAP benefits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(h)(13)(A), does an interchange fee apply to my EBT transaction` IS
    `s 2016(h)(13)(A) an interchange fee applies to the transaction` `the transaction is an electronic benefit transfer transaction`

-- s 2016(h)(13)(B). Through fiscal year 2023 a State, or its agent, contractor or subcontractor, could not impose a fee for switching or routing SNAP benefits.
@export Under section 2016(h)(13)(B), may a State or its contractor charge a fee for switching or routing my benefits?
GIVEN `the date the fee is charged` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the fee charged?
      `the fee is for switching or routing my benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fee for switching or routing your SNAP benefits?
      `the fee is charged by a State or by its agent, contractor or subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fee charged by a State, or by an agent, contractor or subcontractor of a State that helps provide SNAP benefits there?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(h)(13)(B), may a State or its contractor charge a fee for switching or routing my benefits` IS
    `s 2016(h)(13)(B) the person may impose the fee` `the date the fee is charged` `the fee is for switching or routing my benefits` `the fee is charged by a State or by its agent, contractor or subcontractor`

-- s 2016(i)(1). A State may, with the Secretary's approval, give benefits to a person made ineligible only by section 2015(o)(2) or sections 1612 or 1613 of title 8.
@export Under section 2016(i)(1), may my State issue me benefits although I am ineligible for the reason the subsection names?
GIVEN `I am ineligible only because of section 2015(o)(2) or section 1612 or 1613 of title 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason you are ineligible for SNAP section 2015(o)(2) (the rule on certain people with drug felony convictions or work rules, as the State agency tells you) or sections 1612 or 1613 of title 8 (the rules on non-citizens)?
      `the State has the Secretary's approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your State got the Secretary of Agriculture's approval to issue benefits to such people?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016(i)(1), may my State issue me benefits although I am ineligible for the reason the subsection names` IS
    `s 2016(i)(1) the State agency may issue benefits under this chapter to the individual` `I am ineligible only because of section 2015(o)(2) or section 1612 or 1613 of title 8` `the State has the Secretary's approval`

§§ `Under section 2016a -- EBT benefits stolen by card skimming or cloning`

-- s 2016a(b). If your State agency decides benefits were stolen from your EBT account by card skimming, card cloning or a similar method, benefits stolen from 1 October 2022 to 20 December 2024 are replaced, up to the lesser of the amount stolen and two months of your allotment, at most twice per fiscal year.
@export Under section 2016a(b)(2), up to how many dollars of my stolen benefits must be replaced?
GIVEN `the State agency decided the benefits were stolen by card skimming, card cloning or a similar method` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your State agency decide that the benefits were stolen by card skimming, card cloning or a similar fraudulent method?
      `the date the benefits were stolen` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the benefits stolen?
      `the amount stolen` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dollars of benefits were stolen from your household?
      `my monthly allotment just before the theft` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your household's monthly allotment, in dollars, just before the day the benefits were stolen?
      `replacements already made this fiscal year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times has your State agency already replaced stolen benefits for your household in this Federal fiscal year (1 October to 30 September)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2016a(b)(2), up to how many dollars of my stolen benefits must be replaced` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST `the State agency decided the benefits were stolen by card skimming, card cloning or a similar method`) `the date the benefits were stolen` `the amount stolen` `my monthly allotment just before the theft` `replacements already made this fiscal year`
        WHEN `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` most THEN JUST most
        WHEN `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say` THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 2016a(b)(2), does the text rule out replacing my stolen benefits?
GIVEN `the State agency decided the benefits were stolen by card skimming, card cloning or a similar method` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your State agency decide that the benefits were stolen by card skimming, card cloning or a similar fraudulent method?
      `the date the benefits were stolen` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the benefits stolen?
      `the amount stolen` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dollars of benefits were stolen from your household?
      `my monthly allotment just before the theft` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your household's monthly allotment, in dollars, just before the day the benefits were stolen?
      `replacements already made this fiscal year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times has your State agency already replaced stolen benefits for your household in this Federal fiscal year (1 October to 30 September)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2016a(b)(2), does the text rule out replacing my stolen benefits` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement of the stolen benefits` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST `the State agency decided the benefits were stolen by card skimming, card cloning or a similar method`) `the date the benefits were stolen` `the amount stolen` `my monthly allotment just before the theft` `replacements already made this fiscal year`
        WHEN `s 2016a(b)(2) the replacement is required up to an amount` most THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `s 2016a(b)(2) the text says no replacement under this section` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 2016a(b)(2) the text does not say` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Under section 2017 -- the value of my allotment`

-- s 2017(a). The allotment is the cost of the thrifty food plan for your household size, less 30 per cent of your net income, rounded down to a whole dollar; one- and two-person households get at least the minimum allotment.
-- The cost of the thrifty food plan is the Secretary's figure; this question takes the maximum monthly allotment the USDA published for fiscal year 2027 (1 October 2026 to 30 September 2027) as that cost.
@export Under section 2017(a), what is my household's monthly allotment, fiscal year 2027?
GIVEN `my household has been certified as eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your household been certified as eligible for SNAP?
      `the number of people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your household?
      `where my household lives` IS AN Area @desc Where does your household live? (the 48 States and the District of Columbia, Alaska urban, Alaska rural 1, Alaska rural 2, Guam, Hawaii, or the Virgin Islands)
      `my household's net monthly income` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your household's monthly income, in dollars, after the deductions section 2014(d) and (e) allows?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2017(a), what is my household's monthly allotment, fiscal year 2027` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2017 the maximum monthly allotment, fiscal year 2027` `the number of people in my household` `where my household lives`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST cost THEN
            `s 2017(a) the value of the allotment` `my household has been certified as eligible` `the number of people in my household` cost `my household's net monthly income`
                (`s 2017 the figure for the area` `s 2017 the minimum monthly allotment for a household of 1 or 2, fiscal year 2027` `where my household lives`)

-- s 2017(b). Benefits are not income or resources for any purpose under Federal, State or local law, and no State or local body may cut other assistance because you receive them.
@export Under section 2017(b), may a State or local body reduce other assistance I get because I receive SNAP benefits?
GIVEN `the body is a participating State or political subdivision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body that would reduce the help a State or a local government of a participating State?
      `the help is assistance otherwise provided to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the help one that would otherwise be provided to you or your household?
      `the reduction is because I receive benefits under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the reduction be because you receive SNAP benefits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2017(b), may a State or local body reduce other assistance I get because I receive SNAP benefits` IS
    `s 2017(b) the participating State or political subdivision may decrease the assistance` `the body is a participating State or political subdivision` `the help is assistance otherwise provided to me` `the reduction is because I receive benefits under this chapter`

-- s 2017(c)(1). The first month's allotment is prorated by the days left in the month from the date you applied; nothing is issued if that comes to less than $10.
@export Under section 2017(c)(1), what is the value of my first-month allotment?
GIVEN `my allotment for a full month` IS A NUMBER @desc What would your allotment be for a full month, in dollars?
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply?
      `the first day of the month` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the month (or other initial period) for which the allotment is issued?
      `the last day of the month` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that month (or other initial period)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2017(c)(1), what is the value of my first-month allotment` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2017(c)(1) the initial allotment` `my allotment for a full month` `the date I applied` `the first day of the month` `the last day of the month`
        WHEN `s 2017(c)(1) an allotment of` value THEN JUST value
        WHEN `s 2017(c)(1) no allotment may be issued` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `s 2017(c)(1) not covered` THEN NOTHING

@export Under section 2017(c)(1), is my first-month allotment barred because it would be less than $10?
GIVEN `my allotment for a full month` IS A NUMBER @desc What would your allotment be for a full month, in dollars?
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply?
      `the first day of the month` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the month (or other initial period) for which the allotment is issued?
      `the last day of the month` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that month (or other initial period)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2017(c)(1), is my first-month allotment barred because it would be less than $10` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2017(c)(1) the initial allotment` `my allotment for a full month` `the date I applied` `the first day of the month` `the last day of the month`
        WHEN `s 2017(c)(1) an allotment of` value THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `s 2017(c)(1) no allotment may be issued` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 2017(c)(1) not covered` THEN NOTHING

-- s 2017(d)(1)(B). If your benefits under another means-tested public assistance programme are cut because a household member failed to perform a required action, the State may cut your SNAP allotment by no more than 25 percent while the cut lasts.
@export Under section 2017(d)(1)(B), what is the most my State may cut my SNAP allotment because another programme cut my benefits?
GIVEN `another programme has reduced my household's benefits for a member's failure to perform an action it requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a Federal, State or local means-tested public assistance programme reduced your household's benefits because a member failed to do something the programme requires?
      `my household's allotment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your household's SNAP allotment, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2017(d)(1)(B), what is the most my State may cut my SNAP allotment because another programme cut my benefits` IS
    `s 2017(d)(1)(B) the greatest reduction of the allotment` `another programme has reduced my household's benefits for a member's failure to perform an action it requires` `my household's allotment`

§§ `Under section 2022 -- claims for overissued benefits`

-- s 2022(a)(4). Each adult member of the household is liable, jointly and severally, for the value of any overissuance.
@export Under section 2022(a)(4), am I jointly and severally liable for the value of an overissuance to my household?
GIVEN `I am an adult member of my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an adult member of the household?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2022(a)(4), am I jointly and severally liable for the value of an overissuance to my household` IS
    `s 2022(a)(4) the member is jointly and severally liable for the value of the overissuance` (JUST TRUE) `I am an adult member of my household`

-- s 2022(b)(3). If no member of the household was found ineligible for fraud and the State chooses to collect by cutting your allotment, it may cut no more than the greater of 10 percent of the monthly allotment and $10 a month.
@export Under section 2022(b)(3), what is the most my State may cut my monthly allotment each month to collect an overissuance?
GIVEN `a member of my household has been found ineligible for fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any member of your household been found ineligible to take part in SNAP under section 2015(b)(1) (a fraud disqualification)?
      `the State is collecting by cutting my allotment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the State collecting the overissuance by reducing your household's allotment?
      `my monthly allotment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your household's monthly allotment, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2022(b)(3), what is the most my State may cut my monthly allotment each month to collect an overissuance` IS
    `s 2022(b)(3) the greatest reduction of the monthly allotment` `a member of my household has been found ineligible for fraud` `the State is collecting by cutting my allotment` `my monthly allotment`

@export Under section 2022(b)(3), may my State cut my monthly allotment by this amount to collect an overissuance?
GIVEN `a member of my household has been found ineligible for fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any member of your household been found ineligible to take part in SNAP under section 2015(b)(1) (a fraud disqualification)?
      `the State is collecting by cutting my allotment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the State collecting the overissuance by reducing your household's allotment?
      `my monthly allotment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your household's monthly allotment, in dollars?
      `the cut each month` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dollars a month does the State want to cut?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2022(b)(3), may my State cut my monthly allotment by this amount to collect an overissuance` IS
    `s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount` `a member of my household has been found ineligible for fraud` `the State is collecting by cutting my allotment` `my monthly allotment` `the cut each month`

-- s 2022(c)(3). A State agency may recover an uncollected overissuance from an individual's unemployment compensation by an agreement, or, without one, by a court's garnishment process.
@export Under section 2022(c)(3), may my State recover an uncollected overissuance from my unemployment compensation?
GIVEN `I am receiving compensation under a State unemployment compensation law and the State agency checked whether I owe an overissuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving unemployment compensation, and has the State agency checked whether you owe an uncollected overissuance?
      `I agreed to have specified amounts withheld from my unemployment compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you agreed to have specified amounts withheld from your unemployment compensation?
      `a copy of the agreement went to the agency that pays unemployment compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a copy of that agreement been given to the agency that pays your unemployment compensation?
      `a court has issued a garnishment order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court of competent jurisdiction issued a writ, order, summons or similar garnishment process requiring the withholding?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2022(c)(3), may my State recover an uncollected overissuance from my unemployment compensation` IS
    `s 2022(c)(3) the State agency may recover the uncollected overissuance` `I am receiving compensation under a State unemployment compensation law and the State agency checked whether I owe an overissuance` `I agreed to have specified amounts withheld from my unemployment compensation` `a copy of the agreement went to the agency that pays unemployment compensation` `a court has issued a garnishment order`

-- s 2022(d). An overissuance not recovered under subsection (b)(1) may be recovered from Federal pay or a Federal income tax refund, as the other statutes authorize.
@export Under section 2022(d), may an unrecovered overissuance be recovered from my Federal income tax refund?
GIVEN `the amount of the overissuance not yet recovered` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dollars of the overissuance have not been recovered?
      `section 3720A of title 31 authorizes the recovery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 3720A of title 31 (the tax-refund offset law) authorize the recovery in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2022(d), may an unrecovered overissuance be recovered from my Federal income tax refund` IS
    `s 2022(d) the uncollected overissuance may be recovered from the source` `the amount of the overissuance not yet recovered` `s 2022(d) a Federal income tax refund` `section 3720A of title 31 authorizes the recovery`

§§ `Under section 2023 -- restoring allotments wrongly withheld`

-- s 2023(b). In a court case under the Act, allotments found wrongfully withheld are restored only for periods of up to a year before the case began, or before you asked the State for restoration (if the case reviews a final State decision), or before the State found out about the loss.
-- The text joins the three limits with "or"; this question reads them as alternatives, so restoration reaches back as far as the earliest limit that applies (NOTES.md, fork F-2023-1).
@export Under section 2023(b), what is the earliest date from which my wrongly withheld allotments can be restored?
GIVEN `the date the court case began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the court case begin?
      `the case reviews a final State agency decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case a review of a final decision of the State agency?
      `I asked the State for restoration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the State agency to restore the allotments?
      `the date I asked the State` IS A DATE @desc If you asked, on what date? (any date if you did not)
      `the State knew of the loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the State agency notified of, or did it discover, the possible loss?
      `the date the State knew` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (any date if not)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 2023(b), what is the earliest date from which my wrongly withheld allotments can be restored` IS
    `s 2023(b) the earliest date from which allotments may be restored` `the date the court case began` `the case reviews a final State agency decision` `my request date` `the date the State knew, if it did`
    WHERE
        `my request date` MEANS IF `I asked the State for restoration` THEN JUST `the date I asked the State` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the State knew, if it did` MEANS IF `the State knew of the loss` THEN JUST `the date the State knew` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 2023(b), can allotments be restored for a period starting on this date?
GIVEN `the date the court case began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the court case begin?
      `the case reviews a final State agency decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case a review of a final decision of the State agency?
      `I asked the State for restoration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the State agency to restore the allotments?
      `the date I asked the State` IS A DATE @desc If you asked, on what date? (any date if you did not)
      `the State knew of the loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the State agency notified of, or did it discover, the possible loss?
      `the date the State knew` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (any date if not)
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period for which you want allotments restored?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2023(b), can allotments be restored for a period starting on this date` IS
    `s 2023(b) the allotments may be restored for the period` `the date the court case began` `the case reviews a final State agency decision` `my request date` `the date the State knew, if it did` `the first day of the period`
    WHERE
        `my request date` MEANS IF `I asked the State for restoration` THEN JUST `the date I asked the State` ELSE NOTHING
        `the date the State knew, if it did` MEANS IF `the State knew of the loss` THEN JUST `the date the State knew` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Under section 2024 -- what follows from misusing benefits`

-- s 2024(b)(1). Knowingly using, transferring, acquiring, altering or possessing benefits contrary to the Act is a felony if the benefits are worth $100 or more and a misdemeanor if less.
@export Under section 2024(b)(1), is knowingly misusing benefits of this value a felony?
GIVEN `the value of the benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the benefits, in dollars?
      `this would be my second or a later conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would this be your second or a later conviction under this subsection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2024(b)(1), is knowingly misusing benefits of this value a felony` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2024(b)(1) the punishment for the offence` `the value of the benefits` `this would be my second or a later conviction`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 2024 the grade of the offence` EQUALS `s 2024 a felony`)

@export Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the most the fine may be for knowingly misusing benefits of this value?
GIVEN `the value of the benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the benefits, in dollars?
      `this would be my second or a later conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would this be your second or a later conviction under this subsection?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the most the fine may be for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2024(b)(1) the punishment for the offence` `the value of the benefits` `this would be my second or a later conviction`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 2024 the most the fine may be, in dollars`)

@export Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the longest prison term, in years, for knowingly misusing benefits of this value?
GIVEN `the value of the benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the benefits, in dollars?
      `this would be my second or a later conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would this be your second or a later conviction under this subsection?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the longest prison term, in years, for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2024(b)(1) the punishment for the offence` `the value of the benefits` `this would be my second or a later conviction`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 2024 the most term of imprisonment, in years`)

@export Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the shortest prison term, in years, the court must impose for knowingly misusing benefits of this value?
GIVEN `the value of the benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the benefits, in dollars?
      `this would be my second or a later conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would this be your second or a later conviction under this subsection?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2024(b)(1), what is the shortest prison term, in years, the court must impose for knowingly misusing benefits of this value` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2024(b)(1) the punishment for the offence` `the value of the benefits` `this would be my second or a later conviction`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 2024 the least term of imprisonment, in years`)

@export Under section 2024(b)(1), may the court also suspend me from SNAP for this many more months?
GIVEN `I have been convicted of a felony or misdemeanor under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of a felony or misdemeanor under section 2024(b)?
      `the number of extra months of suspension` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many extra months, after the suspension section 2015(b)(1) requires, is the court asked to suspend you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2024(b)(1), may the court also suspend me from SNAP for this many more months` IS
    `s 2024(b)(1) the court may suspend the person for the additional period` `I have been convicted of a felony or misdemeanor under this subsection` `the number of extra months of suspension`

-- s 2024(b)(2). A person convicted under (b)(1) may be allowed by the court to do approved work as restitution; if the court allows it and you agree, the court withholds sentence on that condition.
@export Under section 2024(b)(2), may the court let me do work for restitution instead of being sentenced now?
GIVEN `I have been convicted of an offense under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been convicted of an offense under section 2024(b)(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2024(b)(2), may the court let me do work for restitution instead of being sentenced now` IS
    `s 2024(b)(2) the court may permit the individual to perform work approved by the court for restitution` `I have been convicted of an offense under paragraph (1)`

-- s 2024(c). Presenting benefits for payment or redemption, knowing they were received, transferred or used in violation, is a felony if $100 or more and a misdemeanor if less.
@export Under section 2024(c), is knowingly presenting benefits for redemption in violation of the Act, worth this much, a felony?
GIVEN `the value of the benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the benefits presented, in dollars?
      `this would be my second or a later conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would this be your second or a later conviction under this subsection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2024(c), is knowingly presenting benefits for redemption in violation of the Act, worth this much, a felony` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2024(c) the punishment for the offence` `the value of the benefits` `this would be my second or a later conviction`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 2024 the grade of the offence` EQUALS `s 2024 a felony`)

@export Under section 2024(c), what is the most the fine may be for presenting benefits of this value for redemption in violation of the Act?
GIVEN `the value of the benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the benefits presented, in dollars?
      `this would be my second or a later conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would this be your second or a later conviction under this subsection?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2024(c), what is the most the fine may be for presenting benefits of this value for redemption in violation of the Act` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2024(c) the punishment for the offence` `the value of the benefits` `this would be my second or a later conviction`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST p THEN JUST (p's `s 2024 the most the fine may be, in dollars`)

-- s 2024(e). The Secretary may subject to forfeiture nonfood items, money and other things of value furnished in exchange for benefits, or obtained by use of an access device, contrary to the Act.
@export Under section 2024(e), may the Secretary subject to forfeiture what was given in exchange for benefits?
GIVEN `it was furnished by a person in exchange for benefits, or obtained by use of an access device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing furnished by a person in exchange for benefits, or obtained by use of an access device (such as an EBT card)?
      `this was done in a manner contrary to the chapter or its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done in a manner contrary to the Act or its regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2024(e), may the Secretary subject to forfeiture what was given in exchange for benefits` IS
    `s 2024(e) the Secretary may subject the property to forfeiture and denial of property rights` `it was furnished by a person in exchange for benefits, or obtained by use of an access device` `this was done in a manner contrary to the chapter or its regulations`

-- s 2024(f)(3). No interest in property is forfeited as the result of an act or omission that the owner of the interest shows was done or omitted without the owner's knowledge or consent.
@export Under section 2024(f)(3), can my interest in property be forfeited for an act I did not know about or agree to?
GIVEN `I can show the act or omission was committed or omitted without my knowledge or consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that the act or omission was committed or omitted without your knowledge or consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2024(f)(3), can my interest in property be forfeited for an act I did not know about or agree to` IS
    `s 2024(f)(3) the interest of the owner in the property may be forfeited as the result of the act or omission` `I can show the act or omission was committed or omitted without my knowledge or consent`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part snap4 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (United States, 7 U.S.C. ch. 51, the SNAP statute) -- THE SEAT LAYER for snap4 (sections 2020 and 2021).
--
-- SEAT: a member of a household that applies for, or receives, SNAP benefits.
--
-- This layer phrases rules already encoded in snap4-s2020-a-d.l4, snap4-s2020-e-1.l4, snap4-s2020-o-x.l4 and snap4-s2021.l4
-- as questions that person would ask about their own case: who runs the program for me, what the State agency must do for me and by when,
-- whether it may share what I told it, what I can get while a hearing is pending, what transitional benefits I can get.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds the module's inputs from plain answers and calls the module's rule.
--
-- Not in this layer, by design: sections 2032, 2036b, 2036c and 2036d, and the rest of section 2020 (subsections (e)(12) to (e)(26) and (f) to (r), (t) to (x)).
-- They put duties on the State agencies, on the Secretary or on grantees, and say nothing a household member can ask about their own case.
-- Section 2021 binds stores and wholesale concerns: only its first rule (a store that breaks the rules can be barred from accepting benefits) is asked here.
--
-- READING AN ANSWER. Every question that returns a MAYBE BOOLEAN answers JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words)
-- or NOTHING (the text does not say, or the case is outside what it covers). NOTHING is never a "no".
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs: yes/no, numbers, dates, and the modules' own choices (a ground of discrimination, a basis of operation, a purpose).
-- Where a module takes an answer that the Secretary or another section gives (for example whether a body is a State agency), this layer states the fact the question assumes.
-- The Secretary's regulations and determinations that a module asks for are asked as "Has the Secretary decided ...?" where the person can know them.

§ `Who runs the program and how you must be treated (section 2020(a) to (d))`

-- s 2020(a)(1). The State agency of each participating State is responsible for certifying applicant households and issuing EBT cards.
@export Under section 2020(a)(1), is the State agency the one that certifies my household and issues our EBT cards?
GIVEN `my State takes part in SNAP` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your State take part in the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(a)(1), is the State agency the one that certifies my household and issues our EBT cards` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2020(a)(1) the party responsible for certifying applicant households and issuing EBT cards` `my State takes part in SNAP`
    WHEN JUST `the State agency` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- The module names no other party for a participating State, and none for a State that does not take part.
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 2020(a)(2). The State agency's responsibility is not affected by whether the State or the county runs the program.
@export Under section 2020(a)(2), does it change the State agency's responsibility for my case that my county, not the State, runs the program?
GIVEN `how SNAP is run where I live` IS A `s 2020(a)(2) basis of operation` @desc Is SNAP where you live run by the State, run by your county, or run on some other basis?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- The question is about the State agency, so the module's input "the body is a State agency" is answered yes.
DECIDE `Under section 2020(a)(2), does it change the State agency's responsibility for my case that my county, not the State, runs the program` IS
    `s 2020(a)(2) the responsibility of the State agency is affected by the basis of operation` `how SNAP is run where I live` (JUST TRUE)

-- s 2020(b). The State agency must promptly restore benefits it learns it improperly denied.
@export Under section 2020(b), must the State agency promptly restore benefits it wrongly denied my household?
GIVEN `the State agency has learned it wrongly denied my household benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State agency learned that it wrongly denied benefits to your household, which was eligible?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(b), must the State agency promptly restore benefits it wrongly denied my household` IS
    `s 2020(b) the State agency must promptly restore the improperly denied benefits` `the State agency has learned it wrongly denied my household benefits`

-- s 2020(c)(1). No discrimination in certifying applicant households on five named grounds.
@export Under section 2020(c)(1), may the State agency treat my household differently when certifying us because of race, sex, religious creed, national origin or political affiliation?
GIVEN `the reason I think I am treated differently` IS A `s 2020(c)(1) ground of discrimination` @desc What is the reason you think your household is treated differently: race, sex, religious creed, national origin, political affiliation, or some other reason?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(c)(1), may the State agency treat my household differently when certifying us because of race, sex, religious creed, national origin or political affiliation` IS
    `s 2020(c)(1) the certification of applicant households may discriminate by reason of the ground` `the reason I think I am treated differently`

-- s 2020(d). On an Indian reservation the State agency runs the program, unless the Secretary decides both that it is failing and that a tribal organization is capable.
-- Only for a person who lives on an Indian reservation; the form can ask "Do you live on an Indian reservation?" first.
@export Under section 2020(d), is a tribal organization, not the State agency, the one that runs SNAP on my reservation?
GIVEN `the Secretary has decided whether the State agency is failing properly to administer SNAP on my reservation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary decided whether the State agency is failing properly to administer SNAP on your reservation?
      `the Secretary found that the State agency is failing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did the Secretary find that the State agency is failing? (Answer no if the Secretary has not decided.)
      `the Secretary has decided whether the tribal organization is capable of running SNAP on my reservation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary decided whether the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently running SNAP on your reservation?
      `the Secretary found that the tribal organization is capable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did the Secretary find that the tribal organization is capable? (Answer no if the Secretary has not decided.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(d), is a tribal organization, not the State agency, the one that runs SNAP on my reservation` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2020(d) the party responsible for conducting the program on the reservation` `the Secretary's findings`
    WHEN JUST `a tribal organization` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- The module answers the State agency when either determination is that its condition does not hold: the text's "unless".
    WHEN JUST `the State agency` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the Secretary's findings` MEANS `s 2020(d) the Secretary's finding on a reservation` WITH
            `the Secretary determines that the State agency is failing properly to administer the program on the reservation` IS (IF `the Secretary has decided whether the State agency is failing properly to administer SNAP on my reservation` THEN JUST `the Secretary found that the State agency is failing` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the Secretary determines that the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently conducting the program` IS (IF `the Secretary has decided whether the tribal organization is capable of running SNAP on my reservation` THEN JUST `the Secretary found that the tribal organization is capable` ELSE NOTHING)

§ `Applying and being certified (section 2020(e)(1) to (5))`

-- s 2020(e)(1)(A). If the State agency has chosen to inform low-income households about the program, it must tell them of its availability, eligibility requirements, application procedures and benefits.
@export Under section 2020(e)(1)(A), must the State agency tell low-income households about SNAP, how to apply and what it pays?
GIVEN `my State agency has chosen to inform low-income households` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your State agency chosen to tell low-income households about SNAP (its availability, eligibility rules, how to apply and the benefits)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(1)(A), must the State agency tell low-income households about SNAP, how to apply and what it pays` IS
    `s 2020(e)(1)(A) the State agency must inform low-income households about the availability, eligibility requirements, application procedures and benefits` `my State agency has chosen to inform low-income households`

-- s 2020(e)(2)(B)(iii). A household may apply on the day of its first in-person contact with a SNAP office, during office hours.
@export Under section 2020(e)(2)(B)(iii), may my household apply on the same day we first go to a SNAP office?
GIVEN `we first went to a SNAP office in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the first time your household has contacted a SNAP office in person?
      `we went during office hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you go during the office's office hours?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(2)(B)(iii), may my household apply on the same day we first go to a SNAP office` IS
    `s 2020(e)(2)(B)(iii) the State agency must permit the household to apply on the same day` `we first went to a SNAP office in person` `we went during office hours`

-- s 2020(e)(2)(B)(iv). An application is filed on the day it is submitted, if it has the applicant's name, address and signature.
@export Under section 2020(e)(2)(B)(iv), on what day does my application count as filed?
GIVEN `my application has my name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application have your name on it?
      `my application has my address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application have your address on it?
      `my application is signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application have your signature on it?
      `the day I submitted my application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you submit your application?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(2)(B)(iv), on what day does my application count as filed` IS
    `s 2020(e)(2)(B)(iv) the date on which the application is considered filed` `my application has my name` `my application has my address` `my application is signed` `the day I submitted my application`

-- s 2020(e)(3). An eligible household is entitled to certification and a retroactive allotment within thirty days of filing.
@export Under section 2020(e)(3), is my household entitled to be certified, with a retroactive allotment, within thirty days after we filed?
GIVEN `my household is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your household eligible for SNAP?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(3), is my household entitled to be certified, with a retroactive allotment, within thirty days after we filed` IS
    `s 2020(e)(3) the household is entitled to certification and a retroactive allotment within thirty days of filing` `my household is eligible`

@export Under section 2020(e)(3), did the State agency certify us and provide our allotment within thirty days after we filed?
GIVEN `the day we filed our application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your household file its application?
      `the day we were certified and received our allotment` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you certified and given your allotment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(3), did the State agency certify us and provide our allotment within thirty days after we filed` IF
    `s 2020(e)(3) certification and the allotment were completed not later than thirty days following filing` `the day we filed our application` `the day we were certified and received our allotment`

-- s 2020(e)(4). On recertification: the household is entitled to its next allotment within a month of its last, if it filed on time and is still eligible.
-- Only for a person at recertification; the form can ask "Is your certification period ending?" first.
@export Under section 2020(e)(4), am I entitled to my next allotment within one month after my last, if I am recertified?
GIVEN `we were found still eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your household found still eligible when you recertified?
      `we filed our recertification application in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file the application for recertification in time (at least fifteen days before your certification period expires)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(4), am I entitled to my next allotment within one month after my last, if I am recertified` IS
    `s 2020(e)(4) the household is entitled to its next allotment no later than one month after the last` `we were found still eligible` `we filed our recertification application in time`

@export Under section 2020(e)(4), do we keep getting benefits on the old certification while a fair hearing is pending, if the new period finds us ineligible or eligible for less?
GIVEN `we were found ineligible, or eligible for less, in the new certification period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the new certification period, was your household found ineligible, or eligible for a smaller allotment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(4), do we keep getting benefits on the old certification while a fair hearing is pending, if the new period finds us ineligible or eligible for less` IS
    `s 2020(e)(4) the household continues to receive benefits on the basis of the preceding certification period pending a fair hearing` `we were found ineligible, or eligible for less, in the new certification period`

-- s 2020(e)(5). A State agency may not add requirements to those of sections 2014 and 2015 in deciding eligibility.
@export Under section 2020(e)(5), may the State agency add its own requirement, beyond those in sections 2014 and 2015, when deciding whether I am eligible?
GIVEN `the requirement is more than sections 2014 and 2015 ask` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement the State agency wants to apply one that is additional to what sections 2014 and 2015 of the Act require?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(5), may the State agency add its own requirement, beyond those in sections 2014 and 2015, when deciding whether I am eligible` IS
    `s 2020(e)(5) the State agency may impose the requirement in determining eligibility` `the requirement is more than sections 2014 and 2015 ask`

§ `Acting for you, and keeping your information private (section 2020(e)(7) and (8))`

-- s 2020(e)(7). Someone outside the household may act for it in the certification process, in getting benefits or in buying food, if clearly designated, adult and aware, and no Secretary restriction bars it.
@export Under section 2020(e)(7), may a person who is not in my household act for us?
GIVEN `what they would do for us` IS A `s 2020(e)(7) purpose of the representation` @desc What would the person do for your household: help with the certification process, help with getting benefits, or help buying food?
      `the head of the household or the spouse designated them clearly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the head of your household, or the head's spouse, clearly designate this person for that purpose?
      `they are an adult who knows our household's circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an adult who is sufficiently aware of your household's circumstances?
      `a Secretary restriction bars it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a restriction or criterion set by the Secretary that bars the person from acting for you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(7), may a person who is not in my household act for us` IS
    `s 2020(e)(7) the household may be represented by a person other than a member of the household` `what they would do for us` `the head of the household or the spouse designated them clearly` `they are an adult who knows our household's circumstances` `a Secretary restriction bars it`

-- s 2020(e)(8). The State agency's safeguards must prohibit use or disclosure of what households tell it, except for listed purposes.
@export Under section 2020(e)(8), must the State agency's safeguards stop it from using or sharing what I told it on my application for this purpose?
GIVEN `what the information would be used or shared for` IS A `s 2020(e)(8) use or disclosure of information obtained from applicant households` @desc What would the information from your application be used or shared for?
      `the conditions the Act attaches to that use are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions the Act attaches to that use or sharing met (for example, a request from a law enforcement official, or the notification an officer must make)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(8), must the State agency's safeguards stop it from using or sharing what I told it on my application for this purpose` IS
    `s 2020(e)(8) the safeguards must prohibit the use or disclosure` `what the information would be used or shared for` `the conditions the Act attaches to that use are met`

§ `Getting benefits quickly, hearings and lost benefits (section 2020(e)(9) to (11))`

-- s 2020(e)(9)(A). Expedited service: benefits within 7 days for a household with income under $150 a month and resources of $100 or less, or a destitute migrant or seasonal farmworker household.
@export Under section 2020(e)(9)(A), is my household entitled to benefits within seven days after we apply, because we have very little income and money?
GIVEN `our gross income per month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your household's gross income per month, in dollars?
      `we are a destitute migrant or seasonal farmworker household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your household a destitute migrant or seasonal farmworker household?
      `our liquid resources` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household have in liquid resources (cash, money in bank accounts), in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(9)(A), is my household entitled to benefits within seven days after we apply, because we have very little income and money` IS
    `s 2020(e)(9)(A) the household is entitled to benefits no later than 7 days after the date of application` `our gross income per month` `we are a destitute migrant or seasonal farmworker household` `our liquid resources`

-- s 2020(e)(9)(B). Expedited service: benefits within 7 days where income and resources are less than the household's monthly rent (or mortgage) and utilities.
@export Under section 2020(e)(9)(B), is my household entitled to benefits within seven days after we apply, because our rent and utilities are more than our income and money?
GIVEN `our gross income per month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your household's gross income per month, in dollars?
      `our liquid resources` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household have in liquid resources (cash, money in bank accounts), in dollars?
      `our monthly rent or mortgage and utilities` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household pay each month for rent or mortgage and utilities, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(9)(B), is my household entitled to benefits within seven days after we apply, because our rent and utilities are more than our income and money` IS
    `s 2020(e)(9)(B) the household is entitled to benefits no later than 7 days after the date of application` `our gross income per month` `our liquid resources` `our monthly rent or mortgage and utilities`

@export Under section 2020(e)(9), did we receive our benefits within seven days after we applied?
GIVEN `the day we applied` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your household apply?
      `the day we received benefits` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your household receive benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(9), did we receive our benefits within seven days after we applied` IF
    `s 2020(e)(9) benefits were provided no later than 7 days after the date of application` `the day we applied` `the day we received benefits`

-- s 2020(e)(10). Fair hearing: only for a person aggrieved by the State agency's action or by a claim for an overissuance; the form can ask "Do you disagree with a State agency decision?" first.
@export Under section 2020(e)(10), am I entitled to a fair hearing and a prompt decision after it?
GIVEN `I am aggrieved by the State agency's action on my participation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aggrieved by an action of the State agency under its plan of operation that affects your household's participation?
      `I am aggrieved by a claim for an overissuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aggrieved by a claim made against your household for an overissuance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(10), am I entitled to a fair hearing and a prompt decision after it` IS
    `s 2020(e)(10) the household is entitled to a fair hearing and a prompt determination thereafter` `I am aggrieved by the State agency's action on my participation` `I am aggrieved by a claim for an overissuance`

@export Under section 2020(e)(10), do we keep getting the benefits we were getting while we wait for the hearing?
GIVEN `we asked for a fair hearing in time after individual notice of reduced or terminated benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask for a fair hearing in time after you received individual notice that your benefits would be reduced or terminated within your certification period?
      `the hearing has been held and decided against us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the hearing been completed and decided against your household?
      `our certification period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your household's certification period ended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(10), do we keep getting the benefits we were getting while we wait for the hearing` IS
    `s 2020(e)(10) the household continues to participate and receive benefits on the basis authorized immediately prior to the notice` `we asked for a fair hearing in time after individual notice of reduced or terminated benefits` `the hearing has been held and decided against us` `our certification period has ended`

-- s 2020(e)(11). Only for a person whose benefits were wrongly denied or terminated; the form can ask "Were your benefits wrongly denied or stopped?" first.
@export Under section 2020(e)(11), must the State agency restore benefits for the period we lost them?
GIVEN `we asked for restoration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your household asked the State agency to restore the benefits?
      `the allotment was wrongly denied or terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your allotment, or part of it, wrongly denied or terminated?
      `the first day of the period we want restored` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period for which you want benefits restored?
      `the day the State agency first learned of the loss` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the State agency first receive your request, get notified, or discover that a loss had occurred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(e)(11), must the State agency restore benefits for the period we lost them` IS
    `s 2020(e)(11) the period must be restored to the household in the form of benefits` `we asked for restoration` `the allotment was wrongly denied or terminated` `the first day of the period we want restored` `the day the State agency first learned of the loss`

§ `Transitional benefits after cash assistance ends (section 2020(s))`

-- Only for a household whose cash assistance has ended; the form can ask "Has your household's cash assistance ended?" first.
-- s 2020(s)(2). Transitional benefits for not more than 5 months after the date cash assistance is terminated.
@export Under section 2020(s)(2), may my household still receive transitional benefits on a given day after our cash assistance ended?
GIVEN `the day our cash assistance ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your household's cash assistance end?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you want to know whether transitional benefits are allowed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(s)(2), may my household still receive transitional benefits on a given day after our cash assistance ended` IS
    `s 2020(s)(2) the household may receive transitional benefits on the day` `the day our cash assistance ended` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 2020(s)(3). The amount equals the last allotment before cash assistance ended, adjusted for the change in income.
@export Under section 2020(s)(3), how much are my household's transitional benefits each month, in dollars?
GIVEN `our allotment in the month before cash assistance ended` IS A NUMBER @desc What allotment did your household receive in the month immediately before your cash assistance ended, in dollars?
      `the change in our allotment from losing cash assistance` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much does your allotment change because the cash assistance ended, in dollars? (Use a negative number if it falls.)
      `the State agency takes other program information into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your State agency take information from another program into account for transitional benefits?
      `the change in our allotment from that information` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much does your allotment change because of that information, in dollars? (Use a negative number if it falls; 0 if none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2020(s)(3), how much are my household's transitional benefits each month, in dollars` IS
    `s 2020(s)(3) the amount of transitional benefits` `our allotment in the month before cash assistance ended` `the change in our allotment from losing cash assistance` `the State agency takes other program information into account` `the change in our allotment from that information`

-- s 2020(s)(5). A household that loses eligibility under section 2015, is sanctioned for a cash-assistance failure, or is in a category the State agency designates is not eligible.
@export Under section 2020(s)(5), is my household eligible for transitional benefits?
GIVEN `we lose eligibility under section 2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your household lose eligibility under section 2015 of the Act (for example, for failing a work requirement)?
      `we are sanctioned for failing to do what the cash assistance program requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your household sanctioned for failing to do something Federal, State or local law requires for the cash assistance program?
      `the State agency designated our category of households as ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your household in a category of households that the State agency has designated as ineligible for transitional benefits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2020(s)(5), is my household eligible for transitional benefits` IS
    `s 2020(s)(5) the household is eligible for transitional benefits` `we lose eligibility under section 2015` `we are sanctioned for failing to do what the cash assistance program requires` `the State agency designated our category of households as ineligible`

§ `Stores that take SNAP benefits (section 2021)`

-- s 2021(a)(1). A store that is approved and breaks the Act or its regulations may be disqualified from taking part in the program.
@export Under section 2021(a)(1), can the store where I use my benefits be barred from accepting them for breaking the SNAP rules?
GIVEN `the store is approved to accept SNAP benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the store approved to accept SNAP benefits?
      `the store broke a rule of the Act or its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the store break a provision of the Food and Nutrition Act or a regulation under it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- The sanction asked about is disqualification from the program, the first of the three the module names.
DECIDE `Under section 2021(a)(1), can the store where I use my benefits be barred from accepting them for breaking the SNAP rules` IS
    `s 2021(a)(1) the seller may be subjected to the sanction` (JUST `the store is approved to accept SNAP benefits`) `the store broke a rule of the Act or its regulations` `s 2021(a)(1)(A) disqualification for a specified period of time from further participation`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part snap5 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), sections 2025, 2026a and 2028 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a member of a household that applies for, or receives, benefits under the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions such a person would ask about
-- the parts of sections 2025, 2026a and 2028 that reach them: what a State may keep of money it recovers from their household,
-- what happens to their household's benefits when a State pays an employer to hire them, what the State may ask about their
-- Social Security number, what a State must do before it assigns them to a work program and what follows if they refuse,
-- whether the milk they buy is covered by an incentive project, and, in Puerto Rico and American Samoa, how the block grant
-- and the cash share of their benefit work and what the penalty is for taking its money.
-- Nothing here is new law, and the layer never restates a rule: each question builds the module's inputs from the person's
-- answers and calls the module's own rule.
--
-- THE SEAT IS NEVER AN OFFICIAL. The sections' other provisions (the quality control system, the performance bonus payments,
-- the cost-sharing percentages, the computerisation, the State plans and the funding formulas) address the Secretary or the
-- State agency and ask nothing a household member can state; they are encoded in the modules and are not asked here.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no answers, numbers and the modules' own choices, one for each fact the person states,
-- each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. A judgment the Act leaves to an official (the Secretary's determination
-- that access to Social Security records is necessary) is asked as a yes/no fact: if the answer is not yet known, the question
-- cannot be answered from here.
--
-- UNITS. A share in an answer is a FRACTION, not the percent printed in the Act: 35 percent is 0.35, 20 percent is 0.20, 5 percent is 0.05. Money is in dollars.
--
-- READING THE ANSWERS. A MAYBE BOOLEAN answer is JUST TRUE when the section says yes, JUST FALSE when the section says no in
-- its own words, and NOTHING when the section does not say (see NOTES.md, Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING).
-- The figures the Act sets (the cash caps for fiscal years 2017 to 2021, the penalty amounts) are the Act's own; a later
-- amendment would change these answers.

§ `Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 -- the questions a household member asks`

§§ `Section 2025(a): money the State recovers from my household`

-- s 2025(a). The State may be permitted to keep 35 percent of what it recovers or collects under section 2015(b) (fraud and
-- misrepresentation) or section 2022(c) (intercepting unemployment benefits), and 20 percent of anything else, except what
-- arises from the State agency's own error.
@export Under section 2025(a), what share of the money recovered or collected from my household may the State keep?
GIVEN `the money was recovered or collected under section 2015(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the money recovered or collected from your household under section 2015(b), the section on fraud, misrepresentation and the penalties for them?
      `the money was recovered or collected under section 2022(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the money recovered or collected from your household under section 2022(c), the section on intercepting unemployment benefits?
      `the money arises from an error of the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the money arise from a mistake made by the State agency?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2025(a), what share of the money recovered or collected from my household may the State keep` IS
    CONSIDER `s 2025(a) the share of recovered or collected funds the Secretary may permit the State to retain` `the money was recovered or collected under section 2015(b)` `the money was recovered or collected under section 2022(c)` `the money arises from an error of the State agency`
    WHEN `s 2025(a) may be permitted to retain` share THEN JUST share
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except the value of funds or allotments recovered or collected that arise from an error of a State agency"
    WHEN `s 2025(a) may not be permitted to retain under this proviso` THEN JUST 0
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the two answers above cover every case the rule returns; this branch only completes the CONSIDER
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Section 2025(b): a State paying an employer to hire me (work supplementation)`
-- Ask "Is a State agency using my household's benefits to pay an employer to hire me?" before showing this group.

-- s 2025(b)(3)(C)(i). The money the State agency pays the employer is not counted as income or resources of the household for the
-- purposes of sections 2014 and 2017(a).
@export Under section 2025(b)(3)(C)(i), is the money my State pays my employer left out of my household's income and resources?
GIVEN `the State agency elected to use an amount equal to our household's allotment to subsidize or support a job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State agency chosen to use an amount equal to your household's allotment to pay for, or support, a job in a work supplementation or support program?
      `the State agency identified our household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State agency identified your household as one that contains a person taking part in that program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2025(b)(3)(C)(i), is the money my State pays my employer left out of my household's income and resources` IS
    `s 2025(b)(3)(C)(i) the amount received is excluded from household income and resources for sections 2014 and 2017(a)` (`s 2025(b)(3) the procedure applies` `the State agency elected to use an amount equal to our household's allotment to subsidize or support a job` `the State agency identified our household`)

-- s 2025(b)(3)(C)(ii). The same money is treated as the value of an allotment provided to the household for the purposes of section 2017(b).
@export Under section 2025(b)(3)(C)(ii), is the money my State pays my employer treated as the value of an allotment my household has received?
GIVEN `the State agency elected to use an amount equal to our household's allotment to subsidize or support a job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State agency chosen to use an amount equal to your household's allotment to pay for, or support, a job in a work supplementation or support program?
      `the State agency identified our household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State agency identified your household as one that contains a person taking part in that program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2025(b)(3)(C)(ii), is the money my State pays my employer treated as the value of an allotment my household has received` IS
    `s 2025(b)(3)(C)(ii) the amount received is considered the value of an allotment provided to the household for section 2017(b)` (`s 2025(b)(3) the procedure applies` `the State agency elected to use an amount equal to our household's allotment to subsidize or support a job` `the State agency identified our household`)

-- s 2025(b)(3)(D). The household may receive an allotment from the State agency for as long as a member continues to take part.
@export Under section 2025(b)(3)(D), may my household receive an allotment from the State agency while I stay in the program?
GIVEN `the State agency elected to use an amount equal to our household's allotment to subsidize or support a job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State agency chosen to use an amount equal to your household's allotment to pay for, or support, a job in a work supplementation or support program?
      `the State agency identified our household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State agency identified your household as one that contains a person taking part in that program?
      `I continue to take part in the work supplementation or support program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you continue to take part in the work supplementation or support program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2025(b)(3)(D), may my household receive an allotment from the State agency while I stay in the program` IS
    `s 2025(b)(3)(D) the household may receive an allotment from the State agency for the period` (`s 2025(b)(3) the procedure applies` `the State agency elected to use an amount equal to our household's allotment to subsidize or support a job` `the State agency identified our household`) `I continue to take part in the work supplementation or support program`

-- s 2025(b)(4). Having a work supplementation program is no excuse from the work requirement of section 2015(d) for a person who is not employed under it.
@export Under section 2025(b)(4), am I excused from a work requirement because my State has a work supplementation program?
GIVEN `my State has a work supplementation or support program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your State have a work supplementation or support program?
      `I am employed under that program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under that program?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2025(b)(4), am I excused from a work requirement because my State has a work supplementation program` IS
    `s 2025(b)(4) the individual is excused from a work requirement under section 2015(d) by reason of the fact that the State has a work supplementation or support program` `my State has a work supplementation or support program` `I am employed under that program`

§§ `Section 2025(e): my Social Security number`

-- s 2025(e)(1). Furnishing a Social Security account number is a condition of eligibility for each member.
@export Under section 2025(e)(1), have I met the condition of eligibility of furnishing a Social Security number?
GIVEN `I have a Social Security account number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a Social Security account number?
      `I have given the State agency every Social Security account number I have` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the State agency every Social Security account number you have?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2025(e)(1), have I met the condition of eligibility of furnishing a Social Security number` IS
    `s 2025(e)(1) the household member has met the condition of eligibility of furnishing a social security account number` `I have a Social Security account number` `I have given the State agency every Social Security account number I have`

-- s 2025(e). The Secretary and the State agencies have access to information held by the Social Security Administration about an
-- applicant or participant who receives benefits under title XVI, only to the extent the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security determine
-- the access is necessary for determining or auditing eligibility or the amount of assistance.
@export Under section 2025(e), may the Secretary and my State agency see my Social Security records?
GIVEN `I receive benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act (Supplemental Security Income)?
      `the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security have determined that access to my records is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security determined that access to your records is necessary?
      `the access is for determining or auditing my household's eligibility or the amount of assistance, or verifying related information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the access for determining or auditing your household's eligibility or the amount of its assistance, or for verifying information related to them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2025(e), may the Secretary and my State agency see my Social Security records` IS
    `s 2025(e) the Secretary and State agencies shall have access to the information` `I receive benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act` (JUST `the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security have determined that access to my records is necessary`) `the access is for determining or auditing my household's eligibility or the amount of assistance, or verifying related information`

§§ `Section 2025(h)(1): employment and training, and pilot projects`
-- Ask "Has a State agency offered or assigned me to an employment and training program?" before showing this group.

-- s 2025(h)(1)(E)(ii). A State agency that gets an additional allocation must commit to offer a position to each applicant or recipient who is in the last month
-- of the 3-month period of section 2015(o)(2), and is not eligible for an exception, not eligible for a waiver and not exempt.
@export Under section 2025(h)(1)(E)(ii), does my State agency's commitment to offer a position cover me?
GIVEN `I am in the last month of the 3-month period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in the last month of the 3-month period described in section 2015(o)(2)?
      `I am eligible for an exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for an exception under section 2015(o)(3)?
      `I am eligible for a waiver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for a waiver under section 2015(o)(4)?
      `I am exempt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you exempt under section 2015(o)(6)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2025(h)(1)(E)(ii), does my State agency's commitment to offer a position cover me` IS
    `s 2025(h)(1)(E)(ii) the commitment to offer a position covers the applicant or recipient` (JUST `I am in the last month of the 3-month period`) (JUST `I am eligible for an exception`) (JUST `I am eligible for a waiver`) (JUST `I am exempt`)

-- s 2025(h)(1)(F)(vi)(II). A failure to work for reasons beyond the person's control, in a job of the kinds in subclauses (I) to (III) of clause (iv),
-- "shall not result in ineligibility".
@export Under section 2025(h)(1)(F)(vi)(II), does my failure to work cost me my eligibility?
GIVEN `my activity is a job of the kind in subclause (I), (II) or (III) of clause (iv)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your activity a job: unsubsidized employment, or employment where the employer gets a public subsidy, in the private or public sector?
      `my failure to work was for reasons beyond my control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your failure to work for reasons beyond your control, such as your hours of employment being reduced against your will?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2025(h)(1)(F)(vi)(II), does my failure to work cost me my eligibility` IS
    `s 2025(h)(1)(F)(vi)(II) the failure to work results in ineligibility` `my activity is a job of the kind in subclause (I), (II) or (III) of clause (iv)` `my failure to work was for reasons beyond my control`

-- s 2025(h)(1)(F)(v). Subject to clause (vi), a work registrant is not eligible to take part in the program if they refuse without good cause to take part in
-- a pilot project's employment and training program, to the extent the State agency requires it.
@export Under section 2025(h)(1)(F)(v), am I ineligible for the program because I refused to take part in a pilot project?
GIVEN `I am a work registrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a work registrant under section 2015(d)?
      `I refused to take part in the pilot project's employment and training program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse to take part in an employment and training program run as a pilot project?
      `the State agency requires me to take part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the State agency require you to take part?
      `I had good cause for refusing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have good cause for refusing?
      `my activity is a job of the kind in subclause (I), (II) or (III) of clause (iv)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your activity a job: unsubsidized employment, or employment where the employer gets a public subsidy, in the private or public sector?
      `my failure to work was for reasons beyond my control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your failure to work for reasons beyond your control, such as your hours of employment being reduced against your will?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2025(h)(1)(F)(v), am I ineligible for the program because I refused to take part in a pilot project` IS
    `s 2025(h)(1)(F)(v) the work registrant is ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` `I am a work registrant` `I refused to take part in the pilot project's employment and training program` `the State agency requires me to take part` (JUST `I had good cause for refusing`) (`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(vi)(II) the failure to work results in ineligibility` `my activity is a job of the kind in subclause (I), (II) or (III) of clause (iv)` `my failure to work was for reasons beyond my control`)

-- s 2025(h)(1)(F)(vi)(III). Before assigning a work registrant to mandatory employment and training activities, a State agency must assess whether they are already
-- taking part in substantial activities elsewhere, and if those are acceptable, count their hours.
@export Under section 2025(h)(1)(F)(vi)(III), did my State agency do what it must before assigning me to mandatory activities?
GIVEN `the State agency assessed whether I take part in substantial employment and training activities outside the pilot project` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the State agency assess whether you are taking part in substantial employment and training activities outside the pilot project that are expected to give you increased skills, training, work or experience consistent with the pilot project's objectives?
      `the State agency determined those activities to be acceptable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the State agency determine that those activities are acceptable?
      `the State agency counted my hours in those activities toward any minimum participation requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the State agency count your hours in those activities toward any minimum participation requirement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2025(h)(1)(F)(vi)(III), did my State agency do what it must before assigning me to mandatory activities` IS
    `s 2025(h)(1)(F)(vi)(III) the State agency complied before assigning the work registrant to mandatory activities` `the State agency assessed whether I take part in substantial employment and training activities outside the pilot project` `the State agency determined those activities to be acceptable` `the State agency counted my hours in those activities toward any minimum participation requirement`

§§ `Section 2026a: healthy fluid milk incentive projects`

-- s 2026a(a). "Fluid milk" for the incentive projects: pasteurized cow's milk without flavoring or sweeteners, consistent with the most recent dietary
-- recommendations, in liquid form, with vitamins A and D at levels consistent with the Food and Drug Administration, State and local standards.
@export Under section 2026a(a), is the milk I buy fluid milk for the healthy fluid milk incentive projects?
GIVEN `it is pasteurized cow's milk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it pasteurized cow's milk?
      `it has no flavoring or sweeteners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it without flavoring or sweeteners?
      `it is consistent with the most recent dietary recommendations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it consistent with the most recent dietary recommendations?
      `it is in liquid form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it packaged in liquid form?
      `its vitamins A and D meet the Food and Drug Administration standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain vitamins A and D at levels consistent with the Food and Drug Administration standards for fluid milk?
      `its vitamins A and D meet the State standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain vitamins A and D at levels consistent with your State's standards for fluid milk?
      `its vitamins A and D meet the local standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain vitamins A and D at levels consistent with your locality's standards for fluid milk?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026a(a), is the milk I buy fluid milk for the healthy fluid milk incentive projects` IS
    `s 2026a(a) the product is fluid milk` `it is pasteurized cow's milk` `it has no flavoring or sweeteners` `it is consistent with the most recent dietary recommendations` `it is in liquid form` `its vitamins A and D meet the Food and Drug Administration standards` `its vitamins A and D meet the State standards` `its vitamins A and D meet the local standards`

§§ `Section 2028: Puerto Rico and American Samoa`

-- s 2028(a)(1). The block grants go to two governmental entities: the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico and American Samoa.
@export Under section 2028(a)(1), is the place where I live one the nutrition assistance block grants go to?
GIVEN `where I live` IS A `s 2028 place` @desc Where do you live: the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, American Samoa, or any other place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2028(a)(1), is the place where I live one the nutrition assistance block grants go to` IS
    `s 2028(a)(1) the place is a governmental entity` `where I live`

-- s 2028(e)(3)(A). The Secretary must disapprove a plan that gives a participant more than a stated share of their benefit as cash: 20 percent for
-- fiscal year 2017, 15 for 2018, 10 for 2019, 5 for 2020 and none for 2021 (subject to the exception in subparagraph (B)).
@export Under section 2028(e)(3)(A), what is the largest share of my nutrition assistance benefit that Puerto Rico's plan may pay me in cash?
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER @desc Which fiscal year (a number such as 2019) do you ask about?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2028(e)(3)(A), what is the largest share of my nutrition assistance benefit that Puerto Rico's plan may pay me in cash` IS
    `s 2028(e)(3)(A) the largest share of a participant's benefit a plan may distribute in cash` `fiscal year`

-- s 2028(d). Whoever knowingly and willfully embezzles, misapplies, steals, or obtains by fraud, false statement, or forgery funds provided or financed under this section.
@export Under section 2028(d), is what I did within the offence of taking the block grant's money?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `s 2028(d) conduct` @desc What did you do with the money: embezzle it, misapply it, steal it, or obtain it by fraud, by a false statement or by forgery, or something else?
      `I did it knowingly and willfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it knowingly and willfully?
      `the money, assets or property were provided or financed under section 2028` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the funds, assets or property provided or financed under section 2028?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2028(d), is what I did within the offence of taking the block grant's money` IS
    `s 2028(d) the conduct is within the offence` `what I did` `I did it knowingly and willfully` `the money, assets or property were provided or financed under section 2028`

-- s 2028(d). The penalty: a fine of not more than $10,000 or imprisonment of not more than five years, or both; but where the value is not over $200, a fine of not more than $1,000
-- or imprisonment for not more than one year, or both.
@export Under section 2028(d), what is the most I can be fined for taking the block grant's money, in dollars?
GIVEN `value of the funds, assets or property` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the funds, assets or property involved, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2028(d), what is the most I can be fined for taking the block grant's money, in dollars` IS
    `s 2028(d) the most the person may be fined, in dollars` `value of the funds, assets or property`

@export Under section 2028(d), what is the longest I can be imprisoned for taking the block grant's money, in years?
GIVEN `value of the funds, assets or property` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the funds, assets or property involved, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2028(d), what is the longest I can be imprisoned for taking the block grant's money, in years` IS
    `s 2028(d) the longest term of imprisonment, in years` `value of the funds, assets or property`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part snap6 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (United States, 7 U.S.C. ch. 51), sections 2026, 2031, 2035 and 2036a -- THE SEAT LAYER (snap6).
--
-- The source is a converter's plain-text rendering of the Code, not the official text; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a member of a household that applies for, or receives, benefits under the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP), asking, on
-- facts they can state, what the sections in snap6's ranges mean for them: whether the household may take an aggregate allotment, whether a
-- pilot project may change their benefits and how, whether they may be made to take part in an activity that turns benefits into cash,
-- what the Minnesota Family Investment Project owes a participating family, whether their household may take part in a State's simplified
-- program, and whether they are an eligible individual for nutrition education. Nothing here is new law: each question calls a rule of the
-- layer-1 modules imported above and never restates it.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the person can
-- state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records the layer-1 rules take (an adult member, a vehicle, a parent, a
-- group of minor children) are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME layer-1 rule is then called.
-- A seam input -- an answer that another section of the Act gives, such as s 2014, s 2017, s 2020(e) or s 2027(a) -- is kept as a MAYBE
-- BOOLEAN or MAYBE NUMBER, with the name of the answering section, so that the person can leave it blank when it has not been decided and
-- the answer stays "not covered" instead of becoming "no" (the rule of 2026-10-29: a caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE).
--
-- ONE CASE. The text's natural unit is one household, one adult member, one vehicle, one parent. The layer-1 rules for an adult member
-- (s 2026(d)(3)) and for vehicles (s 2026(h)) take lists; the seat asks about ONE adult member of the household and ONE vehicle, and builds
-- a one-item list. A household with two vehicles asks the vehicle question for each and adds the answers only where the text says so
-- (s 2026(h) excludes one vehicle under paragraph (2), so the sum is not the sum of the one-vehicle answers).
--
-- READING A RESULT. Every question here answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN or a MAYBE NUMBER. JUST TRUE is "the text says yes", JUST FALSE is "the text
-- says no in its own words", and NOTHING is "the text does not cover this case" (see NOTES.md, Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING).
--
-- NOT ASKED, AND WHY. s 2033 is repealed. s 2034 (community food projects) and s 2036 (commodities for the emergency food assistance
-- program) address only the Secretary, grantees and States: nothing in them is done to a household member that the member could state facts
-- about, so they have no question. The Secretary's, a State's and a grantee's own duties in the sections that are asked (reports,
-- deadlines, plans, payments among governments) are in layer 1 only. s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) (the list of projects the Secretary may not run)
-- and s 2031(b)(12), (d), (f) and (i) (money among governments, audits, evaluation) have no question for the same reason.
--
-- SEATS. One seat, the household member. There is no seat for an official. A second seat over the same modules could be added for a State
-- agency in the same folder as snap6-seat-state-agency.l4 (not written here).
--
-- Where this layer departs from the defaults ruled on 2026-10-18 (recorded, not fixed): see NOTES.md, Seat (snap6).

§ `Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 -- a SNAP household member's questions (sections 2026, 2031, 2035, 2036a)`

§§ `Section 2026 -- research, demonstration, and evaluations: pilot and demonstration projects that can change your benefits`

-- s 2026(a)(2). An aggregate allotment is one payment in place of the regular allotment, covering up to 3 months, for a household whose monthly benefits are $20 or less and that chooses it.
@export Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household receive an aggregate allotment in place of its regular allotments?
GIVEN `my household's monthly SNAP benefits, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your household receive in SNAP benefits each month, in dollars?
      `I choose to receive an aggregate allotment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it your choice (your option) to receive an aggregate allotment instead of your regular allotments?
      `the aggregate allotment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much would the aggregate allotment be, in dollars?
      `the number of months' benefits the aggregate allotment would cover` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months' benefits would the aggregate allotment cover?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household receive an aggregate allotment` IS
    `s 2026(a)(2) the household may receive the aggregate allotment` `my household's monthly SNAP benefits, in dollars` `I choose to receive an aggregate allotment` `the aggregate allotment, in dollars` `the number of months' benefits the aggregate allotment would cover`

-- s 2026(a)(2), parenthesis. A household may not begin to receive combined allotments until it has complied with all applicable verification requirements of section 2020(e)(3).
@export Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household begin to receive combined allotments?
GIVEN `s 2020(e)(3) my household has complied with all applicable verification requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Has your household complied with all the verification requirements that apply to it? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(a)(2), may my household begin to receive combined allotments` IS
    `s 2026(a)(2) the household may begin to receive combined allotments` `s 2020(e)(3) my household has complied with all applicable verification requirements`

-- s 2026(a)(2). The first aggregate allotment must come within 40 days of the last benefit issuance.
@export Under section 2026(a)(2), was my first aggregate allotment provided in time?
GIVEN `this is my first aggregate allotment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the first aggregate allotment your household has been issued?
      `days from my last benefit issuance to the aggregate allotment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days passed between your last benefit issuance and the aggregate allotment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(a)(2), was my first aggregate allotment provided in time` IS
    `s 2026(a)(2) the first aggregate allotment was provided in time` `this is my first aggregate allotment` `days from my last benefit issuance to the aggregate allotment`

-- s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii). The limits on a pilot project (15 percent of the State's households, 5 years) apply only where the project would cut benefits by more than 20 percent for more than 5 percent of the households in the area.
@export Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii), do the limits on a pilot project apply to the project in my area?
GIVEN `the percentage of households in my area whose benefits the project would cut by more than 20 percent` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the households in your area would have their benefits cut by more than 20 percent by the project? (Do not count households cut for failing to comply with work or other conduct requirements.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii), do the limits on a pilot project apply to the project in my area` IS
    `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii) the restrictions apply to the project` `the percentage of households in my area whose benefits the project would cut by more than 20 percent`

-- s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v). A pilot or experimental project may include cash payments of allotments only for households all of whose members are 65 or over, or any of whose members get SSI or part A assistance; it may also include privacy-respecting identification and food checks.
@export Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(v), may the project include this kind of change for my household?
GIVEN `the kind of change the project makes` IS A `s 2026 additional included project` @desc Which kind of change does the project make? Choose one of: s 2026 payment of the value of allotments, or the average value by household size, in cash to eligible households; s 2026 the use of identification mechanisms that do not invade a household's privacy; s 2026 the use of food checks or other voucher-type forms in place of EBT cards; s 2026 some other project.
      `all members of my household are age sixty-five or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the members of your household age sixty-five or over?
      `any member of my household gets supplemental security income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any member of your household get supplemental security income benefits (under title XVI of the Social Security Act)?
      `any member of my household gets assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any member of your household get assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(v), may the project include this kind of change for my household` IS
    `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v) the project may be included in a pilot or experimental project` `the kind of change the project makes` `all members of my household are age sixty-five or over` `any member of my household gets supplemental security income` `any member of my household gets assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV`

-- s 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi). A cash-payment pilot project operating on 1 October 1981 for households all of whose members are 65 or over or on SSI shall be continued if the State so requests, subject to appropriations under section 2027(a).
@export Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi), must the cash-payment project I receive be continued?
GIVEN `my project was operating on 1 October 1981 and pays allotments in cash to households whose members are all 65 or over or on SSI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the project that pays you cash instead of an allotment already operating on 1 October 1981, paying cash to households all of whose members are 65 or over or on SSI?
      `my State asks that the project be continued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your State asked that the project be continued?
      `s 2027(a) appropriations are available` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Are appropriations available for it under section 2027(a)? (Leave blank if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi), must the cash-payment project I receive be continued` IS
    `s 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi) the project shall be continued` `my project was operating on 1 October 1981 and pays allotments in cash to households whose members are all 65 or over or on SSI` `my State asks that the project be continued` `s 2027(a) appropriations are available`

-- s 2026(b)(1)(C). After 28 November 1990 no waiver or demonstration program may be approved unless households not on EBT cards are compensated for the sales tax and the State agency pays the cost.
@export Under section 2026(b)(1)(C), may the waiver or demonstration program that covers my household be approved?
GIVEN `the date the waiver or demonstration program is approved` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the waiver or demonstration program approved?
      `my food assistance is issued in a form other than an EBT card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your food assistance issued in a form other than an EBT card?
      `my allotment is increased to cover the sales tax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your allotment increased to make up for any State or local sales tax on food?
      `the sales tax on my food purchases is waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the tax on your food purchases waived?
      `the Secretary has decided the increase is unnecessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary decided that the increase is unnecessary because few items are taxed?
      `the State agency pays the cost of any increased allotments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the State agency running the project pay the cost of any increased allotments?
      `the project already gives me more than the sales tax I would pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the project already give your household assistance that exceeds what it would otherwise get by more than the sales tax on its food?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(b)(1)(C), may the waiver or demonstration program that covers my household be approved` IS
    `s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` `the date the waiver or demonstration program is approved` `my food assistance is issued in a form other than an EBT card` `my allotment is increased to cover the sales tax` `the sales tax on my food purchases is waived` `the Secretary has decided the increase is unnecessary` `the State agency pays the cost of any increased allotments` `the project already gives me more than the sales tax I would pay`

-- s 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii). If the Secretary does not respond to a State's waiver request as clause (i) says, the waiver is considered approved, unless the approval is specifically prohibited.
@export Under section 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii), is the waiver my State asked for considered approved?
GIVEN `the Secretary responded to my State's request in the way section 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary answered your State's waiver request with an approval, a denial that says what to change or why, or a request for clarification?
      `this chapter specifically prohibits the approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Food and Nutrition Act specifically prohibit approving the waiver?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii), is the waiver my State asked for considered approved` IS
    `s 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii) the waiver is considered approved` `the Secretary responded to my State's request in the way section 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) says` `this chapter specifically prohibits the approval`

-- s 2026(b)(2)(D). Taking part in an employment and training activity in which SNAP benefits are converted to cash shall occur only with the participant's consent.
@export Under section 2026(b)(2)(D), may I take part in an employment and training activity that converts my benefits to cash?
GIVEN `the activity converts my SNAP benefits to cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the employment and training activity turn your SNAP benefits into cash?
      `I consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to take part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(b)(2)(D), may I take part in an employment and training activity that converts my benefits to cash` IS
    `s 2026(b)(2)(D) the participant may take part in the activity` `the activity converts my SNAP benefits to cash` `I consent`

-- s 2026(d)(2)(C)(ii). A household that gets cash benefits under the employment initiatives program does not receive other SNAP benefits for the period the cash covers.
@export Under section 2026(d)(2)(C)(ii), may my household receive other SNAP benefits for the period my cash benefits cover?
GIVEN `my household is receiving cash benefits under the employment initiatives program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your household receiving cash benefits under your State's employment initiatives program?
      `my household receives other SNAP benefits in the period the cash covers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your household also receive other SNAP benefits during the period the cash benefits cover?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(d)(2)(C)(ii), may my household receive other SNAP benefits for the period my cash benefits cover` IS
    `s 2026(d)(2)(C)(ii) the household may receive the other supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` `my household is receiving cash benefits under the employment initiatives program` `my household receives other SNAP benefits in the period the cash covers`

-- s 2026(d)(2)(D)(i). A State that runs the employment initiatives program shall increase the cash benefits to cover any State or local sales tax on food, unless the Secretary decides the increase is unnecessary.
@export Under section 2026(d)(2)(D)(i), must my State increase my cash benefits for the sales tax?
GIVEN `a sales tax may be collected on my food purchases` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May a State or local sales tax be collected on your household's food purchases?
      `the Secretary has decided the increase is unnecessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary decided, on information from your State, that the increase is unnecessary because so few items are taxed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(d)(2)(D)(i), must my State increase my cash benefits for the sales tax` IS
    `s 2026(d)(2)(D)(i) the State shall increase the cash benefits for the sales tax` `a sales tax may be collected on my food purchases` `the Secretary has decided the increase is unnecessary`

-- s 2026(d)(3). A household may get cash benefits under the employment initiatives program if an adult member has worked 90 days, earned $350 a month, is on part A benefits (or was and lost them to earned income), keeps earning $350 a month, and elects cash. The question is about one adult member of the household.
@export Under section 2026(d)(3), is my household eligible to receive cash benefits through an adult member?
GIVEN `days this adult member has worked in unsubsidized employment just before today` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in a row, up to today, has this adult member of your household worked in unsubsidized employment?
      `the least this adult member earned in a month over those days, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the least this adult member earned in any month over those days, in dollars?
      `this adult member is receiving part A benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this adult member receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act?
      `this adult member was receiving part A benefits when first receiving cash benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was this adult member receiving part A benefits when they first received cash benefits under your State's program?
      `this adult member is no longer eligible for the State program because of earned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this adult member no longer eligible for the State program because of their earned income?
      `what this adult member continues to earn a month, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does this adult member continue to earn each month from that employment, in dollars?
      `this adult member elects to receive cash benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this adult member choose to receive cash benefits instead of SNAP benefits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(d)(3), is my household eligible to receive cash benefits through an adult member` IS
    `s 2026(d)(3) the household is eligible to receive cash benefits` (LIST `this adult member`)
    WHERE
        `this adult member` MEANS `s 2026 adult member` WITH
            `the days the adult has worked in unsubsidized employment immediately before today` IS `days this adult member has worked in unsubsidized employment just before today`
            `the least the adult earned in a month from that employment over those days, in dollars` IS `the least this adult member earned in a month over those days, in dollars`
            `the adult is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS `this adult member is receiving part A benefits`
            `the adult was receiving such benefits when first receiving cash benefits under this subsection` IS `this adult member was receiving part A benefits when first receiving cash benefits`
            `the adult is no longer eligible for the State program because of earned income` IS `this adult member is no longer eligible for the State program because of earned income`
            `the adult is continuing to earn a month from that employment, in dollars` IS `what this adult member continues to earn a month, in dollars`
            `the adult elects to receive cash benefits in lieu of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` IS `this adult member elects to receive cash benefits`

-- s 2026(h). In a vehicle demonstration project, the value of a licensed vehicle counts as a financial resource only to the extent it exceeds $4,500; a vehicle for earned income, an elderly or disabled member's transport or a home is excluded; one vehicle for work, education or training, or getting food is excluded. The question is about the household's one vehicle.
@export Under section 2026(h), how much of the value of my vehicle counts as a financial resource in the demonstration project?
GIVEN `the fair market value of my vehicle, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fair market value of your licensed vehicle, in dollars?
      `my vehicle is used to produce earned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the vehicle to produce earned income?
      `my vehicle is necessary for transporting an elderly or physically disabled household member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vehicle necessary for transporting an elderly or physically disabled member of your household?
      `my vehicle is used as my household's home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the vehicle as your household's home?
      `my vehicle is used to get, keep or look for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the vehicle to obtain, continue or seek employment (including travel to and from work)?
      `my vehicle is used for employment-related education or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the vehicle to pursue employment-related education or training?
      `my vehicle is used to get food or SNAP benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the vehicle to secure food or the benefits of the supplemental nutrition assistance program?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2026(h), how much of the value of my vehicle counts as a financial resource` IS
    `s 2026(h) the value of the vehicles counted as financial resources, in dollars` (LIST `my vehicle`)
    WHERE
        `my vehicle` MEANS `s 2026 vehicle` WITH
            `the fair market value of the licensed vehicle, in dollars` IS `the fair market value of my vehicle, in dollars`
            `it is used to produce earned income` IS `my vehicle is used to produce earned income`
            `it is necessary for transportation of an elderly or physically disabled household member` IS `my vehicle is necessary for transporting an elderly or physically disabled household member`
            `it is used as the household's home` IS `my vehicle is used as my household's home`
            `it is used to obtain, continue, or seek employment, including travel to and from work` IS `my vehicle is used to get, keep or look for work`
            `it is used to pursue employment-related education or training` IS `my vehicle is used for employment-related education or training`
            `it is used to secure food or the benefits of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS `my vehicle is used to get food or SNAP benefits`

-- s 2026(i). In a resource-accumulation project a household may accumulate up to $10,000 that is excluded as a resource.
@export Under section 2026(i), how much of the resources I have accumulated is excluded as a resource?
GIVEN `the resources my household has accumulated for the purpose, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much has your household accumulated, in dollars, for a later expense that the project tests?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2026(i), how much of the resources I have accumulated is excluded as a resource` IS
    `s 2026(i) the resources excluded from consideration as a resource, in dollars` `the resources my household has accumulated for the purpose, in dollars`

-- s 2026(i). The projects test accumulating resources for education, training or employability, buying a home, changing residence, or major repairs to the home.
@export Under section 2026(i), is the purpose I am saving for one the project tests?
GIVEN `the purpose I am saving for` IS A `s 2026 purpose of accumulated resources` @desc What are you saving for? Choose one of: s 2026 improving the education, training, or employability, including self-employment, of household members; s 2026 the purchase of a home for the household; s 2026 a change of the household's residence; s 2026 making major repairs to the household's home; s 2026 some other purpose of expenditure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(i), is the purpose I am saving for one the project tests` IS
    `s 2026(i) the purpose is one the projects test` `the purpose I am saving for`

-- s 2026(k)(2)(C)(i). A health and nutrition pilot project may be judged on whether it reaches a low-income target audience: households at or below 185 percent of the poverty level.
@export Under section 2026(k)(2)(C)(i), is my household in the low-income target audience of a health and nutrition pilot project?
GIVEN `my household's income as a percent of the poverty level` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your household's income as a percent of the poverty level? (100 means exactly at the poverty level.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(k)(2)(C)(i), is my household in the low-income target audience` IS
    `s 2026(k)(2)(C)(i) the individual is in the low-income target audience` `my household's income as a percent of the poverty level`

-- s 2026(n)(4)(B)(i). A State that sets up a longitudinal database must keep personally identifiable information (social security number, home address, contact information) out of it.
@export Under section 2026(n)(4)(B)(i), does my State's longitudinal database protect my privacy?
GIVEN `the database includes information that identifies me, such as my social security number, home address or contact information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the database include information that identifies you personally, such as your social security number, home address or contact information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2026(n)(4)(B)(i), does my State's longitudinal database protect my privacy` IS
    `s 2026(n)(4)(B)(i) the database protects the privacy of household members` `the database includes information that identifies me, such as my social security number, home address or contact information`

§§ `Section 2031 -- the Minnesota Family Investment Project: if your family takes part in the Project`

-- s 2031(b)(2). A family may receive SNAP benefits if it takes part in the Project only in the ways the paragraph names.
@export Under section 2031(b)(2), may my family receive SNAP benefits?
GIVEN `my family takes part in the Project` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your family take part in the Minnesota Family Investment Project?
      `my family was already on part A or SNAP and was assigned to the Project and found eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your family already eligible for or on the part A of title IV program or SNAP, assigned to the Project, and found eligible for it?
      `my family had to apply for the Project and was found eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your family have to apply for the Project, and was it found eligible?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(2), may my family receive SNAP benefits` IS
    `s 2031(b)(2) the family may receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` `my family takes part in the Project` `my family was already on part A or SNAP and was assigned to the Project and found eligible` `my family had to apply for the Project and was found eligible`

-- s 2031(b)(3)(A). The value of the assistance a family gets under the Project must be at least what it could get under SNAP and part A if it did not take part, less any reduction under (c)(3).
@export Under section 2031(b)(3)(A), is the value of the assistance my family gets under the Project enough?
GIVEN `the value of the assistance my family gets under the Project, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the assistance your family gets under the Project, in dollars?
      `what my family could get under SNAP and part A if it did not take part, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What could your family get under SNAP and part A of title IV together if it did not take part in the Project, in dollars?
      `the reduction under section 2031(c)(3), in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much has your family's assistance been reduced because of a failure to take part in education, employment or training, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(3)(A), is the value of the assistance my family gets under the Project enough` IS
    `s 2031(b)(3)(A) the value of the assistance is enough` `the value of the assistance my family gets under the Project, in dollars` `what my family could get under SNAP and part A if it did not take part, in dollars` `the reduction under section 2031(c)(3), in dollars`

-- s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv). The State shall increase a participating family's assistance to make up for a State or local sales tax on food.
@export Under section 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv), must the State increase my family's assistance for the sales tax?
GIVEN `the State or my locality has a sales tax on food` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the State or your locality charge a sales tax on food?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv), must the State increase my family's assistance for the sales tax` IS
    `s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv) the State shall increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families for the sales tax` `the State or my locality has a sales tax on food`

-- s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv). A person ineligible for the Project, in a household that includes a participating family, gets the higher of $10 or 75 percent of the SNAP amount (worked out with the maximum excess shelter expense deduction), rounded down.
@export Under section 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv), what is my monthly allotment if I am ineligible for the Project but live with a participating family?
GIVEN `I am ineligible for the Project and live in a household that includes a participating family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ineligible for the Project while a member of a household that includes a family taking part in it?
      `s 2017 my monthly allotment under the SNAP standards with the maximum excess shelter expense deduction, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc What would your monthly allotment be under the usual SNAP standards, applying the maximum excess shelter expense deduction, in dollars? (Leave blank if it has not been worked out.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv), what is my monthly allotment if I am ineligible for the Project but live with a participating family` IS
    `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, in dollars` `I am ineligible for the Project and live in a household that includes a participating family` `s 2017 my monthly allotment under the SNAP standards with the maximum excess shelter expense deduction, in dollars`

-- s 2031(b)(6)(A). Where families are selected by application, the State shall promptly determine eligibility and issue assistance retroactive to the date of application, not later than 30 days after the application is filed.
@export Under section 2031(b)(6)(A), did the State determine my family's eligibility and issue assistance in time?
GIVEN `how my family was selected for the Project` IS A `s 2031 way of selecting a family` @desc How was your family selected? Choose one of: s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project; s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program; s 2031 in some other way.
      `the State has determined my family's eligibility and issued assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State determined your family's eligibility and issued assistance to it?
      `days from my family's filing of an application to the day the State did so, or to today if it has not` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days passed from the day your family filed its application to the day the State determined eligibility and issued assistance (or to today if it has not yet)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(6)(A), did the State determine my family's eligibility and issue assistance in time` IS
    `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency determined eligibility and issued assistance in time` `how my family was selected for the Project` `the State has determined my family's eligibility and issued assistance` `days from my family's filing of an application to the day the State did so, or to today if it has not`

-- s 2031(b)(6)(C). Where families are selected by application, expedited benefits shall be provided to a family entitled to expedited service under section 2020(e)(9).
@export Under section 2031(b)(6)(C), must expedited benefits be provided to my family?
GIVEN `how my family was selected for the Project` IS A `s 2031 way of selecting a family` @desc How was your family selected? Choose one of: s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project; s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program; s 2031 in some other way.
      `s 2020(e)(9) my household is entitled to expedited service` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is your household entitled to expedited service under section 2020(e)(9)? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(6)(C), must expedited benefits be provided to my family` IS
    `s 2031(b)(6)(C) expedited benefits shall be provided to the family` `how my family was selected for the Project` `s 2020(e)(9) my household is entitled to expedited service`

-- s 2031(b)(9). Assistance under the Project is reduced by the pro rata value of the SNAP benefits received for the same period.
@export Under section 2031(b)(9), how much assistance is left after the reduction for SNAP benefits I received?
GIVEN `the assistance my family gets under the Project for the period, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much assistance does your family get under the Project for the period, in dollars?
      `the pro rata value of the SNAP benefits I received for the same period, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the pro rata value of the SNAP benefits you received for the same period, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(9), how much assistance is left after the reduction for SNAP benefits I received` IS
    `s 2031(b)(9) the assistance after the reduction, in dollars` `the assistance my family gets under the Project for the period, in dollars` `the pro rata value of the SNAP benefits I received for the same period, in dollars`

-- s 2031(b)(10)(A). The State shall give each family or member whose participation ends, and each family whose participation is terminated, notice of the existence of SNAP and whom to contact.
@export Under section 2031(b)(10)(A), has the State given me the notice about SNAP that I am owed?
GIVEN `my participation in the Project ended or my family's participation was terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your participation in the Project ended, or your family's participation been terminated?
      `the State has told me that SNAP exists and whom to contact for more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State told you that SNAP exists and whom to contact for more information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(10)(A), has the State given me the notice about SNAP that I am owed` IS
    `s 2031(b)(10)(A) the State has given the notice the text requires` `my participation in the Project ended or my family's participation was terminated` `the State has told me that SNAP exists and whom to contact for more information`

-- s 2031(b)(10)(B)(i). When a family or member is determined ineligible for the Project because of income, resources or a change in household composition, the State shall ensure SNAP benefits are provided if the household is found eligible under the SNAP standards.
@export Under section 2031(b)(10)(B)(i), must the State ensure that I get SNAP benefits after I leave the Project?
GIVEN `why my participation ended` IS A `s 2031 why participation ended` @desc Why did your participation end? Choose one of: s 2031 the Project is terminated; s 2031 the family or member is determined ineligible for the Project because of income; s 2031 the family or member is determined ineligible for the Project because of resources; s 2031 the family or member is determined ineligible for the Project because of a change in household composition; s 2031 some other reason.
      `s 2014 my household is found eligible for SNAP under the SNAP standards` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is your household found eligible for SNAP under the usual SNAP standards? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(10)(B)(i), must the State ensure that I get SNAP benefits after I leave the Project` IS
    `s 2031(b)(10)(B)(i) the State shall ensure that benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program are provided` `why my participation ended` `s 2014 my household is found eligible for SNAP under the SNAP standards`

-- s 2031(b)(10)(C). When a family's participation is terminated the State shall screen it for SNAP, ask for the extra information within ten days, and determine eligibility within five days of receiving it.
@export Under section 2031(b)(10)(C), did the State determine my family's SNAP eligibility in time after I supplied the information?
GIVEN `I supplied the additional information the State asked for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you supply the additional information the State asked for?
      `days from my receiving the State's request to my supplying the information` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days passed from your receiving the State's request to your supplying the information?
      `the State has determined whether my family is eligible for SNAP` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State determined whether your family is eligible for SNAP?
      `days from the State's receiving the information to its determination, or to today if not yet` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days passed from the State's receiving the information to its determination (or to today if it has not yet determined)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(10)(C), did the State determine my family's SNAP eligibility in time` IS
    `s 2031(b)(10)(C) the State determined eligibility in time` `I supplied the additional information the State asked for` `days from my receiving the State's request to my supplying the information` `the State has determined whether my family is eligible for SNAP` `days from the State's receiving the information to its determination, or to today if not yet`

-- s 2031(b)(11). A family has a hearing where the Project action is one for which a hearing is available, on notice consistent with the Social Security Act regulations.
@export Under section 2031(b)(11), was my family given notice as the text requires?
GIVEN `a hearing is available for the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a hearing available for the action taken against your family?
      `my family was given notice of the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your family given notice of the action?
      `the notice is consistent with the Social Security Act notice regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice consistent with the notice requirements of the regulations implementing sections 402(a)(4) and 482(h) of the Social Security Act? (Leave blank if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(b)(11), was my family given notice as the text requires` IS
    `s 2031(b)(11) the family was given notice as the text requires` `a hearing is available for the action` `my family was given notice of the action` `the notice is consistent with the Social Security Act notice regulations`

-- s 2031(c)(1). The State may require a parent to take part in education, employment or training, unless the parent is ill, needed at home, caring for a young child, working enough hours, or pregnant late, and so on.
@export Under section 2031(c)(1), may the State require me, as a parent, to take part in education, employment or training?
GIVEN `my family has one parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is yours a one-parent family?
      `I am ill or incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ill or incapacitated?
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in years?
      `I am needed at home because of another family member's illness or incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you needed in the home because of the illness or incapacity of another family member?
      `the age of my youngest child in months, or a negative number if I have no child` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is your youngest child, in months? (Enter a negative number if you have no child.)
      `I personally provide care for my child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you personally provide care for your child?
      `the hours a week I am employed or in education or employment and training services` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week are you employed or taking part in education or employment and training services?
      `the number of hours I work a week can be verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the number of hours you work each week be verified?
      `the hours a week I work, if they can be verified` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week do you work, if they can be verified?
      `my earnings a week, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you earn in a week, in dollars?
      `the trimester of my pregnancy, or 0 if I am not pregnant` IS A NUMBER @desc In which trimester of pregnancy are you? (Enter 0 if you are not pregnant.)
      `the Federal minimum hourly wage rate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Federal minimum hourly wage rate, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(c)(1), may the State require me, as a parent, to take part in education, employment or training` IS
    `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` `me as a parent` `the Federal minimum hourly wage rate, in dollars`
    WHERE
        `me as a parent` MEANS `s 2031 parent` WITH
            `the family has one parent` IS `my family has one parent`
            `the parent is ill or incapacitated` IS `I am ill or incapacitated`
            `the parent's age in years` IS `my age in years`
            `the parent is needed in the home because of the illness or incapacity of another family member` IS `I am needed at home because of another family member's illness or incapacity`
            `the age of the parent's youngest child in months, or a negative number if the parent has no child` IS `the age of my youngest child in months, or a negative number if I have no child`
            `the parent personally provides care for the child` IS `I personally provide care for my child`
            `the hours a week the parent is employed or participates in education or employment and training services` IS `the hours a week I am employed or in education or employment and training services`
            `the number of hours the parent works a week can be verified` IS `the number of hours I work a week can be verified`
            `the hours a week the parent works, if they can be verified` IS `the hours a week I work, if they can be verified`
            `the parent's earnings a week` IS `my earnings a week, in dollars`
            `the trimester of pregnancy, or 0 if the parent is not pregnant` IS `the trimester of my pregnancy, or 0 if I am not pregnant`

-- s 2031(c)(3). If an individual required to take part in education, employment or training fails without good cause, the family's assistance may be reduced, by no more than the family's assistance with no income other than the Project's.
@export Under section 2031(c)(3), what is the most my family's assistance may be reduced by?
GIVEN `I am required to take part in education, employment or training under section 2031(c)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to take part in education, employment or training requirements under section 2031(c)(1)?
      `I failed to comply without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the requirement without good cause?
      `the assistance my family would be eligible for with no income other than the Project's, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much assistance would your family be eligible for if it had no income other than from the Project, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 2031(c)(3), what is the most my family's assistance may be reduced by` IS
    `s 2031(c)(3) the most the assistance to the family may be reduced by, in dollars` `I am required to take part in education, employment or training under section 2031(c)(1)` `I failed to comply without good cause` `the assistance my family would be eligible for with no income other than the Project's, in dollars`

-- s 2031(c)(3). The reduction in the family's assistance may be at most that amount.
@export Under section 2031(c)(3), may my family's assistance be reduced by this amount?
GIVEN `I am required to take part in education, employment or training under section 2031(c)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to take part in education, employment or training requirements under section 2031(c)(1)?
      `I failed to comply without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the requirement without good cause?
      `the assistance my family would be eligible for with no income other than the Project's, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much assistance would your family be eligible for if it had no income other than from the Project, in dollars?
      `the reduction, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much is your family's assistance to be reduced, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(c)(3), may my family's assistance be reduced by this amount` IS
    `s 2031(c)(3) the assistance to the family may be reduced by the amount` `I am required to take part in education, employment or training under section 2031(c)(1)` `I failed to comply without good cause` `the assistance my family would be eligible for with no income other than the Project's, in dollars` `the reduction, in dollars`

-- s 2031(j)(1). A family is a minor child or a group of minor children related as siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings or adopted siblings, together with their natural or adoptive parents or their caregiver; a pregnant woman in the third trimester with no children is also a family.
@export Under section 2031(j)(1), is my group a family for the Project?
GIVEN `we live together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the members of your group live together?
      `the number of minor children in the group` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minor children are in the group?
      `the minor children are siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings or adopted siblings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the minor children related to each other as siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings or adopted siblings?
      `a natural or adoptive parent of the children lives with us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a natural or adoptive parent of the children live with them?
      `the children's caregiver lives with us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the children's caregiver live with them?
      `I am a pregnant woman in the third trimester with no children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the group a pregnant woman in the third trimester of pregnancy with no children?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(j)(1), is my group a family for the Project` IS
    `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` `my group`
    WHERE
        `my group` MEANS `s 2031 group` WITH
            `they live together` IS `we live together`
            `the number of minor children` IS `the number of minor children in the group`
            `the minor children are related to each other as siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings, or adopted siblings` IS `the minor children are siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings or adopted siblings`
            `a natural or adoptive parent of the children lives with them` IS `a natural or adoptive parent of the children lives with us`
            `the children's caregiver lives with them` IS `the children's caregiver lives with us`
            `it is a pregnant woman in the third trimester of pregnancy with no children` IS `I am a pregnant woman in the third trimester with no children`

-- s 2031(j)(3). A caregiver is a listed relative who lives in the home with the minor child and provides care and support when no parent lives there, or any person who does, for determining eligibility for the Project.
@export Under section 2031(j)(3), am I a caregiver of the minor child?
GIVEN `my relationship to the minor child` IS A `s 2031 relationship to the minor child` @desc How are you related to the minor child? Choose one of: s 2031 natural or adoptive parent; s 2031 grandfather; s 2031 grandmother; s 2031 brother; s 2031 sister; s 2031 stepfather; s 2031 stepmother; s 2031 stepbrother; s 2031 stepsister; s 2031 uncle; s 2031 aunt; s 2031 first cousin; s 2031 nephew; s 2031 niece; s 2031 a person of a preceding generation denoted by the prefix great or great-great; s 2031 a spouse of any person named above, even after the marriage ends by death or divorce; s 2031 some other relationship.
      `I live in the home with the minor child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live in the home with the minor child?
      `I provide care and support to the minor child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide care and support to the minor child?
      `a natural or adoptive parent of the minor child lives in the same home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a natural or adoptive parent of the minor child live in the same home?
      `the purpose is determining eligibility for the Project` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you asking in order to determine eligibility for the Project?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2031(j)(3), am I a caregiver of the minor child` IS
    `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `my relationship to the minor child` `I live in the home with the minor child` `I provide care and support to the minor child` `a natural or adoptive parent of the minor child lives in the same home` `the purpose is determining eligibility for the Project`

§§ `Section 2035 -- simplified program: whether your household may take part in a State's simplified program`

-- s 2035(c). A household in which every member receives assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV may take part in a State's simplified program; a household in which only some do may take part if the Secretary approves.
@export Under section 2035(c), may my household take part in the State's simplified program?
GIVEN `the number of members of my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does your household have?
      `the number of members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act?
      `the Secretary has approved my household's participation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary approved your household's taking part? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2035(c), may my household take part in the State's simplified program` IS
    `s 2035(c) the household may participate in the Program` `the number of members of my household` `the number of members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` `the Secretary has approved my household's participation`

-- s 2035(c)(2). A household in which all members receive part A assistance is eligible to take part.
@export Under section 2035(c)(2), is my household eligible to take part in the State's simplified program?
GIVEN `the number of members of my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does your household have?
      `the number of members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2035(c)(2), is my household eligible to take part in the State's simplified program` IS
    `s 2035(c)(2) the household is eligible to participate in the Program` `the number of members of my household` `the number of members who receive assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV`

-- s 2035(c)(4). Benefits under the Program may be determined under the rules and procedures of the State's part A program, of SNAP, or of a combination.
@export Under section 2035(c)(4), may my benefits under the simplified program be worked out under these rules?
GIVEN `the rules my State uses to work out my benefits` IS A `s 2035 source of the benefit rules` @desc Whose rules does your State use to work out your benefits? Choose one of: s 2035 a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act; s 2035 the supplemental nutrition assistance program; s 2035 a combination of the State TANF-funded program and the supplemental nutrition assistance program; s 2035 some other source.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2035(c)(4), may my benefits under the simplified program be worked out under these rules` IS
    `s 2035(c)(4) benefits under the Program may be determined under rules from this source` `the rules my State uses to work out my benefits`

-- s 2035(f)(3)(B). A household's income may be determined under the rules of the State's part A program, SNAP, or a combination.
@export Under section 2035(f)(3)(B), may my household's income be worked out under these rules?
GIVEN `the rules my State uses to work out my income` IS A `s 2035 source of the benefit rules` @desc Whose rules does your State use to work out your household's income? Choose one of: s 2035 a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act; s 2035 the supplemental nutrition assistance program; s 2035 a combination of the State TANF-funded program and the supplemental nutrition assistance program; s 2035 some other source.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2035(f)(3)(B), may my household's income be worked out under these rules` IS
    `s 2035(f)(3)(B) the household's income may be determined under this source` `the rules my State uses to work out my income`

-- s 2035(f)(4). A household eligible only under the State program may not get benefits under this section unless the Secretary has determined that no household with income above 130 percent of the poverty guidelines is eligible for the State program.
@export Under section 2035(f)(4), may my household get benefits under the simplified program because it is eligible under the State program?
GIVEN `the Secretary has determined that no household with income above 130 percent of the poverty guidelines is eligible for the State program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary determined that no household with income above 130 percent of the poverty guidelines is eligible for the State program? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2035(f)(4), may my household get benefits under the simplified program because it is eligible under the State program` IS
    `s 2035(f)(4) the household may receive benefits under this section as a result of its eligibility under the State program` `the Secretary has determined that no household with income above 130 percent of the poverty guidelines is eligible for the State program`

§§ `Section 2036a -- nutrition education and obesity prevention grant program: whether you are an eligible individual`

-- s 2036a(a). An eligible individual is one eligible for SNAP, for certain child nutrition benefits (42 U.S.C. 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4), or 1773(e)(1)(A)), or whom the Secretary determines to live in a significant low-income community or to be another eligible low-income individual.
@export Under section 2036a(a), am I an eligible individual for nutrition education and obesity prevention?
GIVEN `s 2014 I am eligible for SNAP benefits` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for SNAP benefits? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
      `I am eligible for benefits under sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for benefits under sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42 (free or reduced price meals and similar)?
      `I am eligible for benefits under section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for benefits under section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42 (the special supplemental nutrition program for women, infants and children)?
      `the Secretary determines that I live in a community with a significant low-income population` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary determined that you live in a community with a significant low-income population? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
      `the Secretary determines that I am another low-income individual who is eligible` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary determined that you are another low-income individual who is eligible? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2036a(a), am I an eligible individual for nutrition education and obesity prevention` IS
    `s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` `s 2014 I am eligible for SNAP benefits` `I am eligible for benefits under sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42` `I am eligible for benefits under section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42` `the Secretary determines that I live in a community with a significant low-income population` `the Secretary determines that I am another low-income individual who is eligible`

-- s 2036a(b). State agencies may implement a nutrition education and obesity prevention program for eligible individuals that promotes healthy food choices and physical activity consistent with the Dietary Guidelines, consistent with the grant terms.
@export Under section 2036a(b), may the State agency offer me its nutrition education and obesity prevention program?
GIVEN `s 2014 I am eligible for SNAP benefits` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for SNAP benefits? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
      `I am eligible for benefits under sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for benefits under sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42 (free or reduced price meals and similar)?
      `I am eligible for benefits under section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible for benefits under section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42 (the special supplemental nutrition program for women, infants and children)?
      `the Secretary determines that I live in a community with a significant low-income population` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary determined that you live in a community with a significant low-income population? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
      `the Secretary determines that I am another low-income individual who is eligible` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary determined that you are another low-income individual who is eligible? (Leave blank if that has not been decided.)
      `the program promotes healthy food choices and physical activity consistent with the Dietary Guidelines for Americans` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the program promote healthy food choices and physical activity consistent with the most recent Dietary Guidelines for Americans?
      `the program is consistent with the terms and conditions of the grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the program consistent with the terms and conditions of the State's grant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2036a(b), may the State agency offer me its nutrition education and obesity prevention program` IS
    `s 2036a(b) the State agency may implement the program for the individual` (`s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` `s 2014 I am eligible for SNAP benefits` `I am eligible for benefits under sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42` `I am eligible for benefits under section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42` `the Secretary determines that I live in a community with a significant low-income population` `the Secretary determines that I am another low-income individual who is eligible`) `the program promotes healthy food choices and physical activity consistent with the Dietary Guidelines for Americans` `the program is consistent with the terms and conditions of the grant`

-- s 2036a(c)(4). The State agency shall, where practicable, notify applicants, participants and eligible individuals of the availability of nutrition education and obesity prevention services.
@export Under section 2036a(c)(4), must the State agency notify me of the availability of nutrition education and obesity prevention services?
GIVEN `I am an applicant, a participant or an eligible individual under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an applicant for, a participant in, or an eligible individual under the Food and Nutrition Act?
      `notifying me is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it practicable for the State agency to notify you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2036a(c)(4), must the State agency notify me of the availability of nutrition education and obesity prevention services` IS
    `s 2036a(c)(4) the State agency shall notify the person of the availability of the services` `I am an applicant, a participant or an eligible individual under this chapter` `notifying me is practicable`
